window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 154","paragraphs":["Kkobong (1)","Title: Introducing My New Worker","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an albino gorilla glaring viciously while wearing a suppressor around his neck)","This is Kkobong, my new worker who joined me through entirely legal means. Please treat him well from now on~","└ Heavenly Demon: He has the eyes of a beast ready to devour a man. Educating him will take some time.","└ SwordMaster: Considering he’s wearing what looks like a dog collar, I don’t think this is legal.","└ Wild Grylls: What do you mean? I never engage in illegal activities.","└ SwordMaster: That’s plainly a slave;; Isn’t slavery illegal?","└ Wild Grylls: He caused me losses first, so I merely enslaved him temporarily in accordance with the law.","└ SwordMaster: Slavery was abolished ages ago;; And who passed that judgment?","└ Wild Grylls: Me.","└ SwordMaster: Hahahahahaha!","└ He just shamelessly said, \"Me,\" lmao.","└ You should’ve called him a prisoner instead, lol.","└ What kind of legal system is that? Lmao.","└ Is that what they call the law of the wild? Lol.","└ Starlight Princess: If you want, I can give you a potion that will make him more obedient. Would you like it?","└ Wild Grylls: What kind of potion?","└ Starlight Princess: One that kills him unless he drinks an antidote at regular intervals.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s incredibly inhumane;;","└ Starlight Princess: Hehe.","└ You two are exactly the same;;","└ I’m curious. What would Grylls be charged with for this? Animal abuse or illegal slavery?","└ He’d just be arrested. Why are you bothering to distinguish between them?;;","└ Could anyone even arrest him in the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ We only need to watch. Why are you analyzing every little detail? Lol.","└ Something about seeing a gorilla restrained like that is strangely attractive.","└ ?","└ ??","└ Excuse me?","└ Pardon me, but could you please die?","└ Are you perhaps a beastfolk?","└ For the record, she’s a woman.","└ Oh. Then it’s fine.","└ It’s understandable if she’s a beastfolk.","└ Suspiciously: What do you mean, \"understandable\"? Even beastfolk don’t feel that way about animals. That bitch is the weird one, fuck!","└ It’s a talking gorilla. What’s the difference?","└ Yeah, lol. Explain the difference.","Everyone seemed to be welcoming my new worker, Kkobong.","Some people told me to whip him whenever he refused to listen, but I ignored them.","No matter how malicious I might be, I wasn’t that cruel.","Besides, Fast Sloth would intervene first the moment Kkobong tried to touch me.","’First, I need to treat his injuries...’","I looked at Kkobong, who remained frozen while glaring at me.","Not only was he encased in ice, but he was also bound with rope.","He had even been stabbed with a sword, so I needed to treat him.","\"Hey, Kkobong.\"","\"Kkobong, I’m talking to you. I already told you, didn’t I? Your name is Kkobong now.\"","I continued speaking in Korean because I saw no reason to explain it in the language of the Central Plains.","The language of the Central Plains might have been his native tongue(?), but I was Korean.","Moreover, he had tried to kill me and take away the shelter I had painstakingly built.","I had absolutely no intention of accommodating him, so I planned to communicate exclusively in Korean.","\"...Wi Baek.\"","\"What?\"","\"$#%$ Kkobong, #$#! Wi Baek!\"","What the hell was he saying?","Kkobong barked something at me.","Judging from his tone, he seemed to be demanding that I call him Wi Baek instead of Kkobong.","Smack!","\"Urgh!\"","\"What are you saying? Speak Korean. And from now on, your name is Kkobong.\"","Annoyed, I struck him on the head.","Since he had tried to kill me, I had no intention of showing him consideration.","If he disobeyed, I would hit him. If he listened, I planned to reward him.","Therefore, I had no choice but to keep making an effort(?) until he became obedient.","\"Hey. Look at me properly.\"","I crouched down until my eyes were level with Kkobong’s.","Kkobong faced me with a deep scowl.","\"See this key? It’s the key to the suppressor around your neck.\"","\"@&#$!\"","\"Why, you...\"","He needed to listen until someone had finished speaking.","When I raised my hand, Kkobong flinched.","He had already been defeated by me once and struck several more times while restrained.","I intended to teach him until it became instinctively ingrained in his mind that resisting me was pointless.","\"Anyway, you need this key to remove the thing around your neck. But I’m never going to give it to you.\"","\"You already know, don’t you? Surviving in this forest without those martial techniques you’re so proud of will be extremely difficult.\"","Kkobong was an albino gorilla, and albinos had extremely low survival rates in the wild.","Their white fur made them conspicuous, while their poor eyesight slowed their reactions.","He possessed enough martial strength to compensate for those weaknesses, but with the suppressor around his neck, he was effectively an ordinary gorilla.","\"And look over there.\"","I pointed toward a particular spot.","The workpieces Kkobong had destroyed during his rampage lay there in a miserable state.","From now on, I intended to work him relentlessly until the job was complete.","\"You’re going to help me with the woodworking from now on. Understand?\"","It would be best to explain it kindly at first.","He couldn’t understand Korean?","There was no need to worry.","If he couldn’t understand, I would discipline him until he did.","Since he wasn’t even a foreigner but an animal, it would probably take quite some time.","’But that isn’t my problem.’","I stared at Kkobong, who maintained his silence.","His future would be much more comfortable if he obeyed me, yet he didn’t seem to understand that.","It would have been best to break his spirit completely, but unfortunately, I didn’t have a suitable method.","’Torture is... something I don’t want to do. I’ll just have to make him accept reality.’","He must have understood it himself.","Unless he could remove the mana suppressor, surviving in the forest would be difficult.","That meant there was a high probability he would remain here until he acquired the key.","’I should untie him first.’","The ice encasing his entire body had gradually begun to melt.","I placed a campfire near Kkobong to accelerate the process.","His right arm thawed first.","The instant his right arm was free, Kkobong reached out.","His hand moved directly toward my arm.","Apparently, he was trying to grab me.","However—","Bzzzzzt!","\"Oooaaaargh!!!\"","All he earned was another punishment.","The instant Kkobong’s hand touched me, the suppressor activated.","He must have realized one more thing from that.","The moment he made physical contact with me, the electrical current would activate.","I snorted as I watched Kkobong sit there in a daze from the electrocution.","\"You should’ve given up when you had the chance.\"","\"Ugh...\"","Kkobong’s eyes repeatedly went in and out of focus, suggesting that he hadn’t heard me.","Apparently, the suppressor released a stronger electrical current in response to physical contact than it did when he used mana.","’It runs on the wearer’s mana, so I won’t have to worry about it running out of power.’","Kkobong was now destined to remain at this shelter.","While his body thawed, I toyed with the key.","There was a chance he might ambush me, so I had absolutely no intention of carrying it around.","One might ask what I had to worry about when physical contact would activate the suppressor, but—","’He survived in the Forest of Four Seasons, so he must be incredibly tenacious.’","The problem was that this concern was unlikely to remain merely hypothetical.","Even I struggled desperately to survive.","That albino gorilla must have gone through a similar ordeal.","He was also nearly as intelligent as a human, so I had to prepare for every possibility.","Then whom would I entrust the key to?","\"Fast Sloth, you hold on to this.\"","I planned to give it to my master and the strongest member of our shelter—Fast Sloth.","First, I made a cord from the wood fibers I had collected while working.","I threaded it through the hole in the key, tied it securely, and hung it around Fast Sloth’s neck.","Now there was no chance of the key ever being stolen.","What if someone tried to take it by force?","’Then they’ll receive a proper lesson.’","While Kkobong’s ice continued to melt, I went inside the cave.","Since I intended to put him to work immediately, I needed to treat his injuries.","Frostbite was beyond me, but I could treat his puncture wounds to some extent.","\"There. You can walk now, right?\"","\"...\"","I had completely thawed his body and treated every puncture wound.","Kkobong examined his rapidly healed hands and feet from every angle.","Judging solely by his expression, he seemed amazed by the elixir’s remarkable effectiveness.","\"Enough admiring yourself. It’s time to work.\"","\"...\"","\"Look at this bastard. If you don’t—\"","\"Kaishi.\"","When I slowly extended my hand, Kkobong hurriedly spoke.","Even someone as prideful as him seemed afraid of being electrocuted.","I was satisfied with his reaction, but only briefly. I still needed to explain the work he would be doing.","\"Your task is simple. You’re going to process these logs according to specific measurements.\"","\"...?\"","After hearing my explanation, Kkobong tilted his head as though he had no idea what I was saying.","He didn’t appear to be mocking me. He genuinely couldn’t understand, and the realization left me strangely disillusioned.","’Do I really have to teach him Korean?’","I didn’t want to learn the language of the Central Plains.","I saw no reason why I should have to.","After letting out a frustrated sigh, I decided to demonstrate instead of explaining.","\"Watch carefully. If you can’t copy me, you’re getting electrocuted again.\"","\"...\"","At least threats seemed to work well.","Kkobong unfolded his arms and began paying attention after hearing my warning.","He still looked dissatisfied, but that would probably disappear soon enough.","\"See this? This is called a saw.\"","\"...\"","\"And then... Ah, forget it. Just watch and copy me.\"","I finally understood what it meant to recite scripture to a cow.","Humiliation.","Utter humiliation.","That was how the albino gorilla felt after Grylls bestowed upon him the affectionate name \"Kkobong.\"","One might ask how a mere beast could feel humiliation, but animals possessed emotions as well.","Moreover, Kkobong was intelligent enough to learn human speech.","He could experience a greater variety of emotions than an ordinary beast, humiliation included.","’Someday, I will escape.’","Kkobong stared at Grylls.","His naturally poor eyesight prevented him from making out Grylls’s appearance, but one thing was certain.","Kkobong had been ostracized because he was born different from the rest of his kind.","There had once been a human who taught him language and martial arts without discriminating against him.","Remembering that human had initially made Kkobong curious about Grylls, but everything that had happened since their meeting had extinguished that curiosity.","Not all humans were the same.","Another human had threatened him before as well.","Consequently, the only emotions he now felt toward Grylls were humiliation and a desire for revenge.","He might have lowered his head for now, but he planned to escape someday.","’This device is infuriating.’","To accomplish that, he first had to remove the suppressor around his neck.","He hadn’t understood what Grylls said, but judging from the situation, he would need that key.","The key was currently hanging around the neck of a sloth.","Therefore, removing the device meant he first had to defeat the sloth.","\"I’m going up to the river for a moment. Keep a close eye on Kkobong.\"","His opportunity arrived sooner than expected.","Wi Baek—no, Kkobong—looked at the sloth.","It was small and appeared sluggish.","Its sharply honed claws concerned him, but he would be fine as long as he remained vigilant.","’Every one of its movements is slow and lethargic.’","He had observed that during his fight with Grylls.","At the same time, it made him wonder.","Why had Grylls fought with the sloth riding on his back?","Was it so the creature could use its sharp claws to climb trees easily?","He still had questions, but ultimately, a sloth was only a sloth.","It was a beast incapable of the same higher-order reasoning as a human.","’I’ll kill it.’","Kkobong therefore decided to kill the dim-witted-looking sloth.","His actions were as swift as his decision.","He slowly approached the sloth.","Flinch!","\"...?\"","Something was strange.","Kkobong’s body twitched.","The closer he came to the sloth, the stronger his unease grew.","What was the source of this feeling?","He looked around.","For a moment, he wondered if Grylls was secretly watching him, but that wasn’t the case.","’...Something is wrong.’","As a beast ruled more by instinct than reason, Kkobong instinctively sensed danger.","He didn’t know what was unusual about the sloth, but he knew it was extremely dangerous.","Would he retreat, then?","Absolutely not.","Instead, he concluded that he needed to finish it as quickly as possible.","Kkobong released a terrifying aura as he stared at the sloth.","\"...\"","The sloth merely looked back with its characteristically relaxed expression.","Its entire demeanor proclaimed, I’m completely harmless~","Who would ever consider this sloth dangerous?","Most would instead wonder how something so incredibly slow had managed to survive.","’I almost feel sorry for it.’","Looking at the sloth stirred a pang of guilt within Kkobong.","But this was the Forest of Four Seasons—a place where one had to do anything necessary to survive.","His enormous, hammer-like fist slowly rose above the sloth’s head.","The sloth leisurely raised its head and looked up at his arm.","Even that movement was painfully slow, exactly as one would expect from a sloth.","It was slow enough to frustrate anyone—or any animal—watching.","\"Blame your master.\"","Muttering those words, Kkobong brought down his fist.","Slash!","A snow-white head separated from its body and flew through the air."]},{"title":"Chapter 155","paragraphs":["Kkobong (2)","His vision spun round and round. Even time seemed to crawl by at a sluggish pace.","The albino gorilla once known as Wi Baek—Kkobong—found himself wondering amid the dizzying whirl of his vision.","What... is this?","Whether beast or human, it was difficult to comprehend a death that occurred in an instant.","But Kkobong could see it clearly.","In a world that had turned 180 degrees, the sloth was staring at him.","Blood stained the sloth’s razor-sharp claws.","Only belatedly did Kkobong realize that the sloth had cleanly severed his neck.","\"Uwoah?!\"","Kkobong’s eyes flew wide open in horror. Cold sweat poured down his body, and his heart pounded violently.","Having escaped the vision, the first thing he did was feel around his neck.","Until moments ago, his head had been flying through the air. Yet now, his neck was perfectly intact.","W-What in the world was that just now...?","Even though it had been an illusion, he could not readily believe it. The reaction would have been the same even if he were human rather than a beast.","After repeatedly feeling his neck, Kkobong looked ahead with trembling eyes.","The sloth stood before him, wearing its usual relaxed expression.","It even tilted its head as though wondering whether something had happened.","D-Don’t tell me...","The instincts unique to wild beasts told him that it had not merely been an illusion.","If the sloth had brought its arm all the way down, that illusion would have become reality.","As previously mentioned, beasts were incapable of higher-order thought.","But when it came to survival—in other words, matters related to death—they understood more quickly than any other creature.","Scratch, scratch.","Whether Kkobong was horrified or not, the sloth, Fast Sloth, merely scratched its head.","It gave off the impression that it was telling him to hurry up and speak if he had something to say.","But what could a beast who had just experienced something akin to death possibly say?","Kkobong slowly backed away, putting distance between himself and Fast Sloth.","Now... Now I finally understand.","He understood why Grylls had entrusted the key to this sloth.","It had not been some kind of trap.","The reason was incredibly simple: Fast Sloth was the strongest creature here.","At the very least, Grylls was not strong enough to show him an illusion of his own death.","That led Kkobong to another conclusion.","This sloth is stronger than the human. That means...!","That human was ultimately this sloth’s subordinate—in other words, its slave!","It was a train of thought that perfectly demonstrated the limitations of a beast. Ironically, however, it also struck directly at the true nature of their relationship.","In exchange for Fast Sloth’s protection, Grylls offered it all manner of food as tribute.","In other words, even if Kkobong defeated Grylls, he could never regain his freedom as long as the sloth remained.","The leader.","A leader was always accompanied by an intelligent subordinate.","That human probably fulfilled such a role.","He was also responsible for all the various forms of arduous labor around here.","Escape... is impossible.","Kkobong was disheartened. He could instinctively tell.","Even if he died and came back to life, he would not be able to inflict so much as a scratch on that sloth.","How could he dare attack an opponent capable of showing him an illusion of death?","He valued his life, so he could confidently declare that doing so would be an act of sheer madness.","But...","It was not entirely a bad thing. Kkobong had lived what people would call the life of a wild man.","Even if he searched every corner of the Forest of Four Seasons, animals possessing the same level of power as that sloth would be rare.","If he had to name one, it would be his brother, the leader of the gorilla troop.","That meant his safety would be guaranteed if he could only earn the sloth’s favor.","Perhaps this being is the one who...","...could bring down that treacherous hypocrite.","Perhaps it was because he had just seen a vision of his head flying off, but his thoughts were moving unusually quickly.","Kkobong silently faced Fast Sloth for a moment before slowly bowing his head.","\"Chiochyo chawo.\"","It roughly meant that he was asking Fast Sloth to accept him.","Unlike how he acted toward Grylls, Kkobong was seeking the approval of someone he recognized as unquestionably powerful.","Fast Sloth stared blankly at him for a moment before tilting its head.","Its reaction indicated that it had no idea what Kkobong was saying. Kkobong, however, interpreted it differently.","It seems he still doesn’t trust me.","That was only natural. Kkobong had suddenly invaded its territory.","According to the laws of the wild, he would have had no right to complain even if his head had already been sent flying.","Despite that, the sloth before him had spared his life. What tremendous mercy!","First, I must earn his recognition.","Kkobong made up his mind. He would prove his usefulness and become Fast Sloth’s subordinate.","Then he would get rid of that chattering human and earn the sloth’s trust.","Until then, whether I like it or not, I’ll have to obey that human.","He was displeased, but he could endure it. Patience was bitter, but its fruit was sweet.","Those were the words of the human who had once taught him.","Now that he had decided upon his future plans, Kkobong behaved respectfully before Fast Sloth.","But respect alone was not enough. In the wild, one had to demonstrate one’s intentions through actions.","Was this how that human did it?","Though no one had ordered him to, Kkobong began working on the lumber.","He was clumsy, but he used the saw in the manner Grylls had taught him.","Although he could no longer use mana, he still possessed the immense physical strength unique to gorillas.","\"Huh? What’s this? You started working on your own?\"","As if his timing could not have been better, Grylls returned just then.","Several fish flopped around inside the fish trap he had brought back.","Kkobong glanced briefly at Grylls before silently returning to his work(?).","\"Hmm... Well, I guess it all worked out. That’s enough for now. Come and eat first.\"","Kkobong pretended not to hear him. He could not understand what Grylls was saying anyway.","But that lasted only until he saw Fast Sloth slowly beginning to move. The moment he did, Kkobong stopped working.","When even the leader was helping prepare the meal, he could not possibly continue working by himself.","He stuck closely to the slowly moving Fast Sloth and waited quietly beside it.","Meanwhile, Grylls began cooking as he always did.","\"All right, let’s eat. You have one too.\"","Before long, the grilled fish was finished, looking delicious.","Kkobong cautiously watched the others before quietly reaching out.","It was hot because it had only just come off the fire, but not so hot that he could not eat it.","\"How is it? Good, right?\"","\".....\"","Kkobong nodded in response. He hated to admit it, but it truly was delicious.","What a versatile fellow.","He was truly an exceptional slave. Was that why Fast Sloth trusted him?","Kkobong finished his fish while resolving to replace Grylls as quickly as possible.","I’ll have to work even harder.","A slave mentality was gradually taking root within Kkobong.","\"Kkyuu?\"","\".....\"","\"Kkyuuu~\"","At that moment, Wonmo rubbed his face against Kkobong’s leg.","It was an unbearably adorable greeting, as though welcoming him into the family.","Kkobong stared at Wonmo’s lovable behavior before nodding.","He truly is a merciful being. He even took in a youngling.","\".....\"","His subtle misunderstandings were steadily multiplying.","***","Did Kkobong eat something strange while I was at the river?","He had been defiant before, but in that short span of time, he had suddenly become docile.","It was difficult to determine the exact reason, but I could make a reasonable guess.","Did Fast Sloth give him a thorough lesson?","There was no other explanation for how his entire personality could have been remodeled like that.","Fast Sloth must have taught him a harsh lesson and forced him to give up.","From my perspective, this was the best possible outcome.","Scritch! Scritch! Scritch!","\"Yeah, you’re doing great. Just keep doing it like that.\"","\".....\"","I had acquired an excellent worker.","As long as I demonstrated something first, Kkobong would take care of the rest by himself.","He occasionally did things strangely, but I could overlook that much since he was an animal.","Besides, I planned to handle all the delicate work, such as planing the wood, myself.","He was a primate, after all, and delicacy was not exactly his strong suit.","Even so, the addition of another worker doubled our efficiency.","Whoa. We’ve already finished this much?","Before I knew it, nearly all the logs needed to erect the bridge had been prepared.","Most of the logs damaged during Kkobong’s rampage had also been restored.","It had been possible because Kkobong devoted himself solely to sawing while I focused entirely on planing.","\"Kkobong, that’s enough. Take a break. The sun’s about to come up.\"","Kkobong was certainly steadfast—almost excessively so.","Perhaps the spirit of a slave had already taken root in him, or perhaps he simply could not understand me, but he kept working.","As I stared at him, a question suddenly came to mind.","Who taught him how to speak?","Considering that he was the brother of the leader of the gorilla troop, perhaps they had learned from the same human.","Fast Sloth also seemed not to know Kkobong.","It was likely that Kkobong had left the troop when he was young.","Then, as time passed, he had even harmed our esteemed senior—Rice Craone.","There were far too many things I wanted to ask him. I organized my questions in my head.","First, I should ask who taught him to speak.","That was what I was most curious about.","Considering that this person had even taught martial arts to gorillas, they must have possessed profound knowledge.","Furthermore, I might be able to determine why they had entered this forest and learn something about their circumstances.","I should ask the Heavenly Demon.","Ordinarily it might not matter, but for something important, it would be better to use the language of the Central Plains.","We needed to communicate smoothly if I wanted to learn all the details.","While Kkobong finished his work, I asked the Heavenly Demon to translate my questions into the language of the Central Plains.","[Heavenly Demon: (Photo of a drawing with the question written on it) Will this suffice?]","[Wild Grylls: Yes. Thank you for always helping me.]","[Heavenly Demon: It is nothing. This Lady is also curious to hear what answer he will give.]","With the Heavenly Demon’s help, I was able to prepare a separate questionnaire.","Just then, Kkobong finished all his work and approached me.","Despite having performed such strenuous labor, he looked perfectly fine and had not shed a single drop of sweat.","\"Kkobong, take a look at this.\"","When I showed him the questionnaire, he gave me a puzzled look.","It asked who had taught him language and martial arts.","He narrowed his eyes and leaned his head forward.","His eyesight was so poor that he had no choice but to do that.","\"Ho au...\"","Kkobong seemed about to say something after reading the question, but abruptly stopped.","He had probably been about to ask why he should tell me.","He even glanced nervously at Fast Sloth.","It was now certain that he had challenged Fast Sloth while I was away and received a brutal lesson in return.","After hesitating briefly, Kkobong finally opened his mouth.","\"Wi Hochang.\"","\"Wi Hochang?\"","When I repeated the name, Kkobong nodded.","Of course, I had no idea who this person was. The Heavenly Demon probably knew.","It is Wi Hochang, right? Names are usually transliterated according to their pronunciation.","If that did not work, I could always ask the Heavenly Demon.","I had even recorded a video in anticipation of something like this, so there would be no problem.","Before asking the Gallery, I asked the Heavenly Demon who Wi Hochang was.","[Heavenly Demon: Wi Hochang? If he is the same Wi Hochang this Lady knows, then he is quite an astonishing figure.]","[Wild Grylls: Who is he?]","[Heavenly Demon: He was the cause of the Pureblood War and was once known by the epithet Blood-Handed Tyrant.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh.]","A tyrant, huh? That was quite a cool epithet.","[Heavenly Demon: At the same time, he was also infamous as the \"Blood Demon.\"]","[Wild Grylls: Was he very famous?]","[Heavenly Demon: It could be said that he possessed the greatest renown before this Lady entered the martial world. If you are curious, ask the Gallery.]","[Wild Grylls: Understood.]","The Blood Demon. As far as I knew, it was an epithet that frequently appeared in martial arts stories alongside the Heavenly Demon.","I might not have known much about martial arts fiction, but I was familiar with the general meaning of such titles.","Usually, isn’t the Blood Demon even worse than the Heavenly Demon?","With that thought in mind, I made a post on the Gallery.","—Why the fuck are you asking about that bastard?","└Wi Hochang is alive!!!","└Wi!","└Ho!","—Chang!","└Ah, fuck. The Blood Cult fanatics have already caught the scent and swarmed in here;;","└Serious advice: Delete this quickly if you don’t want the comments to get weird;;","└Wild Grylls: What’s wrong with everyone?;;","Responses that completely defied my expectations began pouring in.","R EAD MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 156","paragraphs":["Kkobong (3)","There was an internet term called a \"meme.\"","It was similar to a catchphrase, except it was not limited to particular words. A meme could be a picture, a video, or even a real person.","It was somewhat like an emoticon, but much funnier to those who understood the context behind it.","Since the Gallery was essentially a version of the internet, it naturally had its own memes as well.","There were pictures used for all kinds of jokes, along with videos.","Even the occasional \"memetic contamination\" one suffered while browsing the Gallery could be considered a type of meme.","Title: Who’s Wi Hochang?","Wild Grylls","(Video of Kkobong answering, \"Wi Hochang.\")","I asked Kkobong who taught him how to speak and use martial arts. That was his answer.","The Heavenly Demon said he was the Blood Demon. Can anyone tell me more about him?","└SwordMaster: To think you would utter that name... They will soon come.","└Wild Grylls: Who will?","—Why the fuck are you asking about that bastard?","—Wi Hochang is alive!!!","└Wi!","└Ho!","—Chang!","└Ah, fuck. The Blood Cult fanatics have already caught the scent and swarmed in here;;","└Serious advice: Delete this quickly if you don’t want the comments to get weird;;","└Wild Grylls: What’s wrong with everyone?;;","—Wi!","—Ho!","└Chang!","└Worship Wi Hochang!!","└The Blood Cult has not yet fallen!","└WRYYYYYYY!!!","There was one particularly obnoxious meme among them, and it concerned the very person I had just asked about: Wi Hochang.","The moment I asked who Wi Hochang was, bizarre comments began sprouting up one after another.","They appeared at such an overwhelming rate that it was difficult to get an actual answer to my question.","What the hell is going on?","Just who was this Wi Hochang to provoke such an explosive(?) reaction?","I laboriously scrolled through the comment section, which had been overrun by spam. I was determined to get an answer somehow.","Fortunately, the comments had not been completely consumed by it. A few sensible responses were mixed in.","└Smart Main: Wi Hochang was the main culprit behind the Orthodox–Blood War. You know what that was, right?","└Wild Grylls: No. I don’t know anything about it.","└Smart Main: Just think of it as a civil war that broke out across the country. You know about the orthodox factions, unorthodox factions, the Demonic Cult, and the Blood Cult, right?","└Wild Grylls: I know the basics, but not the details. Could you tell me about the Blood Cult?","└Wi!","└Smart Main: They were completely out of their minds. All they cared about was killing people. The bastard known as the Blood Demon was the worst of them all.","└Ho!","└Wild Grylls: How bad was he?","—Chang!","└Smart Main: He went around bursting people’s heads whenever they annoyed him in the slightest. But he was so powerful that even most renowned masters were no match for him.","—Wi!","└Wild Grylls: Was that why the Orthodox–Blood War broke out?","└Ho!","—Smart Main: Yes, but the Blood Demon was so absurdly powerful that the orthodox and unorthodox factions had to join forces against him.","└Chang!","—Wild Grylls: Sounds like he probably didn’t have any friends.","└You insolent wretch! How dare you question Lord Wi Hochang!","└Divine punishment shall befall you!","└Wild Grylls: Fuck, the Forest of Four Seasons is already more than enough divine punishment, so shut up for a second.","└Hmm. He has a point.","└He is already suffering divine punishment, so there is no need for us to intervene.","└Ugh, I can smell the martial arts boomers from here;;","—Can’t someone do something about these guys? Lol.","└The head admin says they crawl back in like insects no matter how many times he bans them. Lol.","Although bizarre battle cries(?) kept interrupting the discussion, I somehow managed to hear the story.","Wi Hochang had earned the epithet \"Blood Demon\" because of the massacres he committed.","For reasons no one knew, he harbored a desire for revenge against a particular ethnic group and carried out an enormous massacre against them.","It was only natural that people eventually began following him. Apparently, they were simply drawn to his overwhelming power.","└Smart Main: But as I said earlier, he didn’t show any mercy even to his own followers if they displeased him. Their heads probably went pop!","After hearing the entire story, I understood why Wi Hochang had become a meme in the Gallery.","It was because the Blood Demon’s fate had never been confirmed after the Orthodox–Blood War.","Some people were convinced that the Blood Demon had survived, and those people had gradually infiltrated the Gallery.","The Blood Cult already had a terrible reputation, but these bizarre memes had made it even worse.","Then again, it was an organization full of people who enjoyed killing others. Who would like them in the first place?","—Because of the Orthodox–Blood War, all the masters from the orthodox and unorthodox factions died, so the overall standard of martial arts declined. There’s a reason the Heavenly Demon managed to beat the shit out of everyone.","└Wasn’t the army still intact? I heard even the emperor was beheaded.","└There was originally a group allied with the imperial court, but they were devastated too. That’s why.","—That doesn’t change the fact that the Heavenly Demon is a monster;;","—Wasn’t she better known by the epithet \"Yaksha Bloodflower\" back then rather than the Heavenly Demon?","└Yeah. That was why there were even rumors that she was the Blood Demon’s secret child.","└Come to think of it, weren’t that albino gorilla’s palms red?","└Wi Hochang was called the Blood-Handed Tyrant because his palms were red too.","└Did Wi Hochang really flee into the Forest of Four Seasons?","└If he escaped there, what is he doing now? Is he dead?","Just as before, Kkobong narrowed his eyes as he looked at the written question.","It asked where that person was now.","Kkobong gave his answer, and I asked the Heavenly Demon to translate it for me.","If the Immortal King resided in the west, then Wi Hochang resided in the east.","However, while the Immortal King had sent his brother into the Forest of Four Seasons, it appeared that Wi Hochang had come here himself.","Of course, I did not know whether any of that was true. It was merely Kkobong’s answer, after all.","I needed to investigate further. As it happened, there was a related question on the sheet.","\"Kkobong, answer this one too.\"","[Heavenly Demon: He says he left the troop when he was young, so he does not know much about it.]","[Wild Grylls: I see.]","So there was a reason Fast Sloth had not recognized him.","Kkobong possessed more distinctive features than anyone else, so there was no way Fast Sloth would have forgotten him otherwise.","\"@$@%&%@#!\"","Was it because he was talking about someone he knew? Or because the subject stirred old memories?","Even though I had not asked anything else, Kkobong began telling me all sorts of stories.","Naturally, he was speaking in the language of the Central Plains, so I could not understand a single word. Once again, I asked the Heavenly Demon to translate.","[Heavenly Demon: He says Wi Hochang was the only one who cared for him when the rest of the troop discriminated against him. Apparently, Wi Hochang continued teaching him until the day he left the troop.]","[Wild Grylls: Wasn’t the Blood Demon a bad person?]","[Heavenly Demon: He was, but perhaps he was generous toward beasts. The world is filled with people worse than animals, after all.]","That was a rather incisive observation. The reality was that the world was indeed full of people worse than beasts.","In fact, many people committed even more terrible acts precisely because they were capable of higher thought.","After briefly reflecting on Kkobong’s story, I thought about the Blood Demon.","Either way, wasn’t he a criminal?","It may have been an era in which the boundaries of self-defense were broad, but the Blood Demon had gone far beyond that.","He might have become a meme now, but he was someone who had killed people as casually as snacking on peanuts.","Fortunately, there was a very high chance that he was no longer alive.","Had he still been alive, the gorilla leader would have immediately reported it, and I would naturally have met him.","They said the Orthodox–Blood War broke out roughly fifty years ago.","The Blood Demon, Wi Hochang, had been around fifty years old when he was last seen.","That would make him well over a hundred by now, so it would hardly be strange if he had died of old age.","Since he was said to have been monstrously powerful, surviving in the Forest of Four Seasons would not have been particularly difficult for him.","No, wait. Doesn’t that mean even someone like him couldn’t escape the Forest of Four Seasons?","I did not know whether he had been unable to escape or had simply chosen not to, but the former seemed more likely.","According to the posts circulating around the Gallery, the Blood Demon had been extremely prideful.","Yet someone like that had mingled with mere gorillas and taught them language, writing, and even martial arts? Something did not add up.","Of course, I would have to search for traces of him to confirm the truth, but there was a good chance the gorilla leader possessed those as well.","The clothes that guy was wearing back then must have belonged to the Blood Demon.","Some things were finally beginning to make sense, but plenty of others remained incomprehensible.","Had entering the Forest of Four Seasons caused a change of heart in him? Or had he realized that escape was impossible and simply given up?","The truth remained shrouded in mystery, but I could investigate that gradually.","What mattered now was gathering information about the Blood Demon.","└Wild Grylls: What realm was the Blood Demon in?","└I heard he was at the Profound Realm. I think that’s roughly Grand Master level.","└If it’s the Profound Realm, just call it the Profound Realm. Why are you calling it Grand Master?;;","└What’s the difference between a Grand Master and a Grand Swordmaster?","└They’re basically the same. I just called it Grand Master for convenience.","└How strong is that?","└Just think of it as a realm where someone can overturn heaven and earth.","└Heavenly Demon: This Lady has also reached the Profound Realm. Demonic practitioners call it the Realm of Transcending the Demonic.","└SwordMaster: Yes, yes, of course you have. I could reach it too, but I just can’t be bothered.","The question I wanted to ask was this: Why had Kkobong attacked our esteemed senior, Rice Craone?","According to Rice Craone’s journal, he had died from the aftereffects of Kkobong’s attack.","I wanted to know whether Kkobong had learned that vicious temperament from the Blood Demon or whether there had been some other reason.","If he had killed him merely out of boredom... Honestly, I would probably execute him on the spot.","Unless there had been a legitimate reason, I could not overlook murder.","Kkobong frowned after reading the question. He even snorted.","His reaction suggested that he found the accusation utterly absurd, making me even more curious about his answer.","Kkobong eventually responded, and I once again asked the Heavenly Demon to translate.","Apparently, Wi Hochang had been more than monstrously powerful—he had been absurdly fucking powerful. Yet even someone like him had failed to escape the Forest of Four Seasons.","I did not know whether the injuries he sustained during the Orthodox–Blood War had been the problem or whether there had been another reason.","I decided to gather information about the Blood Demon, Wi Hochang, slowly and moved on to another question.","This might be the most important one.","[Heavenly Demon: He says the man stole his food in the past.]","[Wild Grylls: ...]","Thanks to that, I finally learned the circumstances behind the attack. Admittedly, having one’s food stolen would be difficult to tolerate.","Moreover, Kkobong’s poor eyesight would have made pursuit difficult.","Can glasses even be prescribed for an albino?","The thought suddenly occurred to me. Was there no way to improve Kkobong’s eyesight?","One might think better eyesight would be disadvantageous to me, but it was the opposite.","Glasses were essential if we wanted to prevent accidents—in other words, workplace injuries(?)—while he was working.","It would be even better if they helped me earn his goodwill.","Whether we liked it or not, we would be eating from the same pot from now on, so I might as well make his life a little more comfortable.","Title: Does anyone have glasses for low vision?","Wild Grylls","(Video of Kkobong squinting every time he tries to read)","He’s an albino, so his eyesight is really poor. I want to get him a pair of glasses. Does anyone have something suitable?","If you do, I’ll give you a gift in return, provided it’s something I can obtain.","└Heavenly Demon: One of this Lady’s close aides occasionally wears glasses. If you wish, I shall give you those.","└Wild Grylls: You shouldn’t do something that awful;;","└SwordMaster: Mana users don’t ordinarily suffer from deteriorating eyesight. How fascinating. Does he not know how to strengthen his vision?","└Wild Grylls: He was born with poor eyesight.","└SwordMaster: Ah. Then it probably won’t work. That would be equivalent to restoring sight to the blind.","└Wild Grylls: You don’t happen to have any spare glasses, do you?","└SwordMaster: My visual acuity is well over 9.0;;","└What the hell is 9.0...?","└Wild Grylls: Wow. You really do have eyes like a hawk. Can you even see ants crawling along the ground?","—SwordMaster: Why would I look at those? Lol.","└PraiseTheSun: I have a suitable pair. Want them?","└Wild Grylls: I’d appreciate that if you do. Is your eyesight poor?","—PraiseTheSun: No, they’re just a fashion accessory. But they also work for people with poor eyesight, so there shouldn’t be a problem.","└Wild Grylls: Thank you. Is there anything you need?","—PraiseTheSun: No. They’re not worth much money anyway.","└Glasses are surprisingly expensive, though, aren’t they?","└The frames might not be, but the lenses are fucking expensive. A craftsman has to grind them, after all.","—Sounds like this guy is genuinely rich.","└Passing Dwarf: Forget the glasses—put some clothes on him. He’s indecent to look at.","└Wild Grylls: Why would I put clothes on a gorilla?;;","—Princess Cheonggu: Would you like a Chae-Yu uniform, by any chance?","└This bastard is trying to pull another scheme. Lol.","└First Wonmo, then Fast Sloth, and now even Kkobong. Lmao.","—But considering his fur color, he probably should wear clothes.","└Yeah. White fur stands out far too much.","Since this was a world without the concept of plastic, these were probably ordinary glasses here.","\"Kkobong, try these on.\"","Along with the glasses, I had received advice to put some clothes on him.","His white fur certainly placed him at a considerable disadvantage when it came to survival.","He possessed enough strength to compensate for it, but that strength was currently sealed.","For now, it would be best to give him the glasses and think about the clothes later.","They look exactly like an old-fashioned pair of glasses.","The glasses I received from PraiseTheSun looked thoroughly old-fashioned.","They had round rims and a bridge shaped like an upside-down V.","\"...\"","When I handed him the glasses, Kkobong looked deeply suspicious.","He was probably wary because he was already wearing the restraint.","But this item was purely for his benefit.","I held them out insistently, urging him to take them, and Kkobong reluctantly accepted.","\"Uwoah?\"","Kkobong put on the glasses with a suspicious expression.","However, his suspicion soon turned to surprise.","\"Uwoah? Uwoooah!\"","And before long, that surprise transformed into amazement.","\"Ooooooh!!!\"","He reacted as though he had just witnessed an entirely new world.","Afterward, Kkobong repeatedly took the glasses off and put them back on again.","His eyes sparkled brightly, and his formerly fierce expression softened considerably.","Even his lips formed a little circle. It was the reaction of an entirely ordinary primate.","\"Ooooooh.\"","Still wearing the glasses, Kkobong began to walk away.","He headed deep into the forest.","I watched his retreating back with a satisfied expression.","\"Wait a minute.\"","Where the hell was he going?","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 157","paragraphs":["IRL Fight (1)","The pursuit of the runaway Kkobong began, but it ended before long.","It was not as though he had deliberately planned an escape. He had simply become overexcited and wandered all over the place.","Having always seen the world as a blur, it was understandable that he would be astonished when everything suddenly came into focus.","He had lived with congenital low vision his entire life, only to finally see the world clearly with his own two eyes.","If it had happened to me, I would have considered it more than just a whole new world. It would have been nothing short of a miracle.","\"What a wonderful job you’ve done. How long has it been since I gave you those glasses, and you’ve already broken them?\"","\"...\"","Ultimately, the absurd reason Kkobong was caught was that his glasses broke.","Even without the ability to use mana, a gorilla was still a gorilla. His physical strength far surpassed that of a human.","Glasses, meanwhile, could easily break under the slightest pressure.","Considering how excited he had been, it was only natural that they had been damaged.","Fortunately, only the frame broke.","I looked back and forth between the glasses, which had snapped cleanly in half, and the dejected Kkobong.","There was something strangely amusing about seeing such an expression on a creature who usually did nothing but scowl fiercely.","Regaining his eyesight must have made him incredibly happy, even if it had not lasted long.","\"I’ll try to fix them, so just wait here.\"","\"...\"","Kkobong looked at me.","His expression was filled with desperate hope, as though asking whether I could truly repair them.","I chuckled at his expression before immediately accessing the Gallery.","[Wild Grylls: Sir, about those glasses you gave me earlier.]","[PraiseTheSun: What about them? Is the prescription wrong?]","[Wild Grylls: No, Kkobong broke them. I think he got too excited.]","[PraiseTheSun: How badly are they broken? Do I need to make an entirely new pair?]","[Wild Grylls: No, they just snapped through the middle.]","[PraiseTheSun: That’ll be a quick fix, then. Send them over.]","Not long after I returned the glasses, PraiseTheSun sent them back fully repaired.","He even joked that he would charge me for repairs next time.","If Kkobong broke them again, I would have to pay a fair price to have them repaired.","\"Here. If you break them again, I’m putting a lock on them.\"","\"Siye, siye.\"","That probably meant something along the lines of thank you . Kkobong immediately put on the glasses.","Perhaps it was because the lenses had such a powerful prescription, but his features looked much gentler than before.","Without the glasses, he looked like a foul-tempered gorilla. With them on, he looked like the complete opposite.","His eyes even appeared smaller, accentuating the characteristic vacant look of a primate.","It’s surprising how perfectly they fit him.","Gorillas effectively had almost no nose bridge.","I had worried that the glasses would keep sliding down, but my concerns proved unfounded.","His head was so unusually large that wearing them was almost like wearing goggles.","They barely moved at all, even during vigorous activity.","He only broke them earlier because he kept taking them off and putting them back on.","Now that Kkobong’s eyesight problem had been resolved, I checked the questionnaire one last time.","There was something else I wanted to ask after the question about Rice Craone.","It might be a highly sensitive question for him.","\"Kkobong, can you take a look at this?\"","\"Uuu.\"","Perhaps it was because the glasses had corrected his vision and I had even gotten them repaired for him.","Unlike before, Kkobong read the question without squinting.","\"...\"","I take that back. His face crumpled the moment he read it.","His expression was filled with displeasure. To be fair, I had expected that reaction because it was a sensitive question.","I’d probably be offended too.","The question concerned the gorilla leader, whom I suspected was his brother.","Had they learned martial arts together from Wi Hochang? And why had Kkobong left the troop?","The gorilla leader seemed relatively kindhearted for a beast, but I still wanted to hear the details of what had happened.","\"...#%@1%\"","Kkobong considered it for a while before speaking.","Perhaps he was willing to tell me this much because I had given him the glasses.","I recorded everything he said and sent the video to the Heavenly Demon.","I would have liked to upload it to the Gallery, but I decided against it because it would probably cause another uproar.","[Heavenly Demon: It means casting off one’s mortal body and becoming an immortal. Yet this is strange. The Blood Demon’s martial arts were far removed from Taoism, and he must have possessed many lingering attachments to the mortal world. Did living in the forest turn him into a Taoist hermit?]","[Heavenly Demon: This is quite an interesting tale. He says that when a man named Wi Hochang appeared one day, the leader of the troop changed as well.]","[Wild Grylls: Do you mean he killed the leader and took his place?]","[Heavenly Demon: Essentially. What is even more astonishing is that the Blood Demon apparently reached the Life-and-Death Realm and underwent Feathered Ascension.]","[Wild Grylls: The Life-and-Death Realm? Feathered Ascension? What are those?]","I felt as though I had heard the terms somewhere before, but I had no idea what they meant.","Judging by the Heavenly Demon’s astonishment, it must have been an unimaginably lofty realm.","[Heavenly Demon: The Life-and-Death Realm comes after the Profound Realm, which is the realm this Lady currently inhabits. Those who reach it become qualified to undergo Feathered Ascension and can accomplish anything through will alone.]","[Wild Grylls: What is Feathered Ascension?]","The Heavenly Demon repeatedly asked whether the Blood Demon had truly undergone Feathered Ascension.","I still did not know what that meant, but I questioned Kkobong as she requested.","However, Kkobong apparently did not know the term Feathered Ascension . He merely said that Wi Hochang had gone up into the sky.","He even added the phrase \"from time to time.\"","Apparently, whenever the Blood Demon rose into the sky, the bewildered gorillas would desperately cling to his trouser legs.","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm. From that description alone, this Lady cannot tell whether he is truly referring to Feathered Ascension. Nevertheless, there is a strong possibility that the Blood Demon did undergo it.]","[Wild Grylls: Probably. The gorilla leader was wearing his clothes, after all.]","Feathered Ascension or not, the Blood Demon, Wi Hochang, was no longer in this forest.","I did not know the precise details, but it seemed he had led quite an eventful life before departing.","\"#$%%!!\"","When the discussion turned to what happened after the Blood Demon’s Feathered Ascension, Kkobong flew into a rage.","According to the Heavenly Demon’s translation, he had been driven out of the troop immediately after the Blood Demon disappeared.","The troop had resisted his presence so fiercely that even his own brother, Wi Heuk—the current gorilla leader—had been left with no choice.","Naturally, Kkobong could not help but harbor resentment toward the gorilla troop.","I suppose they had no choice if they wanted to survive...","Kkobong was an albino gorilla, an individual who stood out wherever he went.","His presence could easily have endangered the others, so his banishment was understandable.","Judging by the intensity of their opposition, he should have been expelled long ago. As it turned out, the Blood Demon had been preventing it.","Apparently, the Blood Demon had even killed the previous leader because he tried to banish Kkobong despite being warned not to.","Did he have some kind of trauma concerning persecution?","There was the story about him massacring a particular ethnic group out of a desire for revenge, along with the way he had protected Kkobong.","Perhaps he himself had belonged to a persecuted ethnic minority, which made him particularly sensitive to such matters.","Of course, that was only my hypothesis, so I could not be certain.","If I wanted to learn the details, I would have no choice but to visit the gorilla leader, Wi Heuk.","He might have written a book in the meantime, or perhaps left behind some other clues.","[Heavenly Demon: It would be best to post this story on the Gallery.]","[Wild Grylls: What? Won’t those weird people start causing another uproar?]","In the middle of our conversation, the Heavenly Demon made a strange suggestion.","Feathered Ascension meant becoming an immortal. Put simply, it was \"ascension.\"","The Blood Cult had splintered and been reduced to causing trouble in the Gallery because the Blood Demon had disappeared.","But what if it turned out that the Blood Demon had undergone Feathered Ascension?","That would grant them legitimacy where none had existed before. It would hardly be surprising if they began treating the Blood Demon as a martyr.","All kinds of terrorists commit atrocities on Earth too. If anything, this world must be even worse.","Would the Heavenly Demon have suggested it without realizing that?","I did not think so.","She must have had a plan of her own.","[Heavenly Demon: You need not worry about that. We can use this opportunity to crush all the vermin.]","[Wild Grylls: Vermin?]","[Heavenly Demon: As you have seen for yourself, those from the Blood Cult also run rampant within the Gallery.]","There were too many malicious Gallery users to count.","But apparently, the Blood Cult members were the worst of them all.","Not only did they worship the mass murderer known as the Blood Demon, but they occasionally committed copycat crimes whenever the mood struck them.","The reason no related posts appeared in searches was that the head administrator and the Heavenly Demon thoroughly deleted them and issued bans.","However, unless someone had a registered account, filtering anonymous posts was practically meaningless.","Unlike registered users, anonymous users returned shortly after being banned.","According to one person’s hypothesis, that was because the mana they absorbed was constantly changing.","Just as the water one drank each day was not literally the same water, the same principle applied to mana.","That was why banning anonymous users accomplished little.","One might then ask why registered users were different. Did they not also absorb different mana over time?","The situation was slightly different. If anonymous users were identified by their mana, registered users were identified by their dantian.","Of course, although all of this sounded plausible, it was ultimately only a hypothesis and should not be taken too seriously.","Uh... Come to think of it, I think I understand what they’re talking about.","I had seen plenty of them on the internet—users who made you wonder whether they were genuinely mentally ill.","Some were merely playing a character, but others were the real thing, employing genuinely disturbing speech patterns and logic.","At this point, one might ask whether it was truly so strange to worship someone who had lived several decades ago.","There are bastards who worship Hitler, so the Blood Demon isn’t much of a stretch.","The development of the internet had accelerated the exchange of information, but it had also spread dangerous ideologies.","Moreover, because information traveled so quickly, it could also be distorted in increasingly subtle ways.","When you looked into the truth behind the people being idolized, most of them turned out to be thoroughly unimpressive.","Perhaps that was what the Heavenly Demon was aiming for.","It would be like luring out hidden cockroaches so they could be exterminated.","Luring out the cockroaches is all well and good...","But who was going to exterminate them?","That was a problem in itself.","Since the Heavenly Demon had suggested this herself, she must have had a solution.","Frankly speaking, all I had to do was drop the post and walk away. It was what people called pleasure without responsibility.","The incident with the Immortal King had merely made me more cautious. I had always been safely positioned in the eye of the storm.","[Wild Grylls: I’ll ask the head administrator for permission first. I don’t want to get on his bad side.]","[Heavenly Demon: Do so.]","It would be a serious nuisance if I got banned over this.","I immediately informed the head administrator.","[Wild Grylls: I don’t mind posting it, but will you be able to handle the aftermath? I think it could cause serious problems in the real world too.]","[Heavenly Demon: This Lady shall deal with everything, so you need not worry.]","Was the Gallery alone insufficient to relieve her loneliness and boredom?","After hearing the Heavenly Demon’s response, I considered it for a while before making my decision.","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: This much is fine! It isn’t an inflammatory propaganda post!]","[Wild Grylls: Isn’t provoking tension and conflict between nations prohibited?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: I think anyone who unquestioningly believes a gorilla’s claims is an idiot!]","[Wild Grylls: Um...]","Now that I thought about it, he had a point.","In any case, now that I had permission, I uploaded the recorded videos exactly as they were.","Title: Apparently, the Blood Demon underwent Feathered Ascension?","Wild Grylls","(Video of Kkobong saying that the Blood Demon underwent Feathered Ascension)","(Video of Kkobong angrily recounting his past)","From what he says, it sounds like the Blood Demon has already undergone Feathered Ascension. He keeps mentioning that the man repeatedly went up into the sky.","Does that mean Wi Hochang should be considered alive? Or how exactly does this work?","└SwordMaster: He underwent Feathered Ascension? Just how powerful was this man?","└Wild Grylls: According to the Heavenly Demon, he reached the Life-and-Death Realm. What do people in the West call that?","└SwordMaster: We don’t have a specific term for it. Most people ascend after reaching that point, so they can no longer influence the mortal world.","└Wait. Does that mean those two gorillas are the Blood Demon’s official successors?","└Holy shit, his successors are gorillas. Lmao.","└Those Blood Cult bastards worshipped the Blood Demon so obsessively, only to find out they’re worth less than gorillas. Lmfao.","—Wasn’t the gorilla leader fucking strong, though? He even used the Heavy Hand Technique.","└Those gorillas are simply powerful, dude;;","└Aww, are the Blood Cult fanatics seething? That still doesn’t change the fact that you’re inferior to gorillas, does it?","└Your precious Hochang is gone now. Lmao.","The comment section—and probably the Gallery as a whole—would become rather chaotic from this point onward.","Evening was approaching, so I wrapped up my work.","\"Kkobong, come upriver with me. The rest of you come along too.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","\"...\"","I headed upriver with my animal companions to prepare dinner.","Ordinarily, I would have retrieved the fish traps alone, but now I had Kkobong.","Once I showed him how to collect them, he copied me with ease.","This is exactly why you need a worker.","Having another pair of hands made everything so much easier.","Of course, I would still have to handle all the delicate work, such as cleaning and cooking the fish.","\"Keh-eng!\"","\"What kind of herb did you bring me today?\"","The die had been cast. I quietly closed the Gallery.","As a bonus, Father Raccoon had brought me more medicinal herbs. This time, he had brought an entire bundle.","The herb had striking snow-white flowers. I would have to ask about its effects later.","After we finished eating and I completed the cleanup, I accessed the Gallery again.","By now, I expected the Blood Cult members to be throwing an enormous tantrum.","Just as expected.","As expected, the Blood Cult and the other users were fiercely battling for control of the comment sections.","Not that it meant much, since the Blood Cult was already such an irredeemable mess.","Still, they were remarkably skilled at getting under people’s skin, and the ensuing flame war was incredibly intense.","[Sure, but you’re still beneath gorillas. Lmao.]","Of course, that single remark had every one of them seething.","Since it was an attack firmly based on fact, none of them could refute it.","Will the Heavenly Demon really be able to handle this?","With that thought, I opened the Gallery’s trending-post section.","One particularly conspicuous title caught my eye, and I opened it as if entranced.","Title: I’m Going to Kill Those Fucking Gorillas","BloodDemonRebornAllBloodBows","(Photo of palms stained red)","(Photo of the symbol representing the Blood Cult)","(Photo of a secret manual passed down within the Blood Cult)","This Sovereign shall never acknowledge those witless beasts as his successors.","This Sovereign will personally seek them out and claim their heads.","Furthermore, the one who dared mock the Blood Demon shall not escape unscathed.","I could not tell whether the post was part of an act or completely genuine.","Had it come from an anonymous user, I would have dismissed it. But the fact that the poster had created a registered account made it slightly more credible.","There are more lunatics out there than anyone could imagine, after all.","I was not particularly concerned.","If he wanted to come, he was welcome to try.","I was about to leave a comment when—","└Heavenly Demon: This Lady thought you were merely skilled at empty boasting, but it seems you are also talented at coloring pictures.","└BloodDemonRebornAllBloodBows: I cannot tell which of us is merely running their mouth. If you do not fear this Sovereign, show yourself before me in person.","—Heavenly Demon: Wait. This Lady shall send you a private message.","The Heavenly Demon’s comment was sitting there in plain sight.","Isn’t this an actual challenge to an IRL fight?","It felt as though something incredibly entertaining was about to happen."]},{"title":"Chapter 158","paragraphs":["IRL Fight (2)","In every era, there were people who went beyond remembering the past and actively worshipped it.","This was especially true when that past was not merely glorious but had left an indelible mark on history.","It was similar to the familiar refrain, \"Back in my day...\"","The two races that displayed this tendency most prominently were humans and elves.","Since founding their nation, the elves had never experienced a humiliating period in their history.","This stood in stark contrast to the demons, their greatest rivals, who had once run rampant only to have the tables turned on them by the Hero.","However, just as daylight could not last forever, even the brilliance of their golden age eventually began to fade.","That was why the elves who remembered that golden age became trapped in the past, constantly muttering, \"Back in my day...\"","—Then what about humans?","└What do you think? They’re dopamine addicts even worse than the demons.","└Humanity’s highs are absurdly high, so its history is full of all kinds of crazy events;;","—Just look at El Dorado. They strutted around with their chests puffed out for ages after subjugating the Immortal King.","└People still worship the First Hero even now.","—Isn’t that basically like digging up his corpse and desecrating it?;;","└These things normally fade with time. The First Hero is the strange exception. Nobody worships ancient rulers anymore.","Humans were a race whose lows were bottomless but whose highs were absurdly lofty.","Most of the figures who had left a significant mark on world history, such as the Immortal King, were humans.","But did anyone actually worship the Immortal King?","There were some, but only in the Gallery.","If they tried doing that in the real world, they would deserve to be punched by a random passerby.","└BloodDemonRebornAllBloodBows: Even if those mongrels swarmed him, the Blood Demon would not shed a single drop of blood.","└Looks like one of the Blood Demon’s mutts has arrived. But I think he might actually be right?","└Yeah. Honestly, the Blood Demon’s impact was greater. He practically split the martial world in half.","—The Orthodox–Blood War wiped out an entire generation of masters. There’s a reason the Heavenly Demon isn’t as famous. Lol.","—The Orthodox–Blood War happened fifty years ago. How could there still be a shortage of masters?","└If your spine breaks, can you still move your legs?","└Even the promising talents of the younger generation were wiped out. You can imagine what happened to everyone below them.","└What’s the Blood Demon? I occasionally hear about bastards from something called the Blood Cult causing trouble in the real world.","└Those are actual remnants of the Blood Cult;;","└The same Blood Cult remnants causing trouble in the real world are also running rampant in the Gallery.","└Oh.","└But isn’t the Heavenly Demon more famous these days? And just to be clear, I mean the real Heavenly Demon, not the registered user.","└That’s true, but she’s slightly lacking in impact.","└She beheaded the emperor. She defeated all the masters too.","The Blood Demon, however, was slightly different.","They might be called mere remnants, but unlike the Immortal King, he still had genuine followers.","The difference was that the Immortal King had been an undead who was \"subjugated,\" whereas the Blood Demon had demonstrated transcendent human strength before simply \"disappearing.\"","Being drawn toward an overwhelmingly powerful being and wanting to enter the safety of their domain was a natural animal instinct.","No matter how far humanity advanced, that instinct would always remain embedded at its foundation.","People simply did not act on it collectively because they could distinguish right from wrong and wanted to preserve the existing social order.","—The Demonic Cult hasn’t really done anything noteworthy lately either. The Heavenly Demon appeared in the martial world once, and that was it.","└What are they doing these days?","└They’re probably asleep right now.","└Well, it is about time to sleep. Lmao.","└This is so ridiculous. Lol.","The imperial authorities had left the matter entirely to the masters of the martial world without intervening.","Apparently, it was a long-standing tradition.","That was why the government remained quiet even when remnants of the Blood Cult—or the so-called Blood Demon Corps—caused trouble.","Thanks to this combination of factors, the Blood Demon possessed greater name recognition than the Heavenly Demon.","Furthermore, the Blood Cult’s aggressive advertising(?) had also made him infamous throughout the Gallery.","By now, it was difficult to tell whether the Blood Demon had created the meme or the meme had created the Blood Demon.","Either way, fame was still fame.","—Also, every bastard who worships the Blood Demon in real life is completely insane, so it’s better not to provoke them.","└Yeah. You avoid shit because it’s filthy, not because you’re afraid of it.","└This is the martial world. Just think of it as accidentally stepping in shit;;","└Sometimes that shit jumps on me first, though.","The peculiar culture of the Central Plains also played a significant role.","The government and the martial world did not interfere in each other’s affairs.","The authorities stayed out of the martial world—even though the Blood Demon had taken the lives of countless masters and had harmed civilians.","—So public safety there is just fucking terrible. How is that any different from a lawless wasteland?","└That’s why the average person in the Central Plains is absurdly strong. If you pick a fight with some random kid on the street, you’re fucked.","└There’s even a saying in the martial world that you should beware of the elderly, women, and children.","└How are ordinary people supposed to survive?","└They either build connections or strengthen themselves.","└For reference, inns are destroyed by fighting masters practically every day. Lmao.","—That’s why the emperor reduced taxes for inns. That was genuinely a good policy.","—You mean the emperor who got clapped by the Heavenly Demon?","└Yeah, and the next emperor immediately abolished it. Lol.","└Fuck, why are all the emperors of the Central Plains completely useless? The previous emperor even banned the Gallery.","└The country is simply showing signs of collapse.","Still, it was not as though the imperial authorities did absolutely nothing.","A fight between martial artists might be one thing, but the Blood Cult was an organization that harmed civilians.","Since ancient times, when popular support shifted from the government to a particular faction, the country would inevitably fracture.","For that reason, the authorities protected public sentiment in their own way by offering generous compensation and reducing taxes.","Most importantly, the Central Plains covered an enormous territory.","Unless an incident was serious enough to overthrow the entire nation, there was no way the government could respond to every single event.","The Blood Cult had only attempted to drown the martial world in blood. It had never planned to conquer the imperial government.","For this variety of complicated reasons, the authorities quietly swept matters under the rug even when Blood Cult remnants committed atrocities in the real world.","└So what’s the conclusion? Wi Hochang is alive!!","└Wi!","└Ho!","└Chang!","└If he underwent Feathered Ascension, should that even count as being alive? Besides, his successors are gorillas. Lmao.","└The Blood Demon watches over us from the heavens!","└Worship him! Wi Hochang!","└This is driving me insane. Lol.","└They’re causing even more trouble now that they’ve heard he underwent Feathered Ascension;;","└If he really did undergo Feathered Ascension, then I guess we can’t complain about people worshipping him.","└Just please don’t cause trouble in the real world.","Whether sincerely or as part of a meme, the Blood Demon Wi Hochang was worshipped by many.","Plenty of people disliked this atmosphere, but one person was more displeased than anyone else.","\"I don’t like this.\"","That person was the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol.","Whenever stories about Wi Hochang circulated through the Gallery, she could not conceal her displeasure.","She was already thoroughly familiar with the Blood Demon’s reputation.","He was a great demon who had piled corpses into mountains and turned blood into rivers.","He had left an enormous mark on the history of the martial world, and his followers remained active to this day.","Yu Sowol did not like that.","She, too, had left a tremendous mark not only on the martial world but upon the entire Central Plains.","When she first entered the martial world, she defeated every renowned master who stood before her. She had even gone on to behead the emperor.","However, people dismissed the former achievement by claiming that the aftermath of the Orthodox–Blood War had left her with nothing but third-rate opponents.","As for the latter, the imperial family had suppressed and distorted the news.","What did any of her boasting in the Gallery matter if no one worshipped her in the real world?","This Lady is not entirely blameless, though.","Then was Yu Sowol completely without fault?","No, that could not be said.","One of the many problems was her registered username.","She had boldly created an account under the name \"Heavenly Demon.\"","Then she had used that account to spout all manner of martial-boomer nonsense, so naturally, the prestige of the name had faded somewhat.","The decisive problem was that she had done practically nothing since first emerging into the martial world. The remnants of the Blood Cult, meanwhile, had remained consistently active.","The Demonic Brain, Wi Seorak, had advised her to be patient, insisting that the time had not yet come, but...","Now that things have come to this, it seems this Lady has no choice but to go in person.","Since her opponent had challenged her to an \"IRL fight,\" she could no longer avoid confronting him personally.","If she backed down now, the honor of the registered user Heavenly Demon—not the real Heavenly Demon—would fall to the ground.","The honor of the registered user Heavenly Demon was also tied to the pride of Yu Sowol as a human being. Retreat was therefore out of the question.","Yu Sowol immediately summoned Wi Seorak.","\"This Lady shall be away for a short while.\"","Upon hearing that, Wi Seorak struggled to keep his expression under control. The area beneath his eyes kept twitching.","He looked as though he might clutch the back of his neck and collapse at any moment.","For now, he pretended not to know anything and asked why.","After all, this was far from the first time Yu Sowol had caused such an incident.","\"...Heavens above. May I ask your reason?\"","\"It is a personal matter.\"","You’re going to fight someone you met online, you immature woman.","Wi Seorak barely managed to swallow the words rising to his throat.","Things had seemed peaceful lately, but she was finally about to cause another disaster.","As a Gallery user himself, he knew perfectly well what was happening.","But what good did knowing do?","An unstoppable calamity was already upon him.","Wi Seorak racked his brain, wondering how he could persuade Yu Sowol to tell him the truth.","First, this matter must remain completely secret.","Even if a location had been chosen, there was no guarantee that the opponent would actually appear.","If the matter did not remain secret, spectators would undoubtedly gather. And if Yu Sowol ended up standing there all alone...","If she continued waiting there by herself for an opponent who might never arrive...","The mere thought of how people would treat her afterward was horrifying.","Therefore, Yu Sowol needed to handle the matter personally and in the utmost secrecy.","But this is strange. She usually ignores such things. Is it because the opponent belongs to the Blood Cult?","The Heavenly Demon had received plenty of challenges to IRL fights.","Her habit of posting whatever she wanted without caring what others thought had irritated many people.","As far as he knew, she had merely snorted and ignored every previous challenge.","This time, however, her reaction was different. It seemed to be because her opponent had a registered account and was suspected of being an actual remnant of the Blood Demon’s forces.","With that thought, Wi Seorak spoke respectfully.","\"Even if it is a personal matter, we are those who serve the Heavens. The will of the Heavens is our will, and only while the Heavens remain above us can the subjects below continue to live.\"","If you move, we have no choice but to move with you. So please tell us your intentions.","Yu Sowol understood his meaning and ceased being stubborn.","In truth, she also had concerns of her own.","If this Lady goes personally, they might discover that we are the same person.","That was her greatest concern.","Her registered identity might be exposed.","To prevent that, she intended to choose a sparsely populated location, but there was no telling what would happen.","After all, her opponent was the one choosing the meeting place. Yu Sowol knew little about the local geography.","In conclusion, it might be better not to go.","Yu Sowol nodded and spoke.","\"Even though he has sullied the name of the Heavenly Demon?\"","She referred to herself as \"the Heavenly Demon\" instead of \"this Lady.\"","If she used her usual form of address, it would practically confirm that she was the registered user Heavenly Demon.","At first glance, it sounded as though she intended to punish an impostor—but Wi Seorak knew better.","He was already fully aware that she was the registered user known as Heavenly Demon.","That’s it!","Still, it did not matter.","Getting her to admit the truth was enough.","Wi Seorak inwardly cheered before speaking respectfully.","\"No matter how violently vermin struggle, they remain nothing more than vermin. Showing mercy is also a virtue.\"","\"Would you have this Lady remain still when a bug has flown into her ear?\"","The Blood Demon Corps really got under her skin.","Wi Seorak understood immediately.","Yu Sowol was already displeased that the Blood Demon enjoyed greater recognition(?) than the Heavenly Demon.","Furthermore, the Blood Cult was naturally poised to gain even more influence.","After all, Grylls had revealed both the Blood Demon’s fate and his supposed Feathered Ascension.","Yu Sowol must have intended to turn that situation to her advantage.","Wi Seorak finally understood her plan.","But we don’t even know whether her opponent is genuine.","The Heavenly Demon was undoubtedly the real Heavenly Demon.","But was the other person genuine too?","More than half the information circulating through the Gallery was false, and posts from registered users were no exception.","The Gallery was a place where everything had to be taken with a grain of salt.","What, then, should they do?","As Wi Seorak considered the question—","\"Hmm. What an amusing fellow.\"","\"Pardon?\"","\"Access the Gallery.\"","While he was lost in thought, Yu Sowol gave him an order.","Wi Seorak was briefly puzzled, but he quickly realized that something must have happened in the Gallery.","He hurriedly accessed it and looked through the posts.","[Heavenly Demon, Behold.]","Recommendations poured in, propelling the post into the trending section almost instantly.","Wi Seorak opened it without delay.","Title: Heavenly Demon, Behold","BloodDemonRebornAllBloodBows","(Photo of a map showing somewhere in the middle of a major city)","I have chosen the location where our martial duel shall take place.","Your severed head shall serve as the signal announcing the Blood Cult’s return.","—Heavenly Demon: What an arrogant wretch. This Lady shall engrave her might upon your very bones.","└BloodDemonRebornAllBloodBows: I eagerly await the day I bathe my body in your blood.","└Damn. Just imagining this duel makes my heart swell. Lmao.","└Look at the way these martial-boomer bastards talk. Lmfao.","—Doesn’t this count as prohibited socializing?","└IRL fights are exempt from the rule against socializing. People genuinely fight each other surprisingly often. Lol.","\"What an amusing fellow. The same goes for that person impersonating this Lady.\"","\"...\"","You posted that comment yourself. How can you be so shameless?","Wi Seorak stared blankly at the utterly brazen Yu Sowol.","Then an idea flashed through his mind, and his expression abruptly changed.","No. Wait. Wouldn’t this actually be better?","Wi Seorak immediately shared his idea with Yu Sowol.","\"That is quite...\"","After hearing his proposal, Yu Sowol—","\"This Lady likes it.\"","—curved her lips into a pleased smile.","***","Meanwhile, at the same time, Grylls was reading the trending post.","\"Ah, I’m jealous. I want to see it too.\"","He was deeply disappointed that he would not be able to witness such an awe-inspiring duel."]},{"title":"Chapter 159","paragraphs":["IRL Fight (3)","Humanity developed language and, eventually, built civilization, learning to resolve problems through words.","People exchanged words to bridge differences of opinion that could not easily be narrowed, striving to minimize conflict.","That was the decisive difference between humans and beasts: the possibility of resolving problems through words.","However, because humans ultimately pursued their own individual interests, some matters could not be resolved through dialogue alone.","At times like those, they resorted to force—which, in a way, was actually more convenient than conversation.","A binary method that clearly determined a winner and a loser. It was truly simple.","The Gallery was no different.","In fact, unlike the real world, the Gallery was a place dominated by anonymity.","That made people less inclined to persuade the other party.","When a conflict arose, it was more common to mock the other person or stubbornly insist on one’s own opinion than to try to bridge the difference between them.","Since no one could swing a sword on a message board, the person who lost their temper and went berserk was essentially considered the loser.","But occasionally, someone would issue a challenge to an \"IRL showdown.\"","Since they could not settle their differences, they would decide the matter through force instead. That was roughly the idea.","Title: Isn’t challenging someone to an IRL showdown basically admitting defeat?","Your logic is so fucking amazing that I’ve got nothing left to say, so let’s fight.","Isn’t that basically what they’re declaring when they issue the challenge?","└ Yeah, exactly. That’s why almost nobody actually accepts an IRL challenge, lol. Have you ever seen one? Because I haven’t, lmao.","└ Gallery fights should be settled in the Gallery. What’s the point of fighting IRL? lol","└ The person who issued the challenge is the only one who ends up looking pathetic, lol.","Title: Upvote if you’re hyped for the IRL showdown between the Heavenly Demon and the Blood Demon Corps, lololol","Starting with me, lololol.","└ I’m so fucking jealous of the people in the Central Plains. They get to watch such an entertaining match.","└ I live in the Central Plains, but I can’t upvote this.","└ Why?","└ I don’t live anywhere near that region... The Central Plains are so huge that it takes several days just to travel from one city to another.","└ Doesn’t the Central Plains have something like a teleportation system?","└ It does, but I’d have to transfer several times, so it would cost way too much money. T_T","Since issuing the challenge itself was considered an admission of defeat, IRL showdowns were rarely proposed or accepted.","The person being challenged had nothing to lose whether they accepted or refused.","That was why such showdowns rarely happened in reality.","Most users merely chuckled and moved on.","But when an IRL showdown was actually arranged, nothing could be more entertaining.","And if the participants were registered users who were famous even among other registered users?","No one could resist watching that.","The Heavenly Demon, in particular, was even a moderator, so the showdown naturally attracted even more attention.","└ Haven’t moderators fought IRL before?","└ Yeah. A demon and an elf. The junior mod accused the head mod of not doing any work, so they fought IRL.","└ They said the winner would get the moderator position, but they both died, lol.","└ And they still didn’t ban IRL challenges?","└ Why would they? They said they wanted to fight, lololol.","└ I’ve fought someone IRL before too. I’m on my way to dig that bastard’s grave right now.","└ Holy shit, did you actually kill him?","└ No. We became friends while fighting, but he died of natural causes. Human lifespans are really short.","└ Oh dear...","└ Damn...","└ That’s actually kind of sad.","└ You must’ve been really close if you’re going all the way there to dig his grave.","The users eagerly anticipated the first IRL showdown between registered users in a very long time.","Most showdowns ended with the participants throwing their arms around each other’s shoulders and becoming friends.","But that only accounted for roughly seventy percent of them.","In the remaining thirty percent, they fought bloody battles until one of them died.","After all, this was not Earth, protected by a complex society and strict laws.","Furthermore, people fighting each other was simply an everyday occurrence in the Central Plains.","Clamor— Clamor—","A public square in Shaanxi Province of the Central Plains.","As Shaanxi was one of the Central Plains’ major regions, many people came and went through it.","Yet for some reason, an unusually large number of people were standing around the square today, waiting.","\"Excuse me.\"","\"Hmm? What is it?\"","\"Just what is happening here for so many people to have gathered?\"","A martial artist who had been observing the situation approached a passerby and asked.","The passerby examined the martial artist’s appearance.","Unlike a commoner, he had a neat, well-groomed appearance and a carefully maintained beard.","Finally, his black martial robes provided a rough indication of his origins.","\"Ah, it’s nothing serious. It just looks like there’s going to be a fight here soon.\"","\"A fight? Between martial artists?\"","\"I don’t know that much. Have you ever heard of the Gallery?\"","\"The Gallery? You mean that vulgar invention?\"","The martial artist frowned as he replied. He was clearly not fond of the Gallery.","Regardless, the passerby explained why so many people had gathered.","\"You don’t know much about the Gallery, so I’ll keep it brief. You know that anonymity is the norm there, correct?\"","\"Of course. That is precisely why all manner of vulgar words are exchanged there.\"","\"That means even when people fight, they usually don’t carry it over into the real world. But this time...\"","The passerby gave him a rough account of everything that had happened so far.","As the explanation continued, the martial artist’s expression gradually changed.","First came curiosity, then contempt, and finally—","\"What?! The Blood Cult bastards are coming here?!\"","\"Yes. That’s why the other martial artists have come as well.\"","His expression became one of shock.","None other than the remnants of the Blood Cult had issued an IRL challenge.","The Blood Cult was a faction that continued to cause trouble at every opportunity. Even its remnants could not be ignored.","No matter how many times they were stamped out, they never disappeared. Calling them cockroaches would be the most fitting description.","Their mere existence inflicted emotional distress upon others.","’Come to think of it, I heard a rumor that the Blood Demon attained immortality...’","The rumor had begun circulating approximately two days ago.","It claimed that Wi Hochang, the Blood Demon—the source of the Great War of Righteousness and Blood and the vilest demonic fiend of all—had actually ascended to immortality.","Since the rumor had originated in the Gallery, he had only half believed it. But that was no longer the case.","After hearing the complete story from the passerby, something about it felt unsettling.","The timing was far too coincidental.","’What if the Blood Demon really did attain immortality, and the Blood Cult intends to use that as an opportunity to regain its influence?’","More importantly, they had accepted an IRL challenge in the Gallery, where anonymity was the default.","Only someone utterly confident in their martial arts would dare to do such a thing.","That was why he could not bring himself to leave.","Had the Blood Cult’s name not been involved, he likely would have simply clicked his tongue and dismissed the matter as pathetic.","The same was probably true for the other martial artists gathered here.","\"Place your bets on who will win!\"","\"I’m betting on the Heavenly Demon!\"","\"The Heavenly Demon, my ass! Are you underestimating the Blood Demon Corps?!\"","\"What Blood Demon Corps?! They’re probably six of one and half a dozen of the other!\"","’Should I just ignore this?’","His seriousness lasted only a moment. As soon as people began wagering money, the martial artist sighed inwardly.","Normally, whenever a fight broke out in the Central Plains, people fled to avoid getting caught up in it.","From a civilian’s perspective, a battle between martial artists was nothing short of a natural disaster.","But this situation was slightly different.","This was a fight between registered users of the Gallery.","It belonged neither to the government nor to the murim, but to an unrelated third party.","Even now, the government soldiers were watching from a safe distance.","Was this a matter of the murim or not?","Should the principle of noninterference between the government and the murim apply, or should it not?","The situation was so ambiguous that they could do nothing but observe.","As the appointed hour gradually approached, more and more people gathered.","\"What did you just say? How dare you insult our sect?!\"","\"You were the one who insulted us first, you bastard!\"","Whenever people gathered, conversation naturally followed—and so did conflict.","With so many people present, fights both large and small began breaking out everywhere.","The Central Plains was a place where fists flew before words could be spoken.","Scattered fights began erupting among the martial artists.","\"Now, now. Everyone calm down. We didn’t come here to watch you people fight, so keep it quiet.\"","\"What did you just—!\"","\"I said keep it quiet.\"","And the only thing capable of suppressing force was even greater force.","It would hardly be surprising if the occasional so-called \"master\" were mixed in among the spectators.","As a result, time passed surprisingly peacefully.","Then, just as the appointed hour was nearly upon them—","\"Why isn’t anyone here yet?\"","\"Don’t tell me they were all talk and ran away.\"","\"Come on. That would be seriously disappointing.\"","Neither of the two registered users known for speaking like senile martial arts fossils on the Gallery had shown so much as the tip of their noses.","Normally, they should have proudly declared their usernames and presented themselves.","But with the appointed time nearly upon them and neither one in sight, the crowd could not help becoming suspicious.","’Of course. The Gallery is ninety percent lies and only ten percent truth.’","The martial artist who had first questioned the passerby clicked his tongue as well.","Disappointed, he turned around.","Thud!","\"Urgh!\"","He collided with something enormous, as though a boulder had been standing behind him.","The impact knocked him backward.","Falling over was humiliating enough, yet the passerby he had collided with merely continued walking forward in silence.","The martial artist’s face twisted into an angry scowl as he shouted at the man pushing his way through the crowd.","\"Hey! Aren’t you even going to apologize?!\"","\"...\"","At the martial artist’s shout, the passerby slowly glanced back at him before turning away again.","It was the reaction of someone who did not consider him worth responding to.","The martial artist’s pride was wounded. His expression hardened with anger as he rose to his feet.","\"How dare you treat me—!\"","Clench!","Just as the martial artist was about to continue, an enormous hand seized his head without warning.","It was large enough to engulf a man’s entire head—calling it the size of a cauldron lid would not have been an exaggeration.","Crack!","The hand squeezed, and the martial artist’s head burst like a watermelon.","Bright-red blood sprayed in every direction as fragments of his shattered skull rained to the ground.","A human life had been snuffed out in an instant—and in a horrifyingly brutal manner at that.","\"Aaaaargh!\"","\"W-What have you done?!\"","The gruesome sight sent the crowd screaming into a panic.","Even the people of the Central Plains, who were accustomed to combat and killing, found the scene far too brutal.","Yet the giant completely ignored their reactions and hurled the corpse forward.","It landed precisely where the IRL showdown was supposed to take place.","Thud!","The headless corpse fell into the open space the spectators had deliberately created.","Naturally, the startled crowd turned toward the direction from which it had come.","Step. Step. Step.","Like the parting of the Red Sea, the crowd split before the approaching giant.","The people of the Central Plains were generally not very large, but this man looked well over two meters tall.","He wore a rough, tattered martial robe, and his hair had been grown out like a lion’s mane.","Drip. Drip.","Finally, there were his palms, red as blood.","The sight made everyone think of a single organization.","The Blood Cult.","The giant looked around at the frozen crowd, drew a deep breath, and roared.","\"When the Blood Demon returns, all blood shall bow! I am Geumjang! Where is the Heavenly Demon?! I shall announce the Blood Cult’s return with your blood!\"","The giant revealed both his registered username and his true name.","The instant he declared his objective as well, the crowd descended into terror.","\"Th-The Blood Cult! He’s one of the Blood Cult’s remnants!\"","\"R-Run! A real Blood Cultist is here!\"","\"Aaaaargh!\"","They had assumed it was merely another one of the Gallery’s usual jokes.","But the moment they realized it was a vicious reality rather than a prank, they fled for their lives.","Once the civilians had escaped, only the martial artists remained.","They were the ones who had decided that a remnant of the Blood Cult had to be eliminated immediately.","\"It really is the Blood Cult...\"","\"If that’s Geumjang... isn’t he one of the Blood Demon’s disciples?\"","\"I can’t believe he’s still alive.\"","The Blood Cult might be mocked as a meme on the Gallery, but the real Blood Cult could never be taken lightly.","Furthermore, Geumjang was not someone who could simply be dismissed as a \"remnant.\"","He was a demonic master who had made a name for himself during the Great War of Righteousness and Blood.","The martial artists charged at him, but—","\"Aaaaargh!\"","\"B-Brother! This is— Aaargh!\"","\"Kahahahaha! Blood! Show me more blood!\"","They were no match for him.","Geumjang was a master who had survived the Great War of Righteousness and Blood.","There was no way the martial artists of the present age, whose overall standards had declined, could contend with him.","The longer the battle continued, the redder his palms became with the martial artists’ blood.","Crack!","Geumjang casually crushed another martial artist’s head in his grasp and surveyed his surroundings.","Corpses without a single intact part littered the square, and the ground had already been dyed scarlet with blood.","Geumjang smiled in satisfaction and checked whether anyone else remained.","There was no one.","’Good.’","He immediately looked into the air and did the following.","Title: I hereby announce the Blood Cult’s return.","When the Blood Demon returns, all blood shall bow","(Photo of the blood-soaked square)","(Photo of the square littered with corpses)","As of today, I hereby announce the Blood Cult’s return. Descendants of the Blood Cult, come to our former sacred ground so that we may fulfill our long-cherished ambition.","The Blood Demon is watching over us from the heavens. We shall never be broken!","He had logged into the Gallery and written a post.","A post this graphic would naturally get him banned, but he did not care. He had written it fully expecting that consequence.","His goal was to reunite the members of the Blood Cult scattered across the world.","That was what made the Gallery so useful.","’It saves me the trouble of searching for them one by one.’","Rumors spread slowly in the real world.","But not on the Gallery.","Rumors on the Gallery blazed as though someone had poured oil over them.","That was precisely what Geumjang was counting on.","Even a short amount of time would be enough.","’That Heavenly Demon bastard was nothing special either. The moment they saw this, they turned tail and—’","Just as Geumjang was about to leave, satisfied—","\"What a wicked pastime. To befoul the ground so thoroughly.\"","\"?!\"","A delicate woman’s voice pierced his ears.","Geumjang could not help but jump in surprise.","He had remained alert, ready to respond to anything that might happen at any time or place.","Yet he had failed to sense her presence.","He turned toward the source of the voice.","\"You wench...\"","\"You are quite tall. How many cheok are you?\"","A woman stood there wearing a traditional black hat angled strangely enough to conceal her face.","She was dressed in black, and her figure appeared slender overall.","Even so, it could not conceal her mature femininity.","Her beauty could be inferred from the lower half of her face alone. She could certainly be called a peerless beauty.","\"Kneel.\"","\"What?\"","\"This lady commanded you to kneel.\"","The woman had abruptly ordered him to kneel simply because he was tall.","Geumjang was dumbfounded.","Why were so many people begging to die today?","Not that he minded.","Nothing could please him more than spilling even more blood across the ground.","Geumjang snorted and spoke to the woman.","\"You tell amusing jokes. Are those your last words?\"","\"This lady is entirely serious.\"","Thud!","The instant she finished speaking, Geumjang closed the distance between them.","Moving faster than the eye could follow, he thrust out his blood-red palm.","It was the exact same stance—and the exact same attack—as the one a certain gorilla had once demonstrated.","The strike seemed certain to burst the woman’s head, but—","Tap.","\"Wh-What?!\"","It was stopped by a single impossibly slender index finger.","The woman spoke once more to the bewildered Geumjang.","\"Did I not tell you?\"","Her tone was arrogant.","But it came not from conceit, but absolute confidence.","\"This lady was serious.\"","The Heavenly Demon had descended."]},{"title":"Chapter 160","paragraphs":["IRL Fight (4)","’Th-This can’t be...!’","Geumjang could not believe what was happening.","His bloodstained palm—and the finger effortlessly holding it back.","A slender finger that looked as though it would snap with a mere squeeze had casually stopped his palm strike.","That would be impossible unless the difference between their martial arts was overwhelming.","In other words, the gulf between the woman and him was as vast as heaven and earth.","\"Haaah!\"","But Geumjang did not give up. Denying the reality before him, he attacked again.","It was said that masters could gauge the difference between them without ever crossing swords.","Yet Geumjang could sense absolutely nothing from this woman.","She seemed like an ordinary civilian.","Geumjang had reached the Transformation Realm—and not merely its early stage, but the middle stage.","He had undergone bodily reformation and could perfectly control the internal energy that had once rampaged within him like a wild stallion.","Furthermore, what was the current state of the murim?","Had its overall standards not declined drastically because of the Blood Demon’s bloody rampage?","His battle with the martial artists moments ago had confirmed that this was no mere rumor, but the truth.","Thus, both emotionally and rationally, Geumjang had no choice but to deny this impossible situation.","Otherwise, he would have to acknowledge that the woman before him was stronger than he was.","Whoooosh!","His bloodstained palm shot toward the woman’s face once more.","It moved so quickly that the sound of the wind tearing apart could be heard clearly.","Yet the woman maintained the smile beneath her hat and moved her hand.","Just as before, she placed her index finger against his bloodstained palm.","But she did not stop there.","She moved her finger slightly to the side.","To emphasize, it was only a slight movement—at least by the woman’s standards.","Swoosh!","Geumjang’s hand swept past the side of her face.","But that was not all.","Perhaps he had been unable to withstand his own momentum, or perhaps the woman had done something.","Crash!","Geumjang fell.","And in the most humiliating manner imaginable.","He had gone beyond merely kneeling, ending up with both hands planted on the ground as well.","While Geumjang reeled in confusion at the unbelievable reality before him, the woman quietly looked down at him.","\"This lady told you to kneel. I did not tell you to crawl like a dog.\"","\"...\"","\"Stand again. Then kneel and pay your respects to the heavens—\"","Whoosh!","The woman’s command was cut short.","Still on all fours, Geumjang had launched a backward kick.","Unlike before, he did not roar in fury. His expression was cold and calculating.","Perhaps even the woman had not anticipated the surprise attack, for she barely evaded it by tilting her head back.","In that instant, Geumjang forcefully sprang away from her.","\"You are an arrogant wench. But I can see that you have reason for that arrogance.\"","Geumjang spoke to her in a calmer voice than before.","Seemingly surprised by his reaction, the woman tilted her head slightly.","Her hat made it impossible to see her full expression, but her lips twisted faintly.","\"There are fools who believe that the depth of one’s martial arts is everything. That will be your fatal mistake.\"","Geumjang had survived the Great War of Righteousness and Blood, in which countless supreme masters had perished.","There was only one reason he had survived that war.","Objectivity.","If an opponent’s martial arts surpassed his own, he acknowledged it immediately.","With a monster like the Blood Demon standing above him, swallowing his pride was nothing difficult.","Geumjang’s specialty was using that exceptional objectivity to find a way to defeat his opponents, no matter what means he had to employ.","Since ancient times, it was not the strong who survived.","Those who survived were strong.","Geumjang, a survivor of the Great War of Righteousness and Blood, perfectly embodied that principle.","\"You talk too much. First...\"","Rustle.","The woman raised her slender hand.","Geumjang’s expression tightened at the movement.","She then took one step forward.","It was quite literally a single step.","Whoosh!","\"...!!!\"","Geumjang’s eyes widened.","Despite taking only one step, the woman had appeared directly before him.","It was an overwhelming display of martial prowess that seemed to disregard the very constraints of space.","’Sh-Shrinking the Earth into Inches?!’","While he stared in shock, the woman slowly extended her raised hand.","\"I suppose I must tear out that tongue of yours first.\"","Those words snapped Geumjang back to his senses, and he immediately responded.","A cornered mouse could always bite a cat to death.","Without even realizing that he had begun to think of himself as the mouse, Geumjang swept his leg out like a whip.","He planned to break the woman’s balance first and then look for an opening.","Swoosh!","His leg hurtled toward the woman’s ankle with the speed of an arrow.","Until the very instant before it connected, the woman did nothing.","Geumjang rejoiced inwardly, convinced that she had fallen for it.","Tap.","But at some point, the woman had slightly lifted her foot and casually blocked the kick.","At the same time, she thrust her raised hand toward Geumjang’s mouth.","Geumjang had not completely ruled out such a possibility, so he retreated.","Swoosh!","The instant he pulled back, he swept his leg upward, kicking up a cloud of dust.","The thick cloud obscured her vision.","Cowardly?","What did cowardice matter in a fight to the death?","If one could fight with honorable confidence, one could also fight with shameless confidence.","After all, it was not the strong who survived.","Those who survived were strong.","Rooooar!","Taking advantage of her obscured vision, Geumjang unleashed another palm strike.","This time, however, he did not attack her directly. He projected his internal energy outward.","A colossal palm-shaped mass of energy surged toward where the woman had been standing.","True to his epithet, Blood Hand, even the enormous palm was dyed crimson like blood.","Crack—Crash!","The mighty palm blasted through the woman’s position and destroyed every structure behind her.","Just like the gorilla suspected of being the Blood Demon’s successor, he had carved out an entirely new path.","But Geumjang’s foremost concern was whether the woman had survived.","As he scrutinized the devastated area—","\"Are you finished?\"","\"!!!\"","The woman’s voice came from behind him.","Startled out of his wits, Geumjang instinctively launched an attack behind him.","Slip!","\"Guh?!\"","But he was too late.","Before he could strike, something had already slipped into his mouth.","At the same time, his tongue was firmly seized.","Geumjang stared ahead in shock.","Perhaps the force of his previous attack had blown away her hat, for the woman’s face was now completely revealed.","He had already guessed from the lower half of her face that she was a beauty, but her fully revealed appearance exceeded his expectations by an immeasurable degree.","A peerless beauty.","A magnificent flower blooming in the highest reaches of heaven.","Geumjang was briefly entranced by her beauty and noble bearing, only belatedly becoming aware of his physical condition.","’My... my internal energy...!’","He could not use his internal energy, despite none of his acupoints having been sealed.","She had done nothing but seize his tongue.","Geumjang was utterly bewildered.","\"You seem surprised. I suppose that is understandable. You cannot use your internal energy, after all.\"","\"Urgh...\"","\"Now, I shall tell you the one and only way you may survive.\"","The woman—the Heavenly Demon—issued the command once more.","\"Kneel.\"","\"If you kneel, I shall at least spare your life.\"","Geumjang’s answer had already been decided.","Being unable to use his internal energy was not a problem.","His dantian remained intact.","He still had a secret art that he had intended to preserve until the very last moment.","It would not have mattered even if his acupoints had been sealed.","This secret art functioned entirely independently of them.","\"Khehehe...\"","\"Hmm. It seems you have something to say.\"","Hearing Geumjang’s laughter, the Heavenly Demon released his tongue.","With his tongue free again, Geumjang gave her a sinister smile.","\"You remain as arrogant as ever. This is why cats end up being bitten to death by mice.\"","\"...\"","\"Blood Cult! Remember this day! I shall spill my blood upon this land before I depart!\"","Geumjang shouted resolutely and concentrated all his energy into his dantian.","He would use all his internal energy as gunpowder and his dantian as the detonator.","Ordinarily, more than half of Shaanxi would have been engulfed in an enormous explosion.","Yes.","Ordinarily.","\"...?\"","Geumjang was puzzled.","Why had the secret art not activated?","He had unquestionably gathered his energy within his dantian for this very purpose.","Yet now, he could no longer feel it.","\"Is this your dantian? It is as red as blood. Or is that because it is literally covered in blood?\"","\"...Huh?\"","Instead, an excruciating pain erupted in his lower abdomen.","With a dumbfounded expression, Geumjang looked toward her left hand.","Even Geumjang had never seen a person’s dantian with his own eyes.","A dantian was not a tangible organ to begin with, but a convergence of intangible energy.","Yet a crimson mass of energy rested in the Heavenly Demon’s hand.","Then what of his lower abdomen?","Overwhelmed by the pain, he looked down and discovered a hole in it.","Crush!","The Heavenly Demon closed her hand, casually crushing his dantian.","The moment Geumjang witnessed it, all color drained from his face.","His greatest strength—and his greatest weakness—was his objectivity.","Thus, he fully accepted the situation before him.","He understood.","No attack, defense, or desperate struggle would work against her.","She was truly the heaven above the heavens.","\"Did you call yourself a mouse? That does not appear to be the case in this lady’s eyes.\"","The Heavenly Demon smiled serenely.","To Geumjang, that smile resembled the smile of a reaper.","She then seized him by the neck and spoke.","\"You are nothing more than an insignificant insect.\"","\"...\"","\"This lady has no interest in insects that bite people.\"","The Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, issued her proclamation.","\"I merely exterminate them.\"","Crack!","Geumjang’s neck bent at a right angle.","Yu Sowol casually tossed aside the corpse of Geumjang, who had been toyed with until his death.","Splat!","His body tumbled across the blood-soaked ground.","She looked around.","Perhaps realizing that the situation was over, the people who had been hiding cautiously began creeping out.","Their eyes contained fear, terror, reverence, and countless other emotions.","Yu Sowol said nothing and simply turned her back on them.","Then, as though nothing had happened, she vanished from the spot in an instant.","All she left behind was the traditional hat she had dropped on the ground.","Once even Yu Sowol was gone, the remaining people spoke in trembling voices.","\"What... What did I just witness...?\"","\"I-I don’t know either.\"","The situation had been so chaotic that everyone hurriedly asked the others what had happened.","Normally, they would have exchanged their thoughts, but—","\"A-A post has appeared on the Gallery! It looks like someone recorded the whole thing!\"","\"Is-Is that true?\"","\"It is! Hurry and watch it!\"","This was a world where the Gallery existed.","Everyone hurriedly logged into it to witness the Heavenly Demon’s martial prowess for themselves.","\"Good heavens...! Such incredible martial prowess...!\"","\"Is that peerless beauty truly the Heavenly Demon?\"","\"Was the registered user Heavenly Demon actually the real Heavenly Demon?\"","\"Don’t be ridiculous! She must have come to punish the impersonator!\"","An earth-shattering topic had been dropped onto the Gallery.","During this IRL showdown, Yu Sowol had followed Wi Seorak’s advice.","His advice had gone roughly as follows.","Yu Sowol would go there not as the registered user Heavenly Demon, but as the real Heavenly Demon.","Once there, she would seek out the person who had sullied the Heavenly Demon’s name.","It would be fine if her opponent failed to appear, and equally fine if they did.","Whether they appeared or not did not matter.","After all, she had the justification of being there to punish the one who had disgraced the Heavenly Demon’s name.","Wi Seorak had added that matters would become far simpler if her opponent—and an actual remnant of the Blood Cult at that—appeared.","She would merely have to personally dispose of the Blood Cult remnant and proudly proclaim her identity.","Then what would happen to the registered user Heavenly Demon?","Wi Seorak had offered no advice regarding that.","It could not be helped.","The user had dared to disgrace the Heavenly Demon’s name, so as far as he was concerned, it did not matter whether the impersonator lived or died.","Yu Sowol agreed with that reasoning, so she had said nothing more.","’He did not seem to suspect that we are the same person at all.’","Contrary to Yu Sowol’s belief, the perceptive Wi Seorak already knew everything.","It was precisely because he knew everything that he had offered no advice on that particular matter.","After considering the problem, Yu Sowol had devised her own solution.","Thus, the present situation was akin to a performance jointly orchestrated by Yu Sowol and Wi Seorak.","The only problem was that her opponent had not been an actor in their performance.","’It matters not.’","Especially when that opponent had treated human lives like insects.","She might arrogantly call herself the Heavenly Demon, but she was at least a ruler who understood the value of life.","Even when people mocked her on the Gallery for speaking like a senile martial arts fossil, she tolerated it magnanimously.","As someone had once put it, she was simply a little starved for \"attention.\"","By nature, she was closer to good than evil.","Title: Is the registered user Heavenly Demon the real Heavenly Demon?","(Video of Yu Sowol toying with Geumjang)","Are the registered user Heavenly Demon and the real Heavenly Demon the same person? Is this actually real?","└ Stop bullshitting. Do you seriously think that’s possible?","└ If the real Heavenly Demon used the Gallery, everyone in the Demonic Cult would have a collective heart attack.","└ Wow, but she’s seriously beautiful, lol.","└ Forget her beauty, she’s fucking strong. Look at her toy with him like a dog.","└ Isn’t this going to be deleted? It’s pretty graphic.","└ It keeps getting deleted, but anonymous users keep reposting it.","└ Damn, lol. Blood Cult bastards can’t even get past the Heavenly Demon!","└ Is the Heavenly Demon a god? Is the Heavenly Demon a god?","Title: The registered user Heavenly Demon isn’t the real Heavenly Demon.","I heard what that Heavenly Demon said. She said she came to punish the person who was disgracing the Heavenly Demon’s name.","└ Are you friends with that Heavenly Demon?","└ We’re not friends, but I’m from the Demonic Cult, so I heard the rumors. She said she was going to punish whoever had sullied the Heavenly Demon’s name.","└ Makes sense that people from the Demonic Cult would react like that. The impersonator probably never expected the real one to show up, lol.","└ Is the Heavenly Demon popular in the Demonic Cult?","└ Fairly popular. She doesn’t interfere with us much, and life there is reasonably comfortable.","Title: Junior mod, explain yourself.","What the fuck were you doing while the real Heavenly Demon was coming? Were you just sitting quietly in the background?","└ They summoned the Heavenly Demon and did absolutely nothing else, lololol.","└ Heavenly Demon Summoning Art, damn.","└ \"Heavenly Demon Summoning Art,\" fucking hell, lolololol.","└ Isn’t that even more impressive? lolololol.","Above all, there was this attention.","Just look at the explosive topic that had set the entire Gallery ablaze.","Both as the Heavenly Demon Yu Sowol and as the person Yu Sowol, she could not have been more satisfied.","Ordinarily, she would have had to explain herself, but... did she really need to?","She could simply sit back and watch.","She could delete a few posts while she was at it.","She could always claim that her explanation had been delayed because she was carrying out her duties as a junior moderator.","└ Wild Grylls) That person isn’t the Heavenly Demon. She wasn’t even using the sword I gave her.","└ Is that sword particularly conspicuous?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. It stands out like fucking crazy.","└ She beat him senseless with her bare hands. Why would she need a sword?","└ Wild Grylls) I guess so? But she’s a swordswoman, and she wasn’t carrying anything.","There was even unexpected supporting fire from Grylls.","Yu Sowol was pleased with everything.","’Truly satisfying.’","Of course—","\"That woman really does seem like the Heavenly Demon, though. Is she extremely bored or something? She’s surprisingly young. That must be because of her cultivation level too, right?\"","After experiencing a considerably more advanced internet culture, Grylls had already figured out the truth to some extent.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]},{"title":"Chapter 161","paragraphs":["IRL Fight (5)","The IRL showdown I’d only ever heard about had actually happened. I’d heard plenty of stories about them, but this was the first time I’d ever seen one actually take place.","It felt like I was witnessing an antiquated custom straight out of some bygone romantic era.","’Who cares about meeting up in real life? Winning online is all that matters.’","Besides, the world I’d come from had the ultimate finishing move: \"I’m suing you.\"","Of course, filing a lawsuit was essentially a self-destruct button, since it created a huge headache for both parties.","Moreover, it generally only worked in cases of one-sided malicious comments. If both parties could potentially be held responsible, lawsuits usually weren’t an option.","’And the biggest problem is having your face exposed.’","Just look at the Blood Demon. No one even knew what he looked like, yet he was being used for all kinds of memes.","If an IRL confrontation went sideways, you wouldn’t have any grounds to complain when people mocked you relentlessly.","Human malice didn’t disappear just because the era or the world changed.","If anything, Earth’s internet culture seemed even more vulgar.","’It became more depraved as it advanced, I guess.’","Putting that aside, I watched the recording of the Heavenly Demon’s martial prowess.","In the video, a woman dressed in black stood across from a massive man wearing an old, tattered martial arts uniform.","The difference in their physiques was obvious.","Yet despite that difference, the woman was toying with him one-sidedly.","’She’s beautiful.’","The way she toyed with him was impressive, but the Heavenly Demon’s appearance stood out even more.","Her beauty rivaled that of the elves, who were known as the race of beauty. No, perhaps she was even more beautiful than them.","Combined with her aloof air, she resembled a flower blooming atop a sheer cliff.","A flower that required one to overcome countless hardships to pluck, only to discover that even its stem was covered in thorns.","Her strength, beauty, and bearing were all truly befitting the grandeur of the title \"Heavenly Demon.\"","’Someone like her talks like such an old geezer on the gallery?’","I couldn’t be certain whether this Heavenly Demon was the same person as the assistant manager Heavenly Demon.","But for some reason, I had a strong feeling that they were one and the same.","The speech that had made her seem old on the gallery became maturity in reality, while her pigheaded image transformed into aloof dignity.","Then there was the way she seemed to sing praises of her own beauty. There was hardly any difference between her online and real-life personas.","The only potential issues were that she probably held a high position or was quite old, but neither particularly mattered.","└ How incredible is the Heavenly Demon? I’m from the West, so I don’t really know.","└ Smart Demonic Cultist: This is related to the history of the Central Plains. Do you happen to know about the burning of books and burying of scholars?","└ Nope.","└ Smart Demonic Cultist: Just think of it as going beyond persecuting scholars and outright exiling them. There’s this policy of keeping the masses ignorant in the Central Plains—","└ What the hell does that mean, nerd?","└ Stop talking about crap only you understand and give us a one-line summary.","└ Smart Demonic Cultist: She’s just fucking amaaaaaazingly incredible. Is that good enough? She personally took the emperor’s head, too.","└ \"One-line summary\" [7 people]","└ That wasn’t one line, though? Kek.","└ Just fucking get the point, kek.","The very title of \"Heavenly Demon\" meant that she was the leader of the Demonic Cult.","The larger an organization was, the harder it was to dismiss its leader.","Besides, people grew into their positions. The Heavenly Demon’s way of speaking might have changed after she assumed that role.","’If you think about it, arrogance is really just overflowing confidence.’","More importantly, I recalled the Heavenly Demon’s opponent—the registered user who had posted that disgusting image earlier.","The registered user had uploaded photographs of a blood-soaked floor and corpses while the moderators were absent.","The post was deleted shortly afterward, but I’d already read it. And I had realized something.","The Heavenly Demon had only killed people who deserved to die.","’I should at least give her some covering fire.’","I argued that the woman couldn’t be the assistant manager Heavenly Demon because she hadn’t been carrying the sword I had given her.","As everyone knew, the Heavenly Demon was a swordswoman. An exceptional one at that, considering she possessed a ten-thousand-year cold iron sword.","She had toyed with that man barehanded, so having a sword probably wouldn’t have made any difference.","Still, from my perspective, it would be better if the Heavenly Demon’s identity remained hidden.","’I’d hate it if she disappeared because of this.’","More importantly, what would change even if I saw through her identity?","It was meaningless as long as I couldn’t leave this place, and it would still be fine even if I did eventually escape.","We had treated each other with courtesy and respect on a gallery where anonymity was guaranteed.","Would things really be different in reality? I didn’t think so.","’She’s also the person most likely to be capable of rescuing me.’","If the Heavenly Demon’s identity was exposed and she went into hiding, there would be absolutely no benefit for me.","The best outcome was for us to continue speaking respectfully as usual so that I could keep asking her for advice.","I watched the gallery erupt over the Heavenly Demon for a while before sending a message.","Naturally, I sent it to the person who should have been the busiest right now—the Heavenly Demon herself.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, are you busy?]","[Heavenly Demon: This Lady is always at leisure. What is it?]","I had expected her to be busy preparing an explanation—or perhaps an \"explanation\"—but she replied unexpectedly quickly.","At this speed, she was practically watching the commotion like a fire on the opposite side of a river.","After wondering about it briefly, I asked her about the gallery’s current topic.","[Wild Grylls: Are you really the Heavenly Demon?]","[Heavenly Demon: If I said I was, what would you do?]","[Wild Grylls: I doubt anything would change. You’d still be my benefactor.]","[Heavenly Demon: That answer pleases me.]","[Wild Grylls: So, are you really her?]","[Heavenly Demon: The real Heavenly Demon is a vastly greater being.]","Wasn’t she just praising herself?","Even though it strongly felt as if she was desperately trying to deny it, I decided to let it slide.","As I had said earlier, I wanted to maintain my friendly relationship with the Heavenly Demon.","[Wild Grylls: Understood. So when do you plan to explain yourself? I think this will keep raging until you personally say something.]","[Heavenly Demon: I wish to enjoy it for now. Seeing them praise me so greatly warms my heart.]","At least this much was certain: the Heavenly Demon was enjoying the attention.","That explained both her wariness toward the Blood Demon, who was worshiped as a meme, and the attention-seeking posts she had made before becoming an assistant manager.","Despite being the type to march to the beat of her own drum, she still wanted the other users’ attention.","’That’s understandable.’","So the Heavenly Demon was human, too.","Surprisingly, that made her even more charming.","Besides, she didn’t harm others with crude insults or jokes about their parents.","At the very least, she seemed closer to good than evil.","That was the impression I got.","[Heavenly Demon: Still, there is something that concerns me.]","[Wild Grylls: What is it?]","[Heavenly Demon: Some may believe that I and the real Heavenly Demon are the same person. Would you not agree?]","[Wild Grylls: I suppose... that’s possible?]","Apparently, she wanted to keep enjoying the gallery as she always had.","After all, the Heavenly Demon loved the very concept of an online gallery.","I considered her words for a moment before replying.","[Wild Grylls: You are going to post a separate explanation, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: Naturally.]","[Wild Grylls: Then I don’t think you need to worry too much. Things probably won’t change that much.]","[Heavenly Demon: Why not?]","[Wild Grylls: Because you don’t know any of the people talking about you, do you?]","Even if the users knew who the Heavenly Demon was, the Heavenly Demon didn’t know who they were. That was the key point.","It was a one-way street, not a two-way one.","The only issue was that the real Heavenly Demon’s reputation might be tarnished.","[Heavenly Demon: It matters not. People insult even the emperor when he is not around, so why bother stopping them? If they could insult me to my face, I might even acknowledge them.]","[Wild Grylls: \"Me\"?]","[Heavenly Demon: It was a slip of the tongue. In any event, it does not concern me, so there is no need to worry.]","She herself seemed unconcerned.","And honestly, the Heavenly Demon was completely right.","This was a gallery where people called even the emperor by all sorts of derogatory nicknames. There was no reason the Heavenly Demon would be treated differently.","If anything, mere derogatory nicknames were rather mild. As for Earth... I wouldn’t elaborate.","I had learned that a single person could accumulate a truly astounding number of nicknames.","’Athletes had tons of bizarre nicknames. I wonder if it’s the same here?’","I could look into it gradually.","In any case, there seemed to be no need to worry about the Heavenly Demon’s anonymity.","She had apparently found her own way of dealing with it, and our relationship hadn’t changed from before.","So Geumjang was insanely strong, and the Heavenly Demon had toyed with someone like him.","If someone on the Heavenly Demon’s level entered the Forest of Four Seasons, wouldn’t she become a ruler of one of its territories?","As that pointless thought crossed my mind, I turned my head.","Kkobong was diligently sawing wood nearby.","’I wonder if Kkobong knows this Geumjang guy.’","Curious, I asked the Heavenly Demon to write Geumjang’s name for me.","After receiving it, I called Kkobong over.","\"Kkobong! Come here for a second!\"","[Wild Grylls: By the way, who is this Geumjang person?]","[Heavenly Demon: I asked my aide, and apparently he was one of the Blood Cult’s elders. He possessed fairly respectable skills.]","[Wild Grylls: I wouldn’t stand a chance against him, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: He was roughly equal to that leader fellow, not the white one.]","Kkobong stopped sawing and came running over.","Until two days ago, he had ignored me whenever I called him, but now he came obediently.","It seemed he had begun to trust me after I gave him the glasses.","\"Do you know who this is?\"","When I wrote the name on the ground, Kkobong stared at it for quite some time.","Then, as though recognizing it, he nodded and looked at me.","\"#%@#%\"","\"...You still can’t speak Korean, can you?\"","\"Ooh-kee?\"","\"Ugh. F**k.\"","I needed to teach him quickly. It was frustrating as hell not being able to communicate.","Besides, using the Heavenly Demon as an interpreter every time was rather cumbersome. I felt bad about it, too.","In any event, the Heavenly Demon translated Kkobong’s answer exactly.","[Wild Grylls: Will they come to the Forest of Four Seasons in search of the successor?]","Whether they intended to kill the successor or take him back, this should have been a fairly important matter to the Blood Cult.","Even Geumjang, who should have served as both their central pillar and greatest military force, had fallen at the Heavenly Demon’s hands.","Could the Blood Cult possibly do anything after getting on the Heavenly Demon’s bad side?","They had nothing.","Unless they were desperate enough to come looking for Kkobong and the gorilla leader while practically clinging to their trouser legs.","[Heavenly Demon: He says Geumjang was his most trustworthy subordinate. Apparently, he had originally designated him as the Blood Cult’s next successor.]","[Wild Grylls: So he was an incredibly important figure. If someone like that disappeared...]","[Heavenly Demon: Then those gorillas truly are the successors.]","[Heavenly Demon: It is not impossible. The world is vast, and there are many lunatics. According to my aide, the members of the Blood Cult are thoroughly insane, even by the standards of lunatics.]","[Wild Grylls: I want normal people. I’d rather avoid lunatics.]","No matter how much I missed human company, I had no desire to live alongside followers of Hitler.","Not only would we be unable to communicate, but they might also try to harm me.","’Though no normal person would come anywhere near the Forest of Four Seasons...’","Even on Earth, people got lured into cults and committed all sorts of bizarre acts. How much worse would this world be?","It would certainly be worse, never better.","Deciding to keep an eye on the Blood Cult’s activities for the time being, I spoke to the Heavenly Demon again.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you for telling me. You’re going to post something soon, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: I have prepared an explanation perfectly suited to the gallery’s users. It incorporates your advice as well, so you may look forward to it.]","[Wild Grylls: Oh. I’m looking forward to it.]","[This Lady Is the Heavenly Demon.]","A title that could never be ignored caught my eye. It had even been posted by the Heavenly Demon herself.","Had she decided to simply announce who she was after everything she’d said?","Confused by her contradictory behavior, I opened the post.","Perhaps there were so many people viewing it that the gallery lagged slightly.","Just what kind of explanation had she prepared to make me look forward to it?","I tossed Kkobong a fasting pill and told him he’d done well.","Kkobong happily began eating it as though it were delicious.","The swift sloth gave me a strange look, but I deliberately ignored it. I still had plenty left.","’Let’s see. She should have posted it by now...’","That was when I saw it while browsing the gallery.","Title: This Lady Is the Heavenly Demon","Heavenly Demon","In truth, that was a lie.","But what will you do about it?","What can any of you do, you insignificant creatures?","Other than growing angry, hurling insults, and belittling me, what can you possibly do? I can hear the resentment of creatures who cannot even reach the heavens.","└ Swordmaster: What the hell is this? Kekekekeke.","└ What the fuck? Kekekekeke. This is supposed to be the Heavenly Demon? What a load of bullshit. Kekekekek.","└ If that really is the Heavenly Demon, the Demonic Cult’s members are gonna cry. Seriously.","└ The fuck? How could something like that possibly be the Heavenly Demon? Kekeke. She’s just another gallery loser.","└ Smart Demonic Cultist: I’m just going to believe she isn’t. I think that’ll be easier on my heart.","└ Didn’t you say you were a member of the Demonic Cult last time? That thing is apparently your master.","└ Smart Demonic Cultist: Fuck, I said she isn’t, you bastard!","└ Why are you swearing at me...?","\"Um...\"","Whatever else might be said, one thing was certain.","’She really is wise, isn’t she?’","She was an exceedingly wise person."]},{"title":"Chapter 162","paragraphs":["The World Is Vast (1)","Thanks to the Heavenly Demon’s explanation-that-wasn’t-really-an-explanation, the users came to a realization.","Title: Who Cares If She’s the Real Heavenly Demon?","Who cares if the assistant manager is the Heavenly Demon? What difference does it make?","We can just keep mocking her as a crusty old martial arts boomer~","└ So we can just keep insulting the Heavenly Demon like before, right?","└ Yeah. Whether we’re insulting the real Heavenly Demon or the assistant manager Heavenly Demon, what’s the difference? Kekeke.","└ What are you going to do if she really is the Heavenly Demon? What can you do, Heavenly Demon? Kekeke.","└ She can ban you, though?","└ Whether it’s in reality or on the gallery, she still has all the power. Kekeke.","Whether the Heavenly Demon was real or fake was meaningless.","They could simply continue mocking her to their hearts’ content, just as they always had.","Of course, the Heavenly Demon was a registered user with a will of steel, someone who remained unfazed by most insults and provocations.","The users ultimately decided to maintain a strict(?) distinction between reality and the gallery.","’She even fooled me for a moment. Her years of experience really show at times like this.’","The Heavenly Demon had been an active registered user on the gallery for a long time.","Her manner of speaking might have been old-fashioned, but all that experience hadn’t gone anywhere.","Hadn’t I confidently started hurling insults when I’d nearly fallen victim to a scammer?","On the gallery, where desires disguised as honesty were standard, it was an appropriate response.","’Now I just need to watch whether the Blood Cult causes trouble.’","I stared at the Heavenly Demon’s post as its recommendations rose in real time, then returned to the gallery’s main page.","Everyone was going wild over her explanation post.","I was curious about how the Blood Cult had reacted, but unfortunately, it was difficult to pick out any relevant posts amid the commotion.","Even if a post related to the Blood Cult appeared, there would be no way to tell whether it was genuine.","’If the Blood Cult is full of lunatics like Geumjang, they’ll probably post something again.’","Until then, I could simply focus on my own work. I would leave the outside world to the people living in it.","After browsing the gallery a little more, I quietly closed—","Title: Taking Advantage of the Chaos","(Photograph of a female elf with an incredible figure)","Dropping a pic.","—No, I should save that first.","I glanced around, saved the picture, and then closed the gallery.","It was about time to get back to work. Kkobong had worked hard sawing the lumber, so now it needed to be shaped.","’Once we finish this, we should be ready to build the bridge.’","It had already been two days since Kkobong joined the company(?).","He had proven himself to be an outstanding worker, demonstrating remarkable efficiency.","Even with his mana sealed, his natural physical abilities made him excellent at manual labor.","Thanks to him, we finished producing the lumber in less than three days, even though I had expected it to take several.","\"Kkobong. We’re going to use these to build a bridge now. Do you understand me?\"","\"...\"","\"I’ll take that as a yes. Here, look at this.\"","Now that the lumber was ready, it was time to build the bridge.","I explained the structure of a da Vinci bridge to Kkobong and showed him the completed model I had made.","It was honestly simple enough to understand just by looking, even without a verbal explanation.","The fact that Kkobong was a gorilla was slightly concerning, but he was intelligent enough to learn human speech.","\"If you understand, try building one yourself.\"","I gave Kkobong some branches for the demonstration and instructed him to begin.","He pushed his glasses up and slowly stacked the branches as I had shown him.","At first, he seemed unable to grasp the trick, but he gradually began assembling it properly.","Before long, he completed the bridge far faster than I had on my first attempt.","\"Jjwareo.\"","\"Oh...\"","Kkobong showed me the completed bridge while apparently declaring that he was finished.","Judging by the result, he understood the structure perfectly. I was satisfied.","\"You get the general idea, right? Now we’re going to build this over the river.\"","\"...\"","\"The river is up there. It’s where I get the fish. You know the place, right?\"","If he understood, it was time to carry the lumber upstream.","With that, Kkobong and I began transporting the wood.","Anyone who had ever lifted a log would know that wood was incredibly heavy even by itself.","We had cut the wood with a saw and planed it down, reducing its size, but it was still wood.","Even after eating the eel and reinforcing myself with mana, my limit was carrying only a few pieces at once.","’But Kkobong... His strength really is monstrous.’","Despite being unable to use mana, Kkobong carried nearly as many pieces of lumber as I did with his bare hands.","I already knew that his natural physique was exceptional, but I hadn’t expected him to be stronger than me after I ate the eel.","His physical capabilities had probably risen so he could survive in the Forest of Four Seasons. Being a gorilla must have contributed as well.","We transported most of the lumber near the river, then searched for a suitable location.","Naturally, we needed to choose a place where the river was as narrow as possible and the current relatively weak.","I had measured the river’s width beforehand and cut the lumber based on that measurement, but there was always the chance of an error.","’The other side of the river is a mountain today.’","And it was a mountain with a clearly visible precipice.","Beyond the precipice stood countless mountains surrounded by a haze that might have been fog or clouds.","It was a breathtaking sight, but I had no particular desire to visit. I wanted to finish quickly and be done with it.","’First, I should check whether the golden frogs are here.’","I placed my hand in the river.","Normally, the frogs should have leaped out immediately.","However, none appeared.","How long had it been since the weather warmed up? Were they still hibernating?","They might also have migrated to another region.","Whatever the explanation, it was excellent news for me.","I told Kkobong that we were beginning the construction and started carefully stacking the lumber.","\"No, not there. You need to place it here.\"","\"Ooh?\"","\"Yeah. Right. There. Put it there.\"","Kkobong understood my instructions perfectly, allowing the work to proceed quickly.","If I had been doing this alone, it would have taken at least several days.","There was a reason I even gave him fasting pills.","The animals living in the Forest of Four Seasons went crazy for fasting pills as if they were chocolate.","\"Let’s see. The length... We only need to interlock it one more time. We’re almost done.\"","\"Hoo...\"","\"I know it’s annoying, but hold on a little longer. We’ll have a snack once we’re finished.\"","And so, the bridge was completed.","However, completing it and moving it into position were two entirely different matters.","We had to hold opposite ends of the bridge and carry it across the river.","’Just in case, I should tie a rope around myself.’","The current was strong, so preparing for an accident was essential.","I securely tied the rope to a tree, grabbed one end of the bridge, and slowly began moving.","Kkobong also held the structure firmly so that it wouldn’t collapse.","’Ah. Should I have tied ropes around all the interlocking sections?’","At the very least, I could have poured a little cement over them.","Why did these ideas always occur to me too late?","After briefly lamenting my stupidity, I maintained the bridge’s balance and moved all the way to the opposite bank.","Thanks to the extraordinary effectiveness of the shoes the dwarf had given me, I didn’t fall along the way.","\"Hoo-ah!\"","The instant we set the bridge down on the opposite bank, I hurried back.","With that, the da Vinci bridge was complete.","Now all that remained was to place planks over it.","Though it was only a temporary bridge, the structure was exceptionally good at supporting weight. A little more work should finish it.","Since I also had cement, I might even be able to turn it into a proper bridge rather than a temporary one.","Title: Bridge Complete!","Wild Grylls","(Photograph of a da Vinci bridge connecting to the opposite bank)","Kkobong and I worked together to build this bridge. Now we just need to place some planks over it.","People of the outside world, you are always welcome here. Cross this bridge to paradise and come visit me!","└ Heavenly Demon: It feels more like a bridge to hell than a bridge to paradise. Am I the only one under that impression?","└ Swordmaster: Surprisingly, I felt the same way.","└ Passing Dwarf: You built it better than I expected. Is that gorilla a good worker?","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah. He’s amaaaaaazingly good. Kekeke. I might promote him from laborer to assistant eventually.","└ Passing Dwarf: Why don’t you make a sword with him while you’re at it? Kekeke.","└ Wild Grylls: Is that possible?","└ Passing Dwarf: I can’t explain it in words, so figure it out yourself. Just hammer it into shape or something.","The Passing Dwarf’s explanation went something like this.","Blacksmithing was originally a profession in which it was difficult to work alone.","Until a blacksmith earned the title of \"Artisan,\" they couldn’t create tools by themselves.","Before reaching that level, blacksmiths always worked in teams of at least two.","’I’ll get around to it someday.’","It wasn’t urgent, so I simply took the suggestion as general advice.","If I started making tools myself, I would probably make a pickaxe first.","Besides, Kkobong and I couldn’t even communicate properly, so it would take a long time.","’I really do need to teach Kkobong how to speak.’","I had thought the same thing earlier, but the frustration of being unable to communicate was terrifying.","It would have been different if he were a speechless beast, but knowing that he was capable of learning language made it even more frustrating.","My original plan had been to keep talking to him until he gradually learned to understand me.","’But he’s far too capable.’","Over the past three days, I had discovered just how competent Kkobong was.","His talent(?) was too valuable to waste by using him only as a laborer.","I could understand why the Blood Demon had bothered teaching Kkobong martial arts.","He might not have been a genius capable of deducing ten things after being taught one, but he made sure to understand that one thing thoroughly.","Considering how many people failed to understand even a single thing after being taught it, he was an outstanding prospect.","\"Now, Kkobong. Look at me.\"","\"If we’re going to live together smoothly from now on, I need to understand what inconveniences you’re experiencing. That means we need to be able to communicate.\"","The instant I mentioned his discomfort, my gaze fell upon the suppressor around Kkobong’s neck.","Did I feel guilty?","Don’t make me laugh. He was the one who had tried to kill me first.","Without feeling the slightest pang of conscience, I continued.","\"You’ve heard everything I’ve said until now, right? Try saying any one of those words.\"","\"...\"","I didn’t know whether he could understand this instruction either, but I had to try.","I made an effort using both spoken words and body language.","Eventually, Kkobong realized what I wanted and nodded.","After thinking for a long time, he finally opened his mouth.","\"F**k.\"","\"...?\"","\"Ooh-ooh. F**k.\"","\"Hey. Wait a second.\"","It was an exceptionally vulgar curse.","I was utterly bewildered.","Of all the countless words he could have learned, why did he have to learn that one? Was it because of the particularly forceful intonation?","Then again, people did say that curses were the first words one learned in a foreign language.","Besides, I had often cursed while grumbling to myself.","\"What are you going to do after learning that? Don’t you know any other words?\"","\"Kkobong.\"","\"That’s your name. From now on, when I ask you a question, answer with ’Yes.’ Got it?\"","I decided I should begin by teaching him polite speech.","It wasn’t long after I made that decision that—","\"Fuck off.\"","\"You crazy monkey bastard! When did you learn that one?\"","\"You.\"","\"I’m seriously going insane.\"","We had a long, long road ahead of us.","***","Around the time Grylls began teaching Kkobong Korean, both the gallery and the Central Plains were in an uproar over the Blood Cult.","Although the Heavenly Demon had \"coincidentally\" passed by and defeated one of the Blood Cult’s elders, the fact remained that the cult had resumed its activities.","Members of the older generation who remembered the Blood Cult’s former power trembled in fear, while the younger generation also became vigilant.","Geumjang’s strength, in particular, had proven so overwhelming that even members of the older generation wouldn’t have dared to stop him.","They were fortunate that the Heavenly Demon had killed him. However, the general consensus was that the Blood Cult probably possessed more experts of similar strength.","└ Can’t the Heavenly Demon just kill all of them?","└ What justification would the Demonic Cult have for getting involved? She only came this time because someone was impersonating her.","└ Honestly, it’s better for the Demonic Cult to remain uninvolved. They’ve already made it clear that no one should mess with them.","└ The Demonic Cult can remain neutral only because it has the Heavenly Demon. The Martial Alliance is the only one that’s fucked.","└ The Martial Alliance isn’t what it used to be... It’s seriously grown weaker compared to the old days.","└ More like the Martial Dumbass Alliance now.","└ Martial Dumbass Alliance! Kekekekeke.","└ Listen to how good that sounds. Kekekeke.","Thus, while the Heavenly Demon’s fame skyrocketed, wariness toward the Blood Cult also intensified.","Meanwhile, the Blood Cult’s members had gathered at the \"holy land\" Geumjang mentioned.","\"Of course we should make the black gorilla our successor!\"","\"Ridiculous! How are we supposed to choose a creature that already leads its own troop? We would be better off choosing the white one!\"","\"No, why are we even considering a gorilla as our successor...?\"","\"Silence! We are having a serious discussion!\"","They were engaged in an absurd argument at the worst possible time."]},{"title":"Chapter 163","paragraphs":["The World Is Vast (2)","No matter the faction, a successor was important.","No one lived forever. Eventually, everyone returned to nature’s embrace.","Because all people knew that fate awaited them, each strove to leave behind a legacy.","A successor was part of that legacy. A successor with strong legitimacy was important to any organization.","If they lacked legitimacy, they would constantly be challenged by their retainers or subordinates, and even inheriting the position itself would become difficult.","In that sense, Geumjang had originally been designated as the successor to the Blood Demon, Wi Hochang.","Not only had he been the first subordinate Wi Hochang had accepted, but he had also remained loyal.","Moreover, he possessed more than enough leadership ability to command others, so the remnants of the Blood Cult had intended to follow him without complaint.","At least, until the Heavenly Demon suddenly appeared and snapped Geumjang’s neck.","\"What are we going to do now?\"","An aged voice echoed through the room.","The people sat facing one another, relying on a single lamp for light.","When the old man occupying the seat of honor spoke, the only response he received was a heavy silence.","\"Lord Geumjang was defeated by the Heavenly Demon. Who are we supposed to follow now?\"","Despite the question that bordered on lamentation, no one said a word. They had no answer.","After all, the long-awaited resurrection of the Blood Cult was on the verge of collapsing before it could even begin.","They had only been able to gather here because of the post Geumjang had made on the Gallery.","It had been an ambitious declaration calling upon them to assemble at the sacred ground and proclaim the Blood Cult’s return.","Yet not long after the post went up, a video was uploaded showing him being toyed with by the Heavenly Demon.","\"...Before deciding whom to follow, we should be worrying about whether the Blood Cult can even survive.\"","\"What do you mean by that?\"","\"Just as Elder Taejung said, we have no suitable successor. Worse still, we have lost the focal point that held us together.\"","The others groaned at the relatively young, middle-aged man’s words.","Nothing he said was wrong. At present, far from being resurrected, the Blood Cult was in danger of ceasing to exist altogether.","\"Most importantly, we have almost no new initiates. We have practically run out of young people.\"","In fact, the Blood Cult currently had almost no new recruits at all.","No matter how well-known the Blood Demon was on the Gallery, he was only famous there as a meme.","In the past, most of those who had joined the Blood Cult had been captivated by Wi Hochang’s martial prowess.","But the Righteous-Blood War had taken place a full fifty years ago. It might have been different if only ten years had passed, but half a century had gone by.","Even those who had been in their twenties at the time were now gray-haired old men. Those who had already been fully grown adults back then were in an even worse state.","More than half of the elders had died in the Righteous-Blood War, and half of the survivors had subsequently died from lingering injuries or natural causes.","Even the cultists who were considered relatively young were at least in their fifties. That alone said everything.","\"That... is a grave problem. Without fresh blood, the Blood Cult will naturally disappear. Do you know why no one is joining?\"","\"Hmph. Isn’t it because those green youngsters know nothing of the Blood Cult’s majesty?\"","\"Back in our day, the number of people who wanted to join was as vast as the sea....\"","\"This is all because of that damned Murim Alliance.\"","No, it’s because of you people.","The middle-aged man secretly curled his lips in mockery.","They were so intoxicated by their past glory that they could no longer see reality.","When the Blood Demon had still been around, everything had been fine as long as they followed him. But now he had ascended to immortality.","Moreover, the Murim Alliance, which had emerged victorious from the Righteous-Blood War, had exposed every sordid truth about the Blood Cult.","The Murim Alliance had plenty of skeletons in its own closet, but the victor always took everything, while the loser could do nothing but suffer.","The Blood Demon himself had massacred civilians, after all. In many respects, the Blood Cult was a vile organization that was bound to have difficulty winning anyone’s favor.","Despite this reality, they had failed to manage their image on the Gallery as well. All sorts of information about them had spread, and self-proclaimed Blood Cultists of dubious authenticity had even begun trolling the place, becoming synonymous with lunatics.","Now, whenever anyone so much as mentioned the Blood Cult, people would immediately mock them by saying that the cockroaches had arrived.","\"Silence, everyone! You know complaining like this will accomplish nothing! Come up with a solution!\"","\"If we demonstrate our strength, just as the Blood Demon once did....\"","\"Even Elder Geumjang was toyed with by the Heavenly Demon. What could we accomplish? We would only make the Heavenly Demon look even more impressive.\"","Countless arguments were exchanged, but no suitable solution emerged.","After all, most of them had grown old and lost both their strength and vigor.","To borrow the Gallery’s terminology, they were fossils trapped in a bygone era.","\"There is something more important than that, isn’t there?\"","\"What might that be?\"","\"Whom will we choose as the successor? Whatever else happens, we still need someone to lead us.\"","\"....\"","Let us choose a successor first.","Silence settled over the room at those words.","Everyone knew that they would never reach a consensus if they continued arguing like this.","Therefore, they should choose someone—anyone—as the successor and proceed according to that person’s will.","That was what he meant.","\"Ahem. With even Elder Geumjang having fallen....\"","\"How about Elder Taejung taking the position?\"","\"I am already far too old. It will not be long before this frail body returns to the earth.\"","\"Then whom would you nominate as the successor?\"","\"Since we are the Blood Cult, why not settle it according to the Blood Cult’s traditions?\"","The Blood Cult’s traditional method was simple.","They would fight until only one side remained alive.","It had been a fairly reasonable method during the Blood Cult’s heyday, but that was no longer the case.","Their numbers were so few that every single member was precious.","\"We should refrain from doing that. Fighting among ourselves would be problematic enough, but it would also severely undermine the successor’s legitimacy.\"","\"No one possessed legitimacy comparable to Geumjang’s....\"","Legitimacy within the Blood Cult was simple: it depended on how much instruction one had received from the Blood Demon, Wi Hochang.","Among them, Geumjang had even exchanged martial arts with the Blood Demon, making him the most suitable candidate.","Of course, that was all meaningless now.","In that case, the beings possessing the greatest legitimacy were....","\"Come to think of it, were there not apes whom the Blood Demon personally instructed?\"","\"They were not monkeys but apes. Great apes, to be precise—gorillas.\"","\"Surely you are not suggesting that we appoint those lowly beasts as successors?\"","No matter how far the Blood Cult had fallen, they were still human.","It was only natural for them to recoil at the idea of appointing mere apes as successors.","Even the Blood Cultists half agreed that this was a matter that went beyond simple pride, but....","\"Is there even one person here who inherited the Blood Demon’s martial arts?\"","\"I received a small amount of instruction....\"","\"But no one inherited them as completely as those great apes. Their martial arts may well be superior to ours, but they certainly will not be inferior.\"","\"Even so, appointing apes....\"","\"We would merely be naming one of them as the successor. That does not mean we must worship it.\"","The old man’s point was this: appointing it as the successor and revering it were two separate matters.","They could exploit it for everything it was worth and then secretly kill it.","All they needed was to obtain its martial arts.","It could even speak, so learning from it should not be particularly difficult.","\"Indeed....\"","\"It is not a bad option.\"","\"At the end of the day, it is still only an ape.\"","Through this dubious attempt at persuasion, they began leaning toward appointing an ape—a gorilla—as the successor.","After all, no matter how intelligent a gorilla might be, could it truly be smarter than a human?","\"Obviously, we should appoint the leader of the gorillas as the successor! He is the strongest among them.\"","\"Ridiculous! Have you not heard? That gorilla banished his own brother, the white gorilla! The Blood Demon himself was once cast out merely because his appearance was different. We can never accept such a creature!\"","\"Where did you hear that? I have never heard anything of the sort.\"","\"There was a post about it on the Gallery.\"","\"And you believe that?\"","By now, even the Blood Cult itself lacked reliable information about the Blood Demon.","And thus began a battle of idiots.","Should they choose the leader gorilla or Kkobong?","Martial strength or legitimacy(?)?","It should have been an utterly trivial debate, but somehow....","What kind of idiotic circus is this?","In the middle-aged man’s eyes, there had never been a farce quite like this one.","It had been obscured by the Blood Demon’s achievements, but the truth was that the Blood Cult itself had always been a somewhat deficient organization.","There had once been intelligent members among them, but they had all disappeared during the Righteous-Blood War.","Not a single person who could be called the organization’s \"brain\" remained.","More precisely, no one remained who could comprehend reality.","Then where had all the intelligent people gone?","They had joined either the Murim Alliance or the Demon Cult.","The only question was whether they chose to conform to the established system or resented it.","Either way, no sane person would willingly join the Blood Cult.","What do they think the Forest of Four Seasons is?","The middle-aged man had many things he wanted to say, but there were so many that he could not bring himself to say any of them.","He could not even tell where things had first gone wrong.","Fine. Let them appoint a gorilla as their successor. But how did they plan to bring it here?","Were they seriously planning to enter the Forest of Four Seasons, an inescapable hell and purgatory, themselves?","Thanks to Grylls’s recent activities, a great deal of information about the Forest of Four Seasons had become known, but it was still only the tip of the iceberg.","No one knew what dangers lurked inside it or, more importantly, whether it was even possible to escape.","\"Before that... there is something we must consider.\"","\"Ah, yes. What is your opinion?\"","\"That is not what I meant. The gorillas are in the Forest of Four Seasons.... Even if we manage to find them, will we be able to get back out?\"","\"It would be difficult alone.\"","It would be difficult alone.","In other words....","\"Why do we not all enter the Forest of Four Seasons together?\"","\"Together...?\"","\"Yes. The greater our numbers, the stronger our Blood Cult becomes. Surely the same will hold true within the Forest of Four Seasons.\"","\"Furthermore, is there not already a survivor inside? We can simply receive his assistance.\"","They had no plan whatsoever.","The middle-aged man instinctively realized that entering the forest with these reckless fools would be no different from suicide.","Why don’t you just suggest that we all hold hands and march to our deaths?","Did they not know of the Forest of Four Seasons’ dreadful reputation, or did they think this would be some noble expedition?","They said the world was wide and full of lunatics, but this went far beyond even that.","Wait. Isn’t the Blood Cult itself a den of lunatics?","And he had willingly entered that den.","The middle-aged man’s mouth fell slightly open.","He looked as though he had been struck by an overwhelming wave of existential despair, his pale soul practically drifting out of his body.","The old man mistook his reaction for admiration and smiled with satisfaction as he addressed the other cultists.","\"Then it seems we have narrowed our opinions down to one. However, the Forest of Four Seasons is known as a forbidden realm beyond human reach. We must prepare thoroughly.\"","\"Agreed. We should gather as many cultists as possible before departing.\"","\"I dislike the thought of accepting an ape as our successor... but I suppose there is no other choice.\"","\"Then what shall we do when we meet the survivor?\"","\"He has enslaved our successor. Naturally, he must face divine punishment.\"","Had their minds grown rigid with age?","Did they genuinely believe they could return alive from the Forest of Four Seasons?","Or were they simply empty-headed morons incapable of thought?","\"And what will you do?\"","\"Ah... I believe I must return to my hometown for a while.\"","\"Has something happened?\"","\"I heard that someone there wishes to join the cult.\"","\"Oh. That is welcome news. Very well.\"","On the day the Blood Cult began preparing to journey into the Forest of Four Seasons...","The middle-aged man fled from the Blood Cult.","└ Why do those people look so sinister? They’ve got some seriously vicious faces.","└ Now you understand how hard my life has been, right?","Title: It Was Awful While It Lasted","(A photograph of old men chatting and laughing heartily)","Let’s never meet again, you fucking fossils.","└ Who are they? Your bosses?","└ Yeah, technically, but every last one of them was an unbearable old fart. I quit.","└ Sounds like you had it rough. People from the Central Plains are especially full of old-fashioned geezers.","└ So what are you going to do now?","└ I’m heading back to my hometown to farm. I used to be pretty strong, so it shouldn’t be difficult.","Apparently, someone had quit their job today. That was what I discovered while browsing the Gallery.","There were occasional comments about the Blood Cult entering the Forest of Four Seasons, but I ignored those.","\"All right. Repeat after me. Park.\"","\"Park.\"","\"Jong.\"","\"Jong.\"","\"Hyuk.\"","\"Hyuk.\"","\"And when you put them together?\"","\"Moron.\"","\"You little shit! Where the hell did you learn that word?\"","\"Park Jonghyuk.\"","\"You damn....\"","What would it take to make this bastard gorilla listen to me?","They said the world was wide and full of lunatics, but I never imagined I would end up being verbally toyed with by a gorilla.","This bastard must be smart if he knows how to mess with me like this, right?","If the Blood Cult saw this, wouldn’t they cause an uproar and insist on honoring him as their successor?","Nah. That’s impossible.","Anyone who did that would be beyond insane.","They would be dumber than the gorilla."]},{"title":"Chapter 164","paragraphs":["Wild Horse (1)","I had even reinforced the bridge supports with concrete.","Now that its sturdiness had been improved, it was safe enough to crawl across.","The Gallery showdown was over as well, so there was nothing else I needed to keep an eye on.","Aside from teaching Kkobong Korean and training, everything I could and needed to do had been completed at once.","I’m gradually getting the hang of controlling the cold.","This was how I had learned to use it:","Normally, I kept the cold separated and used it only when necessary.","It took time to gather it back together, but once I became accustomed to it, that process would probably grow faster too.","What should I do now?","Simply waiting for the environment across the river to change and for people to arrive was not necessarily a bad idea, but it would waste far too much time.","The Forest of Four Seasons—the wilderness—changed from one moment to the next. Doing nothing here and merely waiting for something to happen was practically the same as saying I wanted to die.","Should I ask Kkobong to train me?","One might wonder what kind of training I could possibly receive from a gorilla, but what I wanted to learn was martial arts.","Kkobong’s martial arts were exceptionally advanced.","Although his cultivation was lower than the leader gorilla’s, he possessed a solid foundation.","And me?","Forget knowing how to throw a proper punch—I did not even have the foundations.","As someone had put it, I was growing stronger like a complete idiot, so I had managed so far, but I was empty inside.","I had only been able to defeat Kkobong because he had not known about my ability to use cold.","Didn’t they say that, of mind, energy, and body, I overwhelmingly lacked energy?","Even the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster had been unable to teach me about \"energy.\"","To emphasize it again, it was not that they had refused to teach me. They simply couldn’t.","SwordMaster’s post had also meant that its effects could only be maximized if one already possessed the proper foundation.","That was why I asked Kkobong if he could teach me something simple, but—","\"No.\"","\"Why?\"","\"You. Don’t like.\"","\"....\"","I gave up immediately after hearing Kkobong’s sulky answer.","There was no point threatening him. If he deliberately taught me something wrong, the consequences might be irreversible.","In conclusion, now that I had finished the bridge, I suddenly had plenty of free time.","Maybe I should go exploring.","That thought crossed my mind.","If I’m going to do that, it would be better to remove Kkobong’s restraint....","But then he would immediately run away. I did not even need to see it happen to know that.","At the very least, I had no intention of removing the restraint until we could completely trust each other.","Or should I just use him as a porter?","That seemed like the best option.","The spatial backpack could not reduce mass, so its contents still weighed the same.","If I made Kkobong carry all of it, exploring would become much easier.","Since he was a gorilla, he should be able to carry heavy loads too.","The more I think about it, the better it sounds.","I had never realized how valuable gaining a single worker could be.","Excellent.","After slowly formulating a plan in my head, I examined the map.","If I brought Kkobong with me, the one place we obviously needed to avoid as much as possible was the gorillas’ territory.","No one knew what sort of conflict might arise if we entered it.","In particular, if we encountered the leader gorilla, Kkobong might have another fit.","Come to think of it, there was not much time left until evening.","We could explore for an hour or two and then return.","It did not matter if we revisited somewhere I had already been, since the season had changed.","I needed to determine how the terrain changed with each season.","I should also check the place with that enormous tree.","The gigantic tree that had stood alone.","Would Kkobong know about it?","It might be worth asking Father Raccoon as well.","\"Kkobong, do you know a place where there’s a tree much bigger than all the others?\"","\"Don’t know.\"","\"Really?\"","\"Yes.\"","Kkobong answered fluently, even though it had not been long since I started teaching him Korean.","If even Kkobong, who had probably lived as a wanderer, did not know, I would ask Father Raccoon.","\"Kyeng?\"","\"You don’t seem to know either. Thanks for the medicinal herbs.\"","Since neither of them knew, I had no choice but to find it myself.","However, reaching that place would take at least a day, perhaps even longer.","Compasses did not work in that region, so one mistake could leave me lost forever.","Carving marks into trees probably wouldn’t be enough to serve as reliable signposts.","It would be better to keep making signposts and install one whenever I entered a new area.","Without a compass, that was my best option. I had a worker now anyway, so transporting them would not be a problem.","\"Kkyuu?\"","I was still considering where to explore when Wonmo cautiously approached me.","Apparently, he had seen my expression and come over because he thought something bad had happened.","I stared at Wonmo’s adorable face for a moment before suddenly lifting him into the air.","He had lost some weight over the winter, so his formerly chubby build had become pleasantly plump instead.","His fur fell out in no time too.","It was not just his weight. He had also shed a tremendous amount of fur. Cleaning it all up had been quite a chore.","Still, his overall body continued to grow steadily.","\"All right, Wonmo. Pick somewhere you want to go.\"","\"Kkyuu?\"","\"You can choose anywhere.\"","Since I could not decide, I would leave it to Wonmo’s luck.","Rather than thinking of it as exploration, I could consider it a walk that would let Wonmo get some fresh air.","Wonmo was clever enough to understand me and stared intently at the map.","Then he flailed his adorably short forelegs before finally pointing at a particular spot.","\"Kku!\"","\"Here? This place is....\"","It was completely blank.","I had never explored it before.","It lay near the path the leader gorilla had personally made for me.","I had always intended to visit it someday, but one thing after another had come up, preventing me from going.","After thinking about it, I nodded.","It should be fine as long as we returned quickly.","\"All right. Let’s go. But we’re coming back soon, okay?\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","Wonmo smiled brightly when I gave him permission to go outside.","How could he possibly be this cute?","I rubbed my cheek against Wonmo’s adorable face before gently setting him down.","The moment his feet touched the ground, he began running around and bouncing excitedly.","He must have really liked going outside.","\"All right, Kkobong. You carry this.\"","\"Ook.\"","I entrusted Kkobong with the tools and miscellaneous supplies. I carried important items such as the elixir myself.","Once I placed the fast sloth on my back, we were ready to leave.","Since someone might break into our home while we were away, I did not forget to set up the CCTV cameras.","Title: Exploring Again After So Long","Wild Grylls","(A photograph of Kkobong transformed into a porter)","I’m going exploring for the first time in ages. We’re only checking out the area right in front of us, so we should be back soon.","The photo is Kkobong after being turned into a porter. Having an extra pair of hands makes things unbelievably convenient.","└ Heavenly Demon) He certainly looks gentler with glasses on.","└ SwordMaster) He looks absolutely full of complaints, though. Lol.","└ What’s he going to do about it if he’s unhappy? Lol.","└ Seriously, what can he do besides grumble? Lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) Kkobong curses in Korean now. Says he learned it from me.","└ Look at that learning ability. Isn’t he smarter than most people?","└ The more I see him, the more I think so. Lol.","└ All-Father) You are venturing outside, I see. What do you think you will discover this time?","└ Wild Grylls) If I find a unicorn or something, I’ll upload a photo immediately.","└ All-Father) If possible, I would appreciate its horn. Hoho.","└ Wild Grylls) Is it valuable?","└ You won’t come to your senses until a unicorn runs you through with its horn.","└ Countless hunters have been gored to death trying to catch unicorns. Just leave them alone.","└ They have vicious tempers too. Avoiding them entirely is your best option.","I had only been joking, yet a flood of comments appeared trying to dissuade me.","Judging by their reactions, unicorns must have even fouler tempers than I had imagined.","I should have known from the moment I heard all that nonsense about how only pure maidens could ride them.","Unless they had utterly fucked-up personalities, they would not behave like that.","Well, that only matters if I actually encounter a unicorn.","I headed toward the path the leader gorilla had personally made for me.","Wonmo took the lead, while Kkobong followed at the very rear.","We would probably maintain this formation for the foreseeable future.","Nothing should be particularly different—","I had assumed that beyond the path cleared by the leader gorilla lay an utterly ordinary forest.","But I was wrong.","The area felt far more desolate than overgrown.","It was almost as though the entire region had been painted gray. The fallen leaves were gray, and so were the trees.","Scorched marks remained here and there.","Had there been a forest fire recently?","No. If there had been a forest fire, everything would have burned away completely.","Instead, it looked as though all the moisture had simply been drained out, turning everything gray.","Something about this place was ominous.","I continued forward cautiously.","\"Hey, Kkobong. Do you know why this place is like this?\"","\"Fire.\"","\"Fire?\"","\"Fire.\"","When I asked Kkobong, all he would say was \"fire.\"","Apparently, fire was responsible for turning this forest gray, but I did not know the specifics.","Fortunately, it was far from our shelter. Otherwise, I might have suffered considerable damage too.","What in the world could be related to fire strongly enough to transform the entire area like this?","It was not as though the space itself had changed, like the land across the river.","It simply felt as though \"fire\" had claimed this entire region as its \"territory.\"","I carefully checked between the fallen leaves for venomous insects as I continued forward.","Whoooooosh—","\"....\"","Then we encountered a cave that filled me with foreboding the moment I saw it.","My instincts told me that something was inside.","I had a feeling we should not disturb the cave’s owner.","I was just about to turn around quietly when—","\"Kkyuu!\"","Wonmo charged ahead, excited to discover a new animal.","In an instant, he vanished into the cave’s darkness.","The moment I saw that, I jumped in alarm and prepared to rush after him.","Fwoooosh!","\"Kkyaaaaah!\"","A massive blaze illuminated the entire dark cave.","The instant Wonmo realized how ominous those flames were, he turned tail and bolted.","He hid behind my legs and trembled.","Wonmo was normally fearless, so if even he was this frightened, whatever lived inside must be extraordinary.","Clop—clop. Clop—clop.","Before long, the flames burning inside the cave began slowly drawing closer.","The tremendous heat forced me to stumble backward.","At last, I understood why the entire forest had turned gray and why no moisture remained anywhere.","Shhhhh!","I stirred the energy within my body, preparing to unleash my cold at any moment.","Tap!","\"....\"","Finally, the owner of this territory emerged from the cave and revealed itself.","A... horse?","The animal wreathed in flames was a horse—and a remarkably large one at that.","It stood tall enough that I had to tilt my head back slightly to look at it.","Flames flickered where its mane should have been.","Its eyes also blazed as though engulfed in fire.","Its entire body was pitch-black, giving it an overwhelming presence.","\"Prrrrr.\"","The flame horse snorted as though demanding to know why we had disturbed its nap.","I slowly edged backward, trying to show that I had no intention of fighting.","Wild horses generally had nasty tempers, so provoking it further would accomplish nothing.","Slowly. Just keep backing away....","As I retreated, a stone suddenly flew over the flame horse’s head.","A moment later, it landed directly on the horse’s head with a sharp tap.","Fwoooooosh!","At that exact moment, the flame horse’s fire blazed far more fiercely than before.","As if to prove how furious it was, the flames gradually changed from red to blue.","\"Fucking great, isn’t it?\"","\"....\"","The culprit who had thrown the stone was grinning broadly.","Apparently, Kkobong had done it deliberately to screw me over.","He seemed to have decided that it would be great if I died, and that he could simply run away if things became dangerous.","\"You fucking bastard!\"","Just wait.","I’m putting a lock on those glasses later.","***","Shortly before Grylls’s battle with the flame horse began, on the grasslands—","Ludwig was still riding atop the giraffe.","His foot was currently so badly injured that even walking was difficult.","He had searched for the most useful medicinal herbs he could find and administered emergency treatment, but even that had not been enough.","Will I have no choice but to amputate it?","He could clearly feel the injured area undergoing necrosis.","Whenever he circulated his mana, it felt as though that particular part of his body had vanished entirely.","Keeping the worst-case scenario in mind, Ludwig stared across the river.","At present, the opposite bank was a barren rocky region devoid of anything else.","—Kkuooooooo!","—Uooooooo!","And there, two enormous creatures were fighting each other.","They possessed tough outer shells that made them look like armored elephants.","Their legs were much thicker than an elephant’s, giving them remarkably stable balance.","Finally, their tusks had transformed into blades.","They were terrifying creatures even at a glance.","Is this what they mean by watching a fire from across the river?","Ludwig quietly watched the two creatures fight.","\"Hot! Hot, hot, hot, hot!\"","Meanwhile, someone else had fallen straight into the fire."]},{"title":"Chapter 165","paragraphs":["Wild Horse (2)","Thanks to Kkobong, the troll of the century, things went wrong from the very beginning.","He had provoked the flame horse, which looked extraordinary at a glance.","I had assumed he had done it to make trouble for me, but—","\"Oookyaaaaagh!\"","\"Neighhhhh!\"","What kind of place was the Forest of Four Seasons?","Even the raccoons were remarkably intelligent, while the gorillas displayed intelligence comparable to that of humans.","And even where I had come from, horses were already considered exceptionally intelligent animals.","Contrary to their image, wild horses also lived in herds. Naturally, they had rules to follow and possessed strong social instincts.","We already knew perfectly well what happened when an animal that was naturally intelligent lived in the Forest of Four Seasons, didn’t we?","That’s right.","This horse was far more perceptive than I had imagined, and it grasped the situation remarkably quickly.","Fwoooosh!","The flames erupting from the horse’s mouth were directed not at me, but at Kkobong.","Unable to use mana, Kkobong could not even think about fighting back. He was too busy trying to dodge.","The flame horse focused exclusively on him.","Perhaps it knew that I was innocent(?), or perhaps it had simply caught the culprit red-handed.","Either way, I was able to watch leisurely from a short distance away. The heat was intense, but not unbearable.","\"Kyihihing.\"","\"This is delicious. Eat up.\"","While I was at it, I fed the flame horse’s foals.","I had wondered why it had threatened us the instant it saw Wonmo, but apparently, it had foals inside the cave.","As expected of young foals, their flames were not as large as their mother’s.","The fire in their eyes and manes merely flickered like tiny embers.","\"Uagh! Kuagh! Kkueeeek!\"","\"Wow. Look at him spin.\"","At the end of the chase, the flame horse bit Kkobong and began swinging him around in circles.","Kkobong was quite large himself, but the horse apparently possessed tremendous jaw strength.","After playing with him for a while, the flame horse flung him far into the distance.","He had been battered so badly that his white fur was scorched black.","Judging by the occasional twitch, he was still alive.","That’s why you shouldn’t get too clever for your own good.","Kkobong had probably planned to ask me to remove his restraint once I was in danger.","Considering the flame horse’s strength, it certainly could have put me in such a situation.","I could tell that he had taken the fast sloth into account as well.","Kkobong knew it too.","The fast sloth was our party’s ultimate weapon, deployed only as an absolute last resort.","Did he figure it out when I asked the fast sloth to teach me before?","He had also watched me train, so he had probably begun plotting from that point onward.","I had no idea what chain of reasoning had led him to provoke another creature, but one thing was certain.","He had dug his own grave.","Idiot.","I mocked Kkobong inwardly while cautiously watching the flame horse’s reaction.","Apparently having vented all its anger, the flame horse approached its foals.","Then it glanced at me and jerked its head as though ordering me to get the hell out of its territory.","Since I had no intention of fighting, I obediently withdrew.","We were the ones who had wronged it first, after all.","\"Kkyueeeeng! Kkyueng!\"","\"Kkuiiiing!\"","The flame horse’s foals began crying when I moved away.","All I had done was feed them a few fasting pills I had brought as emergency rations and pet them several times,, yet they already seemed to have grown attached to me.","While their mother calmed them down, I headed toward Kkobong.","His mouth hung slightly open, and he looked only half-conscious.","Smoke even rose faintly from his mouth.","He actually managed to protect his glasses.","The funny part was that he had guarded the glasses until the very end.","Apparently, he was so determined not to lose his newfound sight that he had protected them with everything he had.","Using the elixir on him feels like a waste... but I have no choice.","I administered some elixir to Kkobong.","Using the whole bottle would have been wasteful, so I gave him only half.","I did not care about his fur. Healing the seriously injured areas would be enough.","Crackle!","\"Uoooooogh!\"","Healing him was one thing, but he still needed to be punished.","When I struck his forearm hard with my palm, the restraint activated.","Kkobong flailed as the electricity tore through him, causing pain even sharper than the flames.","Given the situation, I did not curse at him. I merely spoke a few short words.","\"Just wait until we get home.\"","\"....\"","Kkobong said nothing.","More likely, he was incapable of speaking.","He might curse at me whenever he pleased, but Kkobong was still technically my \"slave.\"","What he had done today could have endangered me, so I felt the need to approach the matter more seriously.","In other words, I had changed my mind.","I needed to think more carefully about what to do with Kkobong.","Even if it was somewhat harsh, I would have to devise an efficient and effective way to deal with him.","A carrot was important, but it seemed I would need a stick as well.","Tap, tap—","I had just finished dealing with the situation and was preparing to leave when the fast sloth, riding on my back, poked the nape of my neck with its claw.","Wondering what it wanted, I turned my head and looked at it.","Swoop.","The fast sloth pointed at itself with one claw.","It seemed to be telling me to leave Kkobong to it.","As I had mentioned earlier, Kkobong was ultimately still a beast.","Even if he could speak human language fluently, animals probably had ways of communicating among themselves.","Since the fast sloth had volunteered, leaving Kkobong to it might be a good idea.","Besides, the fast sloth has the highest rank here anyway, doesn’t it?","Even I had to watch my behavior around it whenever I ran out of fasting pills.","Moreover, I owed the fast sloth my life several times over.","It might spend every day lazing around, but it had always done what needed to be done.","I could trust it with this.","\"Kkuiiiiiik!\"","\"Wow. Does this place have nothing but fire-element beasts?\"","Before that, however, I needed to finish exploring.","I marveled at the wild boar whose mane blazed with fire.","Since it was a combination of a boar and flames, perhaps I should call it a fire boar.","I immediately understood why this entire region had turned ashen gray.","\"Kkuiiiiiiiik!\"","\"Hot! Hot, hot, hot, hot!\"","Unfortunately, it had a filthy temper too.","I barely dodged the attack of the boar as it spewed fire from its mouth.","Even if I blocked something like that with my shield, the flames would inevitably burn me.","Instead, I responded by wrapping my entire body in aura.","Even if it could not absorb all the damage, reducing it by even a little would be enough.","\"Kkuiiiiiik!\"","The boar snorted flames through its nostrils and scraped the ground with its forelegs.","It was an unmistakable warning that said, \"I’m about to ram you.\"","A moment later, true to its warning, the boar charged at me.","The sight of it rushing forward with its entire body wreathed in flames was incredibly intimidating.","Swoosh—","But that was its fatal mistake.","What kind of sword was I holding?","All I did was place the blade in the boar’s path.","The charging boar passed cleanly across the Heavenly Demon’s sword before collapsing to the ground.","Ordinarily, it should have been sliced neatly in half.","Instead, because of the cold, it merely froze solid.","The ice held the severed surfaces together as though it were glue.","I won’t have to worry about it rotting, either.","Tonight’s dinner would be wild boar.","I put the boar inside the spatial backpack and headed back.","We did not encounter any other beasts on the return journey.","\"Kkyuiiiiing!\"","\"Kkyuhiiing! Kkyuhiiing!\"","The flame horse’s foals clinging to me were the only problem.","I could not tell whether they wanted more fasting pills or simply wanted me to pet them.","After considerable effort, I managed to return them to their mother and headed back to the shelter.","Come to think of it, wasn’t the reason animals enjoy being touched by humans because we can scratch places they can’t reach themselves?","If so, their reaction made sense. Since I had given them fasting pills as well, they probably regarded me as a kindly uncle.","I would have loved to tame them, but unfortunately, their manes were made of fire.","If I tried riding one, my entire body might burn to a crisp, so it was better to give up on that idea.","Absorbing some kind of fire-related essence probably wouldn’t help, either.","I had only just gained the ability to control cold, yet I possessed no resistance to low temperatures.","After returning to the shelter, I began preparing dinner.","First, I planned to butcher the boar that had been split in half and then frozen back together.","...How am I supposed to butcher this?","The tiger had not been cut in two.","This creature, however, had already been severed. Its frozen surfaces were the only thing holding the two halves together.","In other words, the moment it thawed, the membranes surrounding its organs would be gone and everything inside would spill out.","Draining the blood will be difficult too. I should just salvage the edible parts.","It was a shame. I had wanted pork belly for the first time in ages, though I did not know whether this creature even had what could be considered pork belly.","After agonizing over how to butcher it, I eventually made a post on the Gallery.","Title: I Caught a Wild Boar","Wild Grylls","(A photograph of a boar that had been split in half and frozen back together)","How do I butcher this?","It was split in half and then frozen back together, so I could use some advice.","└ Heavenly Demon) It looks like a sturdy boar. You will be eating meat for the first time in quite a while.","└ Wild Grylls) I’m looking forward to it.","└ SwordMaster) I often hunted and ate wild boars during my days as a knight. This brings back memories.","└ Wild Grylls) Did you eat snakes too, by any chance?","└ SwordMaster) Of course. Back then, no matter how much I ate, I was always hungry.","└ Damn. That’ll be a pain in the ass to butcher if it splits apart.","└ Remove the organs and drain the blood first. Cut the head off immediately too.","└ You might only be able to eat the ribs.","└ Wild boar is tough, so eat only the tender parts if possible.","└ Starlight Princess) That wild boar looks rather unusual. Were you in any danger?","└ Wild Grylls) Its mane billowed like fire, and it breathed flames from its nostrils.","└ Starlight Princess) From that description, it sounds like a fire boar.","└ Wild Grylls) Is it a rare animal?","└ Starlight Princess) Naturally. It is a beast fused with an element. However, despite its rarity, its overall anatomy is no different from an ordinary wild boar’s.","She went on to explain that fire energy permeated its hide, so clothing made from it was exceptionally warm.","Consequently, its hide was highly valued by people living in cold regions.","It has already been cut in half, so the hide isn’t intact. Harvesting it will be difficult too.","Still, I should salvage as much as possible.","Even if I did not sell it, I could use it to prepare for winter.","I carefully butchered the boar and placed its organs in a container.","Then I ordered Kkobong to take the container and dump the organs into the river.","Unlike before, he followed my instructions without complaint.","I wondered whether he had learned something from the incident with the flame horse, but—","No. He’s cunning. He might only be pretending to have changed.","I could not lower my guard until the very end.","I would not grow attached to him until I had truly made him submit.","Once I finished butchering the boar, I found that I had obtained a fairly plentiful amount of meat.","Sizzle—","\"Damn.\"","As I always thought, meat could do no wrong.","Fish was delicious too, but meat looked and smelled different from the outset.","There was plenty of flesh as well, so we could feast to our hearts’ content today.","Besides, I can store meat frozen now. This is fucking awesome.","We would be having a meat feast for the foreseeable future.","Of course, we should still eat fish occasionally.","I handed Wonmo a huge chunk of meat.","His eyes sparkled with anticipation.","\"Chomp! Chomp! Chomp!\"","\"Is it good?\"","\"Kkyuu! Yum, yum, yum!\"","Wonmo buried his entire face in the meat as he ate.","I stroked his head and told him to eat more slowly.","\"Do you want some too?\"","\"....\"","Even the fast sloth, who was normally satisfied with fasting pills, was tempted by the ribs and took a bite.","Apparently liking the taste, it chewed slowly and thoroughly.","That left only Kkobong....","\"Ook! Ook!\"","I could not tell whether he was demanding his share because he thought he had done such a wonderful job.","I was staring at him pathetically when—","Smack!","The fast sloth shot forward like an arrow and slapped Kkobong across the face.","Since it normally moved so sluggishly, I could not help but be startled.","Even I was shocked, so imagine how Kkobong must have felt after being slapped.","His eyes went wide, and he stared blankly in utter bewilderment.","He could not simply run away because of the restraint.","More importantly, his food was at stake.","In the wilderness, food was synonymous with life itself.","He would not actually die, but this was still a terrifying punishment.","After slapping Kkobong, the fast sloth alternately pointed at the ribs and me.","It seemed to be telling him that if he wanted to eat, he first needed to show me respect.","Apparently, the fast sloth had also taken a dim view of what Kkobong had done with the flame horse.","Shoo, shoo—","It even waved its hand at Kkobong, telling him to get lost.","What could Kkobong possibly do about it?","In the end, a dejected Kkobong slowly backed away.","He occasionally glanced in our direction, but what could I do?","He had brought this upon himself.","I did not particularly pity him, either.","I could only hope this would break his rebellious spirit without driving him to cause another incident.","Anyway, let’s ignore Kkobong and enjoy these delicious ribs.","Why does this taste flame-grilled? It’s incredible.","Perhaps because it was a boar infused with fire energy, the meat naturally had a smoky, flame-grilled taste.","I was truly fortunate to have enough of it to eat for a while.","Bzzzz—","After we finished eating, a bug flew over while I was cleaning up.","A moment later, it landed on the back of my hand.","Fortunately, I quickly caught it before it could bite me. Otherwise, it might have infected me with some disease.","Come to think of it, I should get some insect repellent too.","Summer was approaching, so insects would soon become rampant.","After purchasing insect repellent, I applied it throughout the cave and shelter.","While I was at it, I also took precautions against snakes.","Bugs and snakes were creatures that absolutely had to be repelled.","I wonder what summer will bring. I just hope there won’t be swarms of mosquitoes.","And sure enough—","BZZZZZZZZZZZ!","The next morning, I was rendered speechless by the terrifying swarm visible outside the cave.","The insects formed a pitch-black mass so dense that I could not see even an inch ahead.","What would have happened if I had not applied the insect repellent?","They would have invaded the cave and gleefully devoured my flesh.","Fortunately, I had even sealed the entrance with a tarp, so we remained safe.","...Is this what they call a Dark Swarm or something?","At this rate, a Plague will probably appear before long.","\"Oookyaaaaagh! Aaaaagh!\"","\"Oh. Right.\"","He was sleeping outside.","I forgot."]},{"title":"Chapter 166","paragraphs":["Premium (1)","Summer.","The season when sweltering heat arrived and all manner of insects ran rampant.","In South Korea, mosquitoes were the most notorious example.","Even saying they \"ran rampant\" was inadequate. They seemed specifically designed to irritate people.","Their bites were unbearably itchy, they buzzed around your ears while you tried to sleep, and they were a damned nuisance to catch.","People often said that while cockroaches were disgusting, mosquitoes were infuriating.","That irritation had even inspired people to devise \"creative\" ways to kill them.","Granted, summers had recently become so hot because of global warming that mosquitoes were rarely seen.","You might see one or two buzzing around in late summer or early autumn, but that was about it.","The insects of the Forest of Four Seasons, however...","They were beyond words.","Winter brought blizzards, spring brought pollen and yellow dust, and summer brought swarms of insects.","As if announcing the beginning of summer, an enormous swarm had appeared, completely obscuring my vision.","Where the hell did so many insects come from?","I brought Kkobong, whom the insects had bitten, gnawed on, tasted, and thoroughly enjoyed, into the cave.","Once I hurriedly applied insect repellent to him, they stopped approaching him.","The repellent had received good reviews, but it worked even better than I had expected.","BZZZZZZZZZZ!","After rescuing Kkobong, I looked outside the cave.","A terrifying number of insects had multiplied and blanketed the entire Forest of Four Seasons.","Not only did they completely fill my field of view, but their collective buzzing was so loud that it was intensely irritating.","It sounded as though a helicopter were hovering nearby.","When I first started living here, it must have been mid-to-late summer at the latest. There weren’t nearly this many insects back then.","Was it because it was early summer?","Or was this year unusual?","Had Rice Crowne written anything about this in his journal?","Questions continued to surface in my mind.","I wonder if the raccoon family is all right. I’m worried about them.","If this situation was unusual, I was deeply concerned about the raccoon family.","Even Kkobong would still have been covered in insects if I had not applied repellent to him.","The raccoon family would have an even harder time dealing with them.","Fortunately, these were not locusts. If they had been, they might have stripped the flesh from our bones.","...Come to think of it, a locust swarm would be a genuine disaster.","Locust swarms were already infamous.","South Korea had winters, so insects generally did not pose that great a threat. Regions that remained warm throughout the year were a different story.","Whenever a locust swarm arrived, it utterly destroyed all the crops.","In Korea, locusts were merely annoying pests. In a region that remained warm throughout all four seasons, they were a natural disaster.","It’s fortunate that the temperature changes so dramatically here.","If the weather remained warm all year, swarms like this might appear whenever they pleased.","The thought alone was horrifying.","In any case, I could not do anything until the swarm disappeared, so I settled for smoked meat for breakfast.","What about Kkobong’s meal?","I asked the fast sloth directly.","Shake, shake.","It told me not to feed him.","Apparently, it intended to establish discipline properly.","Kkobong was still dazed from being attacked by the swarm anyway.","The fish are outside. Will the insects eat them?","If I had known this would happen, I would at least have covered them.","If I was unlucky, I might have to throw away all the fish I had collected.","Granted, I had plenty of food now thanks to yesterday’s wild boar, but it would still be a terrible waste.","At the very least, I need to protect the cores.","The potential waste was one reason, but I was even more concerned about what might happen.","What if an insect ate one of the cores and grew larger?","That would be truly horrifying.","Since winter existed, there probably would not be any drastic changes, but I could not be certain.","After watching the swarm rage outside while refusing to enter the cave, I opened the Auction House.","I purchased more of the insect repellent with the best reviews among those I had previously bought.","I had applied it throughout the cave just in case, but the fact that a swarm of that size would not even attempt to enter made me wonder if the repellent was truly responsible.","Could it really be because of this?","I decided to test it.","I picked up a suitable stone and coated it with insect repellent.","Just to be safe, I slathered on enough to leave it sticky.","Whoosh!","When I threw the stone in an arc, the insects scattered along its trajectory.","The stone landed, rolled across the ground, and finally came to a stop.","BZZZZZZZZ!","Soon, the insects began avoiding the area around it.","Perhaps they hated the smell, because the empty space around the stone gradually widened.","This stuff is seriously effective.","It had not earned such high ratings for nothing.","An insect repellent that worked even in the Forest of Four Seasons.","For reference, the same registered user also made the snake repellent.","I purchased more repellent from the Auction House and made a post.","I was not trying to advertise it. I merely wanted to show everyone what was currently happening.","Title: What the Hell Is Going On?","Wild Grylls","(A video of an insect swarm completely obscuring the view)","(A photograph of Kkobong after being attacked by the insects)","Everything outside was still pitch-black when I woke up, so I took a look. Turns out it’s all bugs ;;","With this many of them, there’s no way to do anything outside. So I’m just holed up in the cave.","Oh, and does anyone know something good for insect bites? This bastard Kkobong got bitten and won’t stop scratching the hell out of himself.","└ Heavenly Demon) I have seen locust swarms before, but this is the first time I have seen one so dense that it obscures all vision.","└ Wild Grylls) How do you deal with something like that, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady is not particularly fond of insects either. One avoids filth because it is disgusting, not because one fears it.","└ SwordMaster) People who say that are usually the most frightened of them.","└ Heavenly Demon) How absurd. This lady, frightened by mere insects?","└ Someone upload pictures of cockroaches and house centipedes and tell her to comment on them.","└ You’ll probably get banned immediately. Lol.","└ Cockroaches are one thing, but don’t upload house centipedes. I nearly fainted when I saw one.","└ Isn’t a \"money bug\" just a house centipede?","└ Yeah. They call it a money bug in the East and a house centipede in the West.","└ Starlight Princess) I can make some medicine for you. Were you bitten as well, Mr. Grylls?","└ Wild Grylls) No. I applied repellent, so I’m fine. Kkobong only got bitten because he slept outside.","└ Starlight Princess) Understood. I’ll send it to you shortly, so please wait a moment!","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you. Would you like one of the cores in return?","└ Starlight Princess) I’m not making an elixir, so I’ll decline.","└ All-Father) For such an enormous swarm to appear... It is truly a bizarre yet fascinating phenomenon. A similar situation was mentioned in the journal.","└ Wild Grylls) A similar situation?","└ All-Father) Yes. It described a particular region being blanketed by a pitch-black swarm of insects. It appears the area where Rice Crowne lived was outside its range of influence.","└ Wild Grylls) Then this is only happening here?","└ All-Father) Yes. According to the journal, they disappear quickly, so you should not need to worry.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) A little casual advertising is perfectly fine! After all, the seller will receive the proceeds directly!","└ The head moderator is here. What have you been doing lately? Are you still being chased?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) I arrived at a harbor and have been fishing! Things have been quite peaceful lately! Oh, and Mr. Grylls! Has Mr. Ludwig still not arrived?","└ Wild Grylls) I still haven’t heard anything from him.","└ Grylls, show us how well it works. How effective is it?","└ Wild Grylls) (A video of the insect swarm flying around a stone coated in repellent) About this effective. Pretty good, right?","└ That’s fucking amazing! Lmao.","└ I should buy some too. Adventurers and explorers will probably use it often.","That was certainly a relief, but I still had one question.","How exactly did a swarm of that size disappear?","It wasn’t as though someone was sucking them up like a vacuum cleaner, so I found it hard to believe they would disappear so quickly.","└ But they aren’t entering the cave? Even with a tarp covering the entrance, keeping them out should be difficult.","└ Wild Grylls) I applied repellent. The stuff I use is seriously effective.","└ Which one are you using?","└ Wild Grylls) The one with the best reviews. It’s made by the Icon Trading Company. Is it okay for me to mention that here?","Somehow, it had turned into an advertisement despite that not being my intention.","Still, this was a genuine testimonial from an actual user. I decided it probably would not cause any problems and stopped worrying about it.","I killed some time browsing the Gallery, but ultimately concluded that I would simply have to wait until the swarm disappeared.","Or should I apply the repellent to my body and go outside?","That might actually be the better option.","As soon as the thought occurred to me, I applied repellent to my body.","Then, to test it, I cautiously extended one arm outside the cave.","BZZZZZZZZ!","Not a single insect came near my arm.","The same remained true when I stepped outside completely.","Even when I reached out to catch them, they all evaded me as though the entire swarm were a single colony organism.","It was incredibly effective.","I should probably use this repellent exclusively from now on.","Let’s see. The fish...","Flap! Flap!","The moment I looked at the container holding the fish, I realized that my concerns had been unfounded.","Why?","Because the fish were going wild as they feasted on the insects.","It was like watching whales wait with their mouths wide open for food to pour inside.","I could probably leave the fish as they were.","That only left the raccoon family.","Crackle! Pop!","When I reached the tree where the raccoon family lived, I witnessed an unusual sight.","Father Raccoon was diligently tending a campfire beneath the tree.","The insects were avoiding the smoke rising from the flames.","\"Kyeng! Cough! Cough!\"","The problem was that Father Raccoon had to keep the fire—and, more importantly, the smoke—going continuously.","The sight was rather pitiful, so I applied insect repellent to him.","Just in case, I gave the raccoon family an entire container of it to make their lives easier.","Having done everything I needed to do, I returned to the cave.","Even on the way back, the swarm avoided me.","It felt strangely surreal.","I should buy about ten containers.","It seemed likely to prove extremely useful, so I immediately opened the Auction House.","I even considered leaving a review while I was there, but....","[Sold Out]","\"...?\"","I could only blink when I saw the notice.","\"What the hell?\"","Where did all my repellent go?","***","The Gallery Auction House charged murderous fees, but its ability to bypass all conventional distribution more than compensated for them.","However, the money earned through the Gallery could not be withdrawn into the real world.","That was its greatest and most crippling drawback.","Consequently, most products listed in the Auction House were one-off items available in extremely limited quantities.","Moreover, even those listings were usually used as a form of advertising.","From a trading company’s perspective, that was the full extent of its value—nothing more, nothing less.","There was little incentive to use it for actual commerce.","\"Master! We’re being inundated with requests for more insect repellent!\"","\"Uh... What?\"","\"Master! The Adventurers’ Guild has submitted an order for repellent...!\"","\"Uh....\"","Marshall, the master of the Icon Trading Company, could not comprehend the current situation.","He had been working diligently as usual, dreaming of a prosperous future for his company, when suddenly—","Orders for insect repellent began pouring in, and their entire stock was wiped out.","The sheer volume of requests was staggering.","Never in his life had he seen insect repellent attract this much attention.","\"W-Why is it selling? What the hell happened? We only listed it on the Gallery as an advertisement.\"","\"Well... have you visited the Gallery recently?\"","\"Not lately.\"","\"A user who tested it in the Forest of Four Seasons posted a review.\"","\"The Forest of Four Seasons?\"","Marshall tilted his head at his secretary’s words.","He knew about the registered user who was allegedly surviving in the Forest of Four Seasons.","But that was all.","He had been too busy with real life, and since there was no way to obtain merchandise from the Forest of Four Seasons, he had dismissed the matter long ago.","\"Yes, the Forest of Four Seasons—the demonic realm where no one knows what may exist.\"","\"I know someone is desperately clinging to life in there. But you’re saying that person reviewed our product?\"","\"He uploaded a video showing that even the insects of the Forest of Four Seasons avoid it. Do you understand what that means?\"","Of course he did.","The trading company master’s mind began racing.","This was an opportunity.","A golden, once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.","There was one problem, however: the ingredients needed to make the repellent.","...I was selling the batch Father made for me.","The repellent had been produced with his father’s knowledge and assistance.","In other words, he would now have to run himself ragged acquiring its ingredients.","Insect repellent had never been one of the Icon Trading Company’s flagship products in the first place.","Repellents were everywhere, and the market had far too many competitors.","After deliberating for some time, Marshall gave his secretary instructions.","First, they needed to deal with the immediate crisis.","\"Start by organizing the orders in the order they were received and calculate the total amount required. Demand has risen without warning, so I cannot guarantee that we will have enough stock.\"","\"Understood.\"","\"And make certain to reserve a minimum quantity for that survivor and keep supplying it to him. That is the most important thing.\"","Marshall might have been cautious, but he was not the kind of man who would throw away an opportunity.","\"While we are at it, why don’t we sponsor him with some of our company’s products?\"","\"Products... sir?\"","\"Yes. Supplies necessary for survival.\"","While the outside world began moving at a frantic pace—","\"I swear I’m checking the reviews before I buy anything from now on.\"","Grylls ground his teeth as he watched the repellent’s price acquire a premium markup in real time."]},{"title":"Chapter 167","paragraphs":["Premium (2)","For merchants selling goods, promotion wasn’t optional—it was essential.","They needed to let the public know what their products were before they could persuade anyone to buy them.","And in this world, there existed the Gallery, a worldwide community rather than one confined to any single nation.","Although not everyone used it, there was no denying that countless people did.","That was why merchants worked hard to promote their products not only in the real world, but also on the Gallery.","Title: That thing the anon just advertised.","I’ve used it before, and it’s fucking trash, lol. Don’t buy it.","└ What do we call a claim with no proof?","└ I’ve used it too. You’re better off without it, lol.","└ I seriously can’t tell if these bastards are lying or telling the truth, lol.","But what kind of place was the Gallery?","It was somewhere you could encounter every conceivable type of person—and experience humanity’s pure, unadulterated malice.","A poorly handled promotion could become entangled in fabricated rumors and deal the seller a devastating blow.","There were occasionally products whose performance was genuinely exceptional, but most of those had already been selling well to begin with.","Therefore, anyone who wanted to advertise on the Gallery had to prepare thoroughly.","They might ask a famous adventurer for an endorsement, sponsor a sports team, or employ any number of similar methods.","Title: Didn’t the Head Manager personally post ads back in the day?","I’m pretty sure the Head Manager three generations ago did. You don’t see that much these days.","└ It just depends on personal preference. That Head Manager got assassinated after running a scam.","└ What kind of scam did he pull?","└ He said he’d advertise something, but never did. Then he went into hiding and eventually died, lol.","└ So he just took the money and ran, lmaooo.","As such, even the Gallery had its own established framework for official promotions.","One might ask how effective it was, but... honestly, its upper limit wasn’t especially impressive.","Cases where word of a product gradually spread, its performance was eventually proven, and it suddenly exploded in popularity?","Those were practically nonexistent.","As previously mentioned, the Gallery was something anyone could use.","Whenever a product began attracting some attention, people frequently exploited their anonymity to muddy the waters.","Apparently, this product is bad for your health. It’s deadly to certain races. It’s highly addictive.","All sorts of baseless rumors would spread, often rendering the entire advertising campaign meaningless.","Title: So, do you have proof?","Do you have any proof that we did it? Lmaooo.","Enough with your suspicions. Show us some hard evidence, lololol.","└ What if it really does have side effects?","└ Not everyone can react the same way to everything~","Therefore, people had to determine whether something was malicious slander disguised as advertising, genuine advertising, a legitimate complaint, or a retaliatory complaint made to counter another one.","That was why Grylls’s product review caused such a massive stir.","I tried it, and it was good.","From Grylls’s perspective, he had merely stated the truth. But it also served as proof that the product worked even in the Forest of Four Seasons.","It was effectively a seal of approval that no one else could possibly match.","└ You really can’t argue against that, lmaooo.","└ Ah, lololol. If you’re upset about it, go into the Forest of Four Seasons yourself, lol.","└ Has he ever criticized a product before, though?","└ Nope. He praised the insect repellent this time, but he’s hardly ever criticized anything.","└ To begin with, there usually aren’t many defective products among the highly rated ones.","└ Then why don’t they usually sell out?","└ Because they’re fuuucking expensive. And unless you’re an adventurer, you generally don’t use repellent.","Title: Forget everything else.","The fact that it works in the Forest of Four Seasons is just ridiculous, lmaooo.","If you want to survive there, you absolutely have to use good equipment. What if he’d used a defective product?","Knowing Grylls, he would’ve cursed the shit out of it, lololol. He would’ve asked what kind of garbage it was.","Title: I’m not an adventurer. I’m a farmer.","I had an idea after watching the video Grylls uploaded.","Wouldn’t pests avoid it if you applied it to stones? The place I live is warm, so there are a lot of insects.","I placed those stones between my crops, and now no bugs come near them, lol.","After seeing this, I’m convinced it’s essential for farmers. Buy it, no matter what. At the very least, you won’t have to suffer because of pests anymore.","└ Was repellent originally meant to be used like that?","└ As far as I know, it’s mostly used by adventurers.","└ Farmers use it too. Insecticides exist, after all.","└ Aren’t most of those insecticides bad for crops?","└ That’s why this repellent is so fucking overpowered.","└ What the hell did the Icon Merchant Company create...?","For these reasons, the repellent quickly sold out.","The same thing happened in the real world, not merely on the Gallery. The Icon Merchant Company’s warehouses had been completely cleaned out.","In truth, something similar had happened once before—during the saber-toothed tiger attack.","Title: Grylls was wearing a uniform, right?","That uniform survived a tiger’s claws without being damaged. Why wasn’t there any news about it?","└ Because Chae-yu uniforms already sold well to begin with?","└ I think it was because of his level of fame. Back then, people merely thought it was interesting.","└ His fame really exploded after the Immortal King incident, lololol.","└ It’ll probably sell well if people rediscover it later.","└ A uniform capable of withstanding the claws of a tiger from the Forest of Four Seasons!","└ But its teeth pierced through it, right?","└ Fuck, the fact that he survived at all was a miracle, lmaooo.","└ Besides, uniforms are more about their design than their performance, so it doesn’t really matter.","Since uniforms were primarily valued for their design rather than their performance, the incident hadn’t produced much of an effect.","Still, sales had increased, so it couldn’t be said that there had been no effect whatsoever.","More importantly, Grylls’s fame had risen dramatically after he exposed the Immortal King.","Naturally, the impact he could have now was completely different from before.","The mere fact that a simple user review from him could produce such a terrifying promotional effect was enough to make merchants salivate.","Title: Hey, you bastards!","Wild Grylls","Give me back my fucking repellent.","└ Why is it yours, you bastard? Lmaooo.","└ Ah, lololol. We’ll put it to good use, so you can use something else, lol.","└ You’ve enjoyed it long enough by yourself, lol.","└ Buuurp~!","└ Hey, Grylls. Do you need any other products? I can recommend something incredible.","└ Wild Grylls: What is it?","└ There’s something called XXX Repellent in the Auction House. Try it.","└ Wild Grylls: K, wait there.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of insects swarming all over the repellent) Wanna die? You smeared honey on this thing, didn’t you?","└ That reverse effect is insane, lmaooo.","└ So it really was honey instead of repellent, lololol.","└ Isn’t that basically fraud? Lol.","└ Breaking news: The repellent that was just listed in the Auction House has been taken down, lololol.","There were, however, some demanding conditions.","First and foremost was performance. If someone recommended a product and it failed to work, there was a high chance Grylls would curse them out.","└ Do we really have to assume that product is defective? This is the Forest of Four Seasons we’re talking about.","└ Exactly. Honestly, I think the Icon Merchant Company’s repellent is the abnormal one.","└ A product that works even in the Forest of Four Seasons is exceptional by definition...","└ Now that you mention it, you’re right.","But what was the important part?","Even if a product proved completely ineffective, its seller could simply blame it on the Forest of Four Seasons and move on.","Working in the Forest of Four Seasons was extraordinary. Failing to work there wasn’t unusual at all.","From an advertiser’s perspective, it was the very definition of low risk and high reward.","It was an especially valuable opportunity for those who were confident in their products’ performance but had never received the attention they deserved.","Title: Grylls, could you please use this just once?","(A photo of what appears to be an insect screen.)","Our merchant company invented it. I think it could be useful in regions with a lot of insects.","We’ll give it to you for free, so please try it just once. We don’t care if you curse us out—just test it for us.","└ Wild Grylls: K, give me a minute. But are you going to list this in the Auction House?","└ Yep. We’ll be listing it soon.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of an insect screen installed over a container holding fish) This works pretty well. I could use it to make a mosquito net too.","└ Thank you ;.; I’m going to start selling it right away.","└ I’m jealous.","└ Hey, Grylls. Let me ask you for a favor too.","It was mutually beneficial, since Grylls received all sorts of products for free.","Of course, people occasionally sent him strange items, but he simply laughed them off as part of the Gallery’s usual nonsense.","Many people were delighted to send Grylls their sponsored products, but naturally, there were also those who weren’t pleased.","\"We cannot simply stand by and watch! At this rate, the sales of our flagship product will take a hit!\"","\"...\"","The merchant companies competing with the Icon Merchant Company were particularly unhappy.","Commerce was, by its very nature, a game of chicken in which victory could only be secured once one’s competitors had been completely eliminated.","Given the era, the concept of a \"monopoly\" barely existed.","It was a world in which the victor took everything. Therefore, they had no choice but to remain conscious of products sold by highly competitive rival merchant companies.","\"Fortunately, the Icon Merchant Company’s repellent isn’t one of its flagship products. Even now, their inventory has been completely depleted, so they can’t maintain proper sales.\"","\"...\"","\"Therefore, we must use this opportunity to devise a method—\"","\"Let me ask you one thing.\"","The company master quietly interrupted his secretary’s impassioned proposal.","The secretary closed his mouth and waited for him to continue.","A heavy silence lingered for a moment before the company master finally spoke.","\"What can we do?\"","\"...Pardon?\"","\"I asked what we can possibly do.\"","His words expressed resignation rather than offering a solution.","Who was the company master?","He was the owner of the merchant company and the one responsible for determining its direction.","It was hardly something anyone would expect to hear from a man in his position, so the secretary couldn’t help but feel bewildered.","But the company master hadn’t said it because he was a fool. On the contrary, he had grasped the reality of their situation faster than anyone else.","\"Do you intend to forcibly drag that man out of the Forest of Four Seasons? Or will you spread propaganda claiming that the product’s effects are fraudulent?\"","\"Can you guarantee that he has absolutely no connection to the Icon Merchant Company? No, even if he doesn’t, we could still find some way to—\"","\"I’m sure that will work wonderfully against a man capable of harvesting fully grown mandrakes as though they were ears of corn.\"","\"...\"","\"There’s nothing we can do. Go grab some popcorn and enjoy the show.\"","In the end, the secretary couldn’t find anything wrong with his reasoning and had no choice but to withdraw.","That didn’t mean the company master had given up, however. He carefully assessed the current situation.","Would our products work in the Forest of Four Seasons?","That was the crucial point. Did their products possess performance so overwhelmingly superior that they could work even in the Forest of Four Seasons?","He could honestly say with certainty that they did not. If the Icon Merchant Company’s repellent had been that exceptional, they would already have treated it as one of their flagship products.","This entire situation had arisen from one coincidence piling upon another.","Unless the master of the Icon Merchant Company is a complete idiot, he’ll turn the repellent into one of their flagship products. Once that happens, our company’s products will inevitably be regarded as inferior by comparison.","It was already too late to ask Grylls for help.","The perception that the Icon Merchant Company’s repellent was the best had already begun to spread.","This was the moment the Gallery’s maximum potential became unmistakably clear. It wasn’t something a single merchant company could stop.","Ultimately, that meant they had to seek another solution. The company master thought long and hard.","I’ll have to negotiate with the Icon Merchant Company.","The outcome of the battle had effectively already been decided.","The company master sighed. He didn’t like the idea of bowing his head to them, but he still had to make money.","Merchant companies were established to earn profits, not to engage in contests of pride.","While one company master was graciously accepting his defeat...","\"M-Master! The volume of orders is still skyrocketing!\"","\"Damn it! I clearly told them to wait! This product uses crops grown on my father’s land!\"","\"They’re telling us to procure more somehow! There are even rumors that it’s good for the skin...!\"","\"Good for the skin, my ass! How does it make any sense for insect repellent to be good for your skin in the first place?!\"","The Icon Merchant Company was plunged into chaos by the tidal wave of work pouring in.","They had already anticipated that the repellent would sell better in the future.","But wasn’t this far too extreme?","\"Why the hell is it selling this well?!\"","It wasn’t as though all their customers were living in the Forest of Four Seasons like Grylls.","***","Grylls had unintentionally stirred up a tremendous storm throughout the commercial world.","Meanwhile, he was still staying inside his cave because of the swarm of insects running rampant outside.","As an added bonus, he was going through the items he had received for sponsorships and promotional purposes.","\"Why the hell did someone send me women’s panties?\"","Although he occasionally received strange products, plenty of them were useful.","He had decided not to write any more reviews because his praise would cause products to acquire a premium. Still, he couldn’t simply take the goods and run after receiving them for free.","He would test their performance and give his honest opinion. Just as he reached that conclusion...","Bwooooooo.","An unfamiliar sound came from outside the cave.","It easily drowned out the buzzing of the insects, drilling deep into his ears.","Grylls stopped organizing the products and poked his head outside the entrance.","He had already applied insect repellent, so none of the insects approached him.","Bwooooooo.","\"...What in tarnation is that?\"","Grylls could see it clearly.","A \"whale\" swimming freely through the sky despite there being no ocean.","It looked exactly like a blue whale, the mammal known to be the largest creature in the world.","The Forest of Four Seasons had always been a place that casually twisted common sense, but this was simply...","This was so absurd that common sense didn’t even enter the equation.","Bwooooooo—","The whale that had been gliding freely through the sky came to a halt directly above Grylls’s head.","Then it turned toward the buzzing swarm of insects and opened its mouth.","A colossal mouth befitting its enormous body.","Whoooooosh!","Before long, its mouth began sucking in the insects like a vacuum cleaner.","The suction itself wasn’t particularly powerful, but the insects were a different matter.","They were numerous, but also exceedingly weak, and they were pulled straight into the whale’s mouth.","In an instant, the sky whale devoured the entire swarm.","Bwooooooo.","As though satisfied with its meal, the whale leisurely swam away through the sky and disappeared.","Title: Do flying whales exist, by any chance?","Wild Grylls","(Video of a whale flying through the sky.)","That whale is flying through the sky. Whales here normally fly around like that, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: That is a creature one would expect to find only in legends.","└ SwordMaster: No, a sky whale is the sort of creature that should only exist in myths... ;;","└ Heavenly Demon: Myths? Do you mean beings such as the Vermilion Bird or the Azure Dragon?","└ SwordMaster: I’m saying it belongs in a myth, not merely a legend... ;;","└ It’s a legendary creature, and we’re actually seeing one in real life... ;;","└ This is insane. Absolutely insane... ;;","After briefly being rendered speechless, Grylls thought,","Hmm... This is a fantasy world, so I guess flying whales exist too?","If unicorns existed, then there was nothing particularly strange about sky whales existing as well.","Hmm. Or was there?","Apparently, sky whales were regarded here in much the same way unicorns were regarded on Earth."]},{"title":"Chapter 168","paragraphs":["Treasure (1)","└ All-Father: By Aragon! This is enough to get my loins stirring! To think the mythical sky whale truly exists!","└ Wild Grylls: What myth is it from? I don’t know much about mythology.","└ All-Father: When the gods still descended into the mortal realm, it was a creature that purified the energies of heaven and earth. It is said to cleanse tainted mana.","└ Wild Grylls: That whale was sucking up insects. Are insects its main diet?","└ All-Father: Oh! It ate insects, you say? I’ve learned something new. The myths claimed that it consumed mana.","└ What kind of place is the Forest of Four Seasons? At this rate, won’t other mythical creatures appear too?","└ Like what?","└ A girlfriend?","└ That came so far out of nowhere that it’s even funnier, lmaooo.","└ Why is a girlfriend a legendary creature? Lmaooo.","└ So you’re saying you have a girlfriend? Blocked.","└ Look how instantly he reacted, lololol.","\"...\"","The impact of the sky whale video was even greater than I’d expected.","For one thing, All-Father was openly excited, and instead of cracking jokes, people were doubting their own eyes.","From my perspective, it was merely another fascinating animal in a world full of them. But apparently, it wasn’t viewed that way by the people of this world.","Was it similar to discovering a unicorn, a creature of legend, back on Earth?","Bwooooooo.","The sky whale’s cry reverberated throughout the Forest of Four Seasons.","Hearing the call of a whale coming from the sky rather than the ocean was quite a bizarre experience.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m curious about something. Are there mammals here that lay eggs?","└ All-Father: Hoho. What an amusing bit of nonsense. If such an animal existed, it would shake the foundations of academia. Ah, although the existence of the sky whale will already do that.","└ You might as well claim that mammals have beaks, lol.","└ Grylls said there are animals with long necks in his world too, lol.","└ What kind of fantasyland did that guy come from?","Just then, something fell from behind the receding sky whale.","The object had come from around its tail and eventually plummeted to the ground.","Considering the distance and perspective, it had fallen fairly far away, but not so far that I couldn’t reach it.","As I watched the sky whale gradually disappear into the distance, a question suddenly occurred to me, so I asked All-Father.","Even this fantasy world adamantly rejected the existence of the platypus.","Perhaps it simply hadn’t been discovered yet, but it was also possible it didn’t exist here at all.","This was a world without giraffes, so it wouldn’t be strange if some other animals I knew were absent as well.","└ Wild Grylls: But wasn’t there anything about sky whales in the journal?","└ All-Father: No, there wasn’t. It did mention strange sounds occasionally coming from the sky, but apparently the trees obstructed the writer’s view. We might regard those sounds as a sign of their presence.","└ Wild Grylls: Ah, that makes sense. The jungle was right on the doorstep, and the trees there were pretty large. Was there anything else?","└ All-Father: Nothing particularly noteworthy. Strictly speaking, even a talking gorilla could be considered a mythical creature.","└ Wild Grylls: Ah.","└ Now that I think about it, that’s true too.","└ A talking gorilla... Are you talking about the Monkey King from the Central Plains?","└ The Monkey King is a monkey, not an ape. He has a tail.","└ Then is the Blood Demon supposed to be Tang Sanzang? Lol.","└ At this rate, a talking pig-man will show up next, lmaooo.","I ended the discussion about the sky whale there and began planning what to do next.","Thanks to the sky whale sucking up the entire swarm of insects before leaving, my surroundings were clear again.","There was no longer any danger of insects clinging to my body, so I could resume my everyday activities.","I guess swarms of insects appear at regular intervals, and then the sky whale comes to dispose of them?","After experiencing the beginning of each season one by one, I’d realized that it was impossible to do anything during the transitional period.","Winter began with a blizzard, spring brought a yellow dust storm of pollen, and summer unleashed swarms of insects.","I didn’t know what autumn would bring, but perhaps it would be comparatively mild.","Now that I can move around again, I should make good use of the time.","When I raised my head, I saw a sky glowing blue.","But what came to mind when one thought of summer? The unbearably long monsoon season.","I planned to accomplish as much as possible before the monsoon arrived.","First, I should find whatever the sky whale dropped.","I knew the general direction.","The problem was that I didn’t know what had fallen, and the other animals would probably take an interest in it as well.","It would be best to prepare thoroughly. As it happened, Kkobong had fully recovered from the insect bites that had left him in such a miserable state.","The special medicine the Starlight Princess had given me had worked wonders. I had a feeling I would be using it often in the future.","And the Icon Merchant Company agreed to keep supplying me with repellent.","They had promised to continue supplying the repellent that had sold out.","I was somewhat suspicious because they’d announced it in a public post instead of sending me a private message, but they had provided various forms of verification, so I could trust them.","Afterward, all sorts of merchant companies sent me sponsored products, though their performance had yet to be tested.","Well... I’d find some way to put them to good use.","I should test the fishing rod soon.","Of all the items, I was most curious about the fishing rod.","Apparently, one merchant company had seen how much fish I ate and sent me one.","Judging by the product, they seemed to specialize in the fishing industry, and their reputation was quite good.","Just like on Earth, high-end fishing rods in this world commanded astronomical prices, yet they had readily given me one of the finest models.","Even though I knew nothing about fishing, it looked so impressive that I immediately decided I had to try it.","I would’ve preferred a fish trap, but perhaps they’d sent a fishing rod because traps were frequently swept away.","\"Kyueek! Kyueeek!\"","\"There, there. Wonmo, hold still. There may still be insects outside.\"","I carefully applied repellent all over Wonmo.","With his sharp sense of smell, Wonmo struggled against the repellent’s peculiar odor, but he was still only a cub.","After Wonmo, I applied it to the fast sloth and Kkobong, completing our preparations to leave.","It might rain while we’re gone, so I should put everything that needs protection inside.","Since it was summer, there was no telling when the rain might start pouring. It was a hunch born of everything I’d experienced so far.","Once I’d taken every precaution available, I set off in the direction where the sky whale had disappeared.","It wasn’t toward the river, but deeper into the forest—in the direction of the orichalcum cave.","If I searched the surrounding area, perhaps I’d find it. If not, I planned to simply give up.","Rustle, rustle, rustle—","\"Hm?\"","I had been moving along smoothly without encountering any obstacles.","It wasn’t unusual for there to be many insects during summer. And \"insects\" naturally included ants.","In other words, a colony of ants was marching diligently toward somewhere.","It was the sort of sight one would normally see only in a documentary—a single, unbroken line of ants advancing without interruption.","They’re heading in roughly the same direction... Should I follow them?","I didn’t know what the ants had discovered, but following them seemed like a good idea.","They were traveling in approximately the same direction, so they had either found whatever the sky whale had dropped or discovered something else.","Given the staggering number of ants on the move, it had to be something unusual.","So they react to the repellent too?","I cautiously approached them just in case, and the ants quietly moved aside.","The only one disappointed by this was Wonmo, who had wanted to eat them. Those are yucky, Wonmo. Yucky.","After finally calming Wonmo down, I followed the ants.","Eventually, I arrived in an unfamiliar area.","Rustle, rustle, rustle!","I couldn’t help recoiling at the horrifying number of ants.","Without exaggeration, they blanketed the entire area.","If I set foot among them, they wouldn’t merely bite me, tear at me, taste me, and enjoy me—they would gnaw at me until nothing but my skeleton remained.","There was a saying that the true rulers of the forest weren’t tigers or wolves, but ants.","No matter how strong the former two were, they were powerless before overwhelming numbers.","The same applied to me. I couldn’t even consider stepping into that swarm.","What’s that?","At least, not until I saw what the ants were so diligently carrying.","The ants covered the entire area, but there was one exception:","The object they were laboriously transporting.","Thanks to the clear space around it, I could see the object perfectly.","A golden... stone?","It was a stone that glittered gold.","At first glance, it looked even more valuable than actual gold.","I had no idea why the ants were carrying it, but it seemed worth examining.","Trusting the repellent to work its magic once again, I approached.","Rustle, rustle, rustle!","As soon as I drew near, the ants quickly scattered, allowing me to inspect the golden stone up close.","A pleasant fragrance wafted from it the moment I approached.","There was also a sweet note to the scent, enough to make me understand why the ants had swarmed around it.","Did the whale create this stone?","I wasn’t sure about that, but I placed it in my spatial backpack for the time being.","As soon as the golden stone disappeared into the spatial backpack, the ants scattered completely.","Whoosh!","They moved incredibly quickly, like a well-trained army executing a retreat.","If I’d faced summer without applying the repellent... I didn’t even want to imagine it.","This was an area where the seasons changed frequently, yet the ants were still able to maintain such vast numbers. That alone was remarkable.","I had said it as a joke before, but perhaps they truly were the strongest creatures here.","In the wild, it wasn’t the strongest who survived—the ones who survived were the strongest.","\"Sniff, sniff. It’s already rubbed off on me.\"","I had touched the golden stone while placing it inside the spatial backpack, and its scent had already clung to my hands.","To be honest, its texture hadn’t been particularly pleasant.","I had thought it was a stone, but it was as soft as slime and slightly sticky.","That only made me more curious about the true identity of this golden stone(?). I’d have to ask All-Father or the Starlight Princess.","When I finally returned to the shelter, I didn’t take the golden stone back out.","I had no choice but to be careful, since doing so might attract another swarm of ants.","Fortunately, I’d taken a photograph beforehand. I immediately made a post.","Title: I found something interesting","Wild Grylls","(A photo of what appears to be a golden stone being carried by ants.)","Something strange fell from the sky whale, so I went to where it landed. But a swarm of ants was heading there too.","I stole what the ants were carrying and brought it back. Its most distinctive feature is the pleasant fragrance it gives off.","I’m going to ask what it is before deciding what to do with it.","└ Heavenly Demon: It glitters more brilliantly than gold. How beautiful.","└ SwordMaster: You’re saying that came from the sky whale? Just looking at it, you can tell it must be incredibly precious.","└ \"Precious\" doesn’t even begin to describe it. If that thing reaches the outside world, there’ll be an uproar.","└ The sky whale itself is already a mythical creature. If that fell from such a being, then... Lmaooo.","└ What the fuck could it be? Why would something like that come out of a whale?","└ What if it’s actually poop? Lol.","└ That’s fucking disgusting, lmaooo.","└ Praise the Sun: Can you give that to me? If it’s fragrant, I might be able to use it as incense.","└ Wild Grylls: It’ll probably attract a lot of insects. Will you be all right with that?","└ Praise the Sun: What insects would there be in a desert? Lol. At worst, there might be scorpions and spiders.","└ Wild Grylls: Those sound even more dangerous... ;; I’ll think about it after I find out exactly what this is.","└ Praise the Sun: It looks pretty large. If possible, could you give me even a small piece?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll decide after finding out what it is.","└ All-Father: Hoho. Goodness. I’d only just calmed down, and now it seems my loins will begin stirring again.","└ This old man seems to get worked up pretty often these days...","└ Isn’t he going to die of high blood pressure at this rate? Lmaooo.","└ Necromancy Is Love: Given his age, that isn’t impossible.","└ Says the guy who can’t get worked up at all, lol.","└ Necromancy Is Love: Silence, you wretch!!!","└ Lmaoooooo, look at him throwing a fit.","└ Getting worked up is still way better than having no reaction at all, lmaooo.","└ Starlight Princess: I’m outside at the moment, so I don’t think I can examine it.","└ Wild Grylls: Does anything come to mind?","└ Starlight Princess: If it fell from a whale, the only possibility I know of is ambergris. Besides, I know almost nothing about sky whales.","└ Wild Grylls: Understood.","Ultimately, I had no choice but to ask All-Father.","All-Father readily agreed and accepted the golden stone for examination.","We both agreed that I should cut off only a small piece for him. If I sent the entire thing, it might attract hordes of insects to his location.","Not long afterward, All-Father informed me of a shocking fact.","└ All-Father: This is feces.","└ Wild Grylls: ...Pardon?","└ All-Father: It’s feces. Whale feces.","I was briefly dumbfounded by the revelation that it was poop.","└ All-Father: Hohohohoho! This old man is truly happy. Not only have I learned that sky whales exist, but I have even obtained sky-whale feces! Living a long life truly does bring wonders.","All-Father ascended toward paradise."]},{"title":"Chapter 169","paragraphs":["Treasure (2)","Ambergris, the jewel of the sea.","It was a substance formed from the excrement or intestinal stones of sperm whales.","Although it looked like an ordinary rock, it possessed an astronomical value befitting its title as the jewel of the sea.","Apparently, it sold for roughly forty to fifty million won per kilogram, and since most pieces were quite large, they were often worth hundreds of millions.","Even ordinary ambergris from my world was worth that much. So what about ambergris from a mythical creature like a sky whale?","If anything, it was something that couldn’t be sold.","It was a valuable specimen that scholars needed to study, and besides, it was something \"mythical.\"","It was impossible to put a price on it, and there was no telling how severely I would be criticized if I sold it.","└ Wild Grylls: I understand that it’s priceless, but it’s basically just used as a fragrance, right?","└ All-Father: We’ll have to conduct further research to know for certain, but for now, yes. Since it is ambergris from a sky whale, it must contain some sort of special power.","└ Wild Grylls: The power to attract ants?","└ All-Father: Rather than an ability like that, it should possess something befitting a sky whale. Perhaps it has exceptional purification properties.","The possibility that it possessed purification powers gave me pause.","Even if it did, I had no idea what I would use them for.","It might possess other abilities, but discovering them would probably take a long time.","I can’t just leave it sitting around forever, either.","Although I had a spatial backpack, the ambergris still had weight, and the backpack’s capacity wasn’t infinite.","It was undoubtedly valuable and extraordinary, yet it was of no practical use to me.","I let out a hollow laugh at the irony, then decided that I should first determine what to do with it.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll take my time thinking about it. Now that I’m actually trying to dispose of it, I don’t even know where it should go.","└ Praise the Sun: Couldn’t you give me just a little?","└ Wild Grylls: Do you know how to use it?","└ Praise the Sun: I want to use it as incense. I’m genuinely curious about it. Is there anything you want in exchange?","└ Wild Grylls: Not particularly. I’ll just cut off a small piece and give it to you. But be careful not to attract insects.","└ Grylls, couldn’t you break it into pieces and list them in the Auction House?","└ That’s not a bad idea. It’s useless to you anyway.","└ Wild Grylls: Not yet. There’s something I want to test first.","There was still plenty of time, so I didn’t need to rush my decision.","Besides, there was something I wanted to try—an idea inspired by the swarm of ants attracted to the ambergris.","If it attracted a swarm of ants, wouldn’t it similarly attract a school of fish?","The two might seem completely unrelated, but there was always a chance.","All-Father would probably pound the floor in outrage if he saw what I was planning, but I didn’t care.","└ All-Father: You intend to use ambergris as fishing bait? It sounds incredibly idiotic, but I must admit that I’m looking forward to it.","└ Wild Grylls: You’re surprisingly calm. I thought you’d consider it a waste.","└ All-Father: I’ve already received a piece, haven’t I? Besides, I’m curious too. What kind of fish will you catch with it? I suspect everyone else is thinking the same thing.","└ Who the hell goes fishing with whale shit? Lmaooo.","└ It isn’t even ordinary whale shit. It’s the shit of a mythical whale, lmaooo.","└ What kind of life does Grylls even live?","└ The life of a fly?","└ Youuuuu are seriously awful, lmaooo.","└ Why? His life really is as fleeting as a fly’s, lololol.","Surprisingly, everyone seemed curious.","Then again, I was probably the only person capable of doing something like this.","I carefully inspected the sponsored fishing rod.","It appeared to be made of bamboo and didn’t have a reel for adjusting the length of the line.","Considering the era, there seemed to be a limit to their technological capabilities. Still, it looked sturdy, and that was enough for me.","Title: Going fishing","Wild Grylls","(A photograph of the fishing rod and another showing ambergris being used as bait.)","I’m going to try fishing with this as bait. What do you think I’ll catch?","└ Heavenly Demon: This lady predicts that you will catch an enormous fish.","└ SwordMaster: I think you may be the only person in existence who would use whale feces as fishing bait, Mr. Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: That’s a compliment, right?","└ SwordMaster: It is admirable that you always look on the bright side.","└ He wouldn’t survive if he weren’t optimistic.","└ I would’ve gone insane a long time ago.","└ When you put it that way, Grylls really is rather pitiful.","No matter how often I saw it, I couldn’t understand the flow of conversation on the Gallery.","One moment, everyone was busy mocking me, and the next, they were looking at me with pity.","I closed the Gallery and headed toward the river with my animal companions.","First, I removed the fish trap and then checked the river’s condition.","Roooooar!","It was no different from usual. Beyond the river, the vast desert still stretched into the distance.","Nothing in particular stood out, so I immediately began preparing to fish.","I didn’t forget to spray repellent around the area in case the ambergris attracted insects.","Then what should everyone else do?","\"Wonmo, play with this.\"","\"Kyu!\"","I gave Wonmo a stuffed puppy.","One might wonder why I had a stuffed puppy, but that was another sponsored product.","Apparently, it was made from a fabric that animals especially liked.","Wonmo was happily playing with it, so I was very satisfied.","\"Kkobong, if a fish bites, you’re going to help me pull the rod. Understand?\"","\"...\"","\"Answer me.\"","\"Yes.\"","It was decided that Kkobong would help me reel in whatever I caught.","Everything was ready. I attached a piece of ambergris to the hook.","A pleasant fragrance was already wafting from it, making it easy to understand why it was used in perfumes.","It’s rather funny that feces can smell this wonderful.","I chuckled and swung the fishing rod with all my strength.","The hook landed in the river with a splash.","Since the current was so powerful, I worried it might immediately be swept away, but my concern proved unfounded.","Splash-splash-splash-splash!","An enormous school of fish had converged on it.","At the same time, the fishing rod grew incredibly heavy.","Startled, I shouted at Kkobong to pull. Following my command, he tugged on it with all his strength.","It was difficult to pull up, perhaps because several fish had become tangled together, or perhaps because the fish here were naturally powerful.","\"Graaaaaah!\"","\"Uwooooooh!\"","But it was a different story when Kkobong and I combined our strength.","The two of us strained with all our might and hauled the fishing rod upward.","Splaash!","As a result, one enormous fish burst from the water.","I was delighted to have caught such a large fish—until disappointment immediately set in.","\"That’s it?\"","The fish I’d caught was no different from the ones that regularly entered my trap.","It seemed ambergris would work better as a lure for attracting fish than as actual bait.","Still, I’d obtained enough food for the day. That alone was something to be grateful for.","I overcame my disappointment and packed everything away.","It’s not completely useless, since it works as bait, but...","How should I put it?","It felt like an outrageous waste.","I could catch fish merely by setting a trap, even without bait.","There was no reason to go out of my way to use ambergris.","Well, perhaps All-Father would discover some other effect while researching it.","I handed the flopping fish to Kkobong and returned to the shelter.","The days really are longer because it’s summer.","Ordinarily, it should have been growing dark by now, but the sun was still shining brightly.","At least summer gave me more time to remain active.","That would be a different story once the monsoon arrived, though.","When will All-Father finish researching the ambergris?","It was excrement left behind by a mythical creature that even All-Father had never witnessed before.","There had to be something unusual about it.","I had no choice but to wait patiently if I wanted to learn what that was.","But why were the ants trying to carry it away? Was it simply because of the fragrance?","Ants weren’t the only insects that liked sweet things.","Perhaps the ants had claimed it first, preventing other insects and animals from approaching.","While entertaining such idle thoughts, I turned my head.","My gaze fell upon the cave wall—the wall where I had recorded the number of days I had survived.","Does this make today the twenty-sixth day?","In three days, it would be exactly one month.","Time had passed surprisingly quickly.","I could still only check the situation outside through the Gallery, but things were far from peaceful.","El Dorado had descended into a state bordering on civil war, while the Blood Cult was also displaying ominous movements.","Personally, I hoped to encounter Ludwig, who was somewhere in the Forest of Four Seasons, as soon as possible.","Come to think of it, wasn’t the football match today?","Since I had nothing in particular to do, I opened the Gallery.","As it happened, Cheonggu Princess had just posted an announcement that the match was beginning.","I opened the post and left a brief greeting.","└ King Leor: Hey, what do you think the score for our Leor match will be? We’re facing a weak team today.","└ Wild Grylls: You’ll take a 1–0 lead, then concede an equalizer near the end because of poor stamina.","└ King Leor: Come on. That stamina problem again? ;; They’ve had a week off. Shouldn’t they have recovered by now?","└ Wild Grylls: I’ve done exhausting work myself, and once fatigue accumulates, it takes more than a week to recover—sometimes over a month. Besides, football players fill their free time with training too, don’t they?","└ King Leor: When you put it that way, it really does sound likely. We absolutely need to sign someone next time...","└ Does Leor have that much money?","└ It’s less about money and more about the manager changing next season. We’ll have to wait and see.","└ So basically, expect no new signings, lol.","└ What about Chae-U?","└ Chae-U has moved to a different team, so I’m honestly looking forward to it. The manager properly understands tactics.","└ Cheonggu Princess: All we need to do next season is reinforce our defensive tactics! And throw away that useless piece of trash who cost one hundred billion yura!","└ Isn’t that a little harsh? Lol.","└ But judging by how badly he’s playing now... he simply has no talent.","└ Exactly, lol. Even Kone has made a comeback, so what’s that guy’s excuse?","└ You can blame the defense on the line being too high, but that bastard—","└ Wild Grylls: Exactly how strong are today’s opponents?","└ Cheonggu Princess: The Saint has arrived! Today’s opponents are a mid-table team! What do you predict the score will be?","└ Wild Grylls: Your defense is still terrible, so I predict 3–2.","└ Cheonggu Princess: That makes me nervous...! Still, I’m relieved that we’ll win!","After making a rough prediction, I quietly waited.","The match would take a long time to finish, so I decided to practice my cultivation method.","The cold energy has grown to the size of a fist now.","As time passed, my control over the cold energy improved by leaps and bounds.","What had once been the size of a grain of millet was now as large as my fist.","Moreover, its growth rate was gradually slowing, suggesting that I would soon master it completely.","Once I finish mastering the cold energy, I should ask the Heavenly Demon for the next mnemonic verse.","Perhaps I could ask her when exactly thirty days had passed.","Until the football match ended, I practiced the cultivation method and handled my other tasks before opening the Gallery again.","It was almost time for dinner, so I’d taken a short break.","[Chae-U vs. Cadrol: Match over! Just as the Saint prophesied, Chae-U finishes with a 3–2 victory!]","[Leor vs. Hunin: An equalizer in stoppage time brings the match to a draw!]","\"Oh?\"","I had gotten it right again.","This time, I had even predicted both the scores and the course of the matches.","I could dismiss getting it right once or twice as coincidence, but getting it right a third time left me with a strange feeling.","└ Cheonggu Princess: Everyone, say it together! Mr. Grylls is a saint!","└ Please let me marry my girlfriend.","└ Please let me score one hundred points on my academy practicum.","└ Please let the remaining half of the year be amazing.","└ King Leor: Please let Chae-U be relegated.","└ Cheonggu Princess: What the fuck is wrong with you?! Get lost! Your team could only manage a draw, lol.","└ King Leor: So, are you making it into the Champions League? Lol.","└ Cheonggu Princess: We can if we win every remaining match~","People even began making their pilgrimage to the prophetic post as though it were only natural.","I chuckled at the Gallery, which had descended into chaos over the match results, and closed it.","I noticed a post from someone claiming to have made a fortune through gambling, but casually ignored it.","Money or no money, my own survival was what mattered.","Then I stepped outside.","Blub—blub—","It was the fish I had caught earlier with the fishing rod.","And it was swimming through the air.","...What is this? A bug?","The world truly was coming to an end."]},{"title":"Chapter 170","paragraphs":["Treasure (3)","I could only stare dumbfounded at the fish swimming freely through the air like the sky whale.","The sky whale was a mythical creature, so I could simply chalk it up to being mysterious.","I could have even understood it if the fish had flopped and crawled across the ground like a lungfish.","But what unfolded before my eyes defied every expectation I had.","If this world were a game, it would be fair to say that I had encountered a bug.","Blub! Blub!","The fish swam smoothly as though the air itself were water.","If it could do that, why did it even have gills and fins?","The sky whale already denied the very existence of physics, but this thing took it a step further.","Title: What the hell is this thing?","Wild Grylls","(Video of a fish flying through the sky)","Are there any fish that can fly around in the sky?","└ Heavenly Demon: First the gorilla learns martial arts, and now even a fish has learned Void-Stepping.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s Void-Stepping?","└ Heavenly Demon: It is the ability to fly through the air, like the fish you are looking at. One must at least reach the Transformation Realm to barely perform it.","└ SwordMaster: Why don’t we just keep it for display? I’m curious how long it’ll keep flying.","└ Wild Grylls: I need to eat too, you know.","└ Passing Dwarf: Hey, upload more videos. I’m not believing this until you upload a few more.","└ Wild Grylls: You don’t believe in the sky whale either?","└ Passing Dwarf: At least that has appeared in myths before. I’ve never even heard anyone make up a lie about something like this. Kekeke.","└ Wild Grylls: (Video of a fish flying through the sky 1) (Video of a fish flying through the sky 2) Happy now?","└ Passing Dwarf: Oh;; Do you have any idea why it’s doing that? It can’t be happening for no reason.","└ Wild Grylls: It did eat some sky-whale poop I used as bait. I think that changed it somehow.","└ All-Father: Since the opportunity has presented itself, why don’t you try a bite as well, Mr. Grylls? It gives off such a pleasant fragrance that I imagine it would taste rather good too.","└ Wild Grylls: Dude;;","└ If that’s what you think, why don’t you eat it yourself? Why are you telling Grylls to do it? Kekekeke.","└ Isn’t that basically the same as eating curry-flavored poop?","└ It really is curry-flavored poop. Haha.","All-Father briefly spouted some nonsense, but I had roughly identified the cause.","The ambergris I had used as bait.","That was the only thing I could think of.","Otherwise, there was no way this fish would suddenly go insane and start flying through the sky.","And most importantly—","’Is this safe to eat?’","Could I really eat this thing?","What if eating it did more than merely make me sick and caused me to float around too?","But I couldn’t just leave it alone either. It might attract the attention of other animals.","If I couldn’t eat it, the safest course of action would be to release it.","I was about to return it to the river when—","Slap!","\"Ghurk?!\"","The instant I reached toward it, the fish smacked me across the cheek with its tail.","The impact was so powerful that I heard a sharp crack from my neck.","Thankfully, it hadn’t broken my neck. It had merely made a noise.","More importantly, the cheek it had struck was stinging badly. How could its tail be so powerful?","’Did eating whale poop make it stronger too?’","So many absurd things had already happened that it seemed like a plausible hypothesis.","Then how was I supposed to bring this thing down?","After thinking for a moment, I lunged at the fish.","No matter how much it ignored gravity, it ought to fall if I pressed down on it from above.","Flap! Flappity-flap!","\"Uwoooooagh?!\"","Or so I thought, but I was completely wrong. Far from descending, it began swimming vigorously the moment I grabbed it.","It moved so quickly that the scenery flashed past me in real time.","Realizing I might end up falling somewhere strange at this rate, I desperately fought back.","Pow! Thud!","I punched the fish in the head.","No matter what kind of animal it was, a blow to the head should at least make it dizzy.","Hadn’t I always hit fish on the head whenever I needed to knock them unconscious?","Just as I expected, the fish soon passed out and went limp.","Naturally, my body plummeted toward the ground as well.","Crash! Thud!","I rolled several times before finally slamming into a tree and stopping.","My entire body ached. Grimacing, I brushed the dirt from my eyes and opened them.","The unconscious fish was twitching on the ground, while my animal friends stood at the shelter entrance staring at me.","They all wore expressions that seemed to ask, What the heck are you doing?","Kkobong and the fast sloth were one thing, but even Wonmo was looking at me that way. It was embarrassing.","\"This fish is a menace.\"","I had no idea what might happen if I ate it.","Since it was mealtime anyway, I hurriedly butchered it.","I intended to remove only its inner core and throw everything else away.","However—","’Its inner core... is golden?’","There was something strange about it.","No, perhaps extraordinary would be a better description.","It shone with a brilliant golden radiance, as though it had captured the exact color of the ambergris.","Would eating this make me float through the sky as well?","If so, I would rather not eat it.","’Should I give it to Fastsloth?’","Instead, I considered giving it to the fast sloth.","I figured that this creature might be able to control its effects.","\"Want to eat it?\"","\"...\"","Fastsloth accepted the inner core without the slightest hesitation.","It examined the core with its characteristically sluggish movements before putting it into its mouth.","It used to live on inner cores before we obtained fasting pills, so it would probably be fine.","Float—","Or so I thought. Was the core’s energy difficult even for Fastsloth to contain?","When it began gently floating upward, I hurriedly pressed down on its shoulders.","Fastsloth seemed perfectly fine, however, and waved its arms as if telling me to let go.","Float— Float—","Fastsloth levitated around every corner of the shelter for quite some time.","Fortunately, it appeared capable of controlling itself.","In the meantime, I finished eating with my animal friends.","Oh, and for the record, I fed Kkobong as well. Fastsloth had given me permission.","\"Kyu! Kyukyu!\"","Wonmo, who had been completely preoccupied with its food, began bouncing excitedly when it noticed Fastsloth.","It seemed to be asking me to let it fly too.","It was unbelievably adorable when it acted like that.","But if Wonmo climbed onto Fastsloth’s back, Fastsloth would quickly be crushed.","Even though Wonmo was still a cub, it was an owlbear. The fundamental difference in their size was simply too great.","\"Kyii! Kyii!\"","\"Keng!\"","So instead, I placed an equally adorable raccoon kit on its back.","The baby raccoon smiled brightly the instant it climbed atop the floating Fastsloth.","The father raccoon beneath them looked amused, while the mother raccoon looked worried.","\"Kyu! Kyu!\"","Wonmo, on the other hand, apparently became upset that it was the only one that couldn’t ride and sulked in a corner of the cave.","There was hardly anything cuter than a round little animal scrunching itself up in a corner.","I walked over to Wonmo, who was expressing I’m upset with its entire body, and spoke to it.","\"Wonmo, cheer up. If I become able to fly later, I’ll give you a ride. Okay?\"","\"Kyuuu...\"","I somehow managed to coax Wonmo back into a good mood.","Before long, Fastsloth also landed.","\"Can you fly whenever you want?\"","\"...\"","When I asked, Fastsloth shook its head.","Apparently, there was some kind of time limit.","If there weren’t, I might have been able to escape this place quickly.","’It would be... a little much for me to eat one too, wouldn’t it?’","I hadn’t even mastered cold energy yet. Biting off more than I could chew would only cause trouble.","Besides, I wasn’t sure whether I could absorb it properly.","Fastsloth possessed better instincts than I did, so it had eaten the core because it knew it wasn’t dangerous.","But I had no way of knowing whether it was compatible with my body, so I had no choice but to put the matter off until later.","’In any case, I can assume that ambergris grants the ability to fly... right?’","I had no idea what side effects it might carry.","I considered testing it on Kkobong as well, but since Kkobong couldn’t use mana anyway, wouldn’t that be pointless?","For now, I could only trust the instincts that had prompted Fastsloth to swallow it without hesitation.","Title: Discovered one effect of ambergris","Wild Grylls","(Video of Fastsloth floating through the air)","(Video of Fastsloth flying with a raccoon kit on its back)","Fastsloth ate the inner core of the fish that was using Void-Stepping, and now it can fly around like this.","Looks like ambergris gives things the ability to fly.","It can’t do it permanently, though. There’s a time limit. Still, there’s no denying how useful it is.","└ Heavenly Demon: I suddenly feel a peculiar sense of futility. This lady trained for years to attain Void-Stepping.","└ SwordMaster: Years? How many years did you train in total?","└ Heavenly Demon: I began when I was around ten years old, so exactly ten years.","└ SwordMaster: I’m saying this as a Swordmaster: if you don’t want other people to beat the crap out of you, you shouldn’t say things like that.","└ Heavenly Demon: Why not? It was a full ten years.","└ SwordMaster: Other people could devote their entire lives to training, never mind ten years, and still barely have a chance of becoming Swordmasters. Hahahahaha.","└ I seriously want to beat the crap out of her. Kekeke.","└ The Heavenly Demon is deliberately flexing on everyone, right? She has to be.","└ Grandmaster in only ten years? What a load of fucking bullshit. Hahaha.","└ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. How strange. Why are they unable to accomplish something so easy?","└ All-Father: Then, Heavenly Demon, allow me to ask you one thing. Have you reached the end?","└ Heavenly Demon: No. The closer I came, the farther away it seemed.","└ All-Father: It is the same for me. No matter how deeply I delve into this accursed magic, there seems to be no end. Hohoho.","└ Heavenly Demon: Something with an end would be more boring, if anything.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll get upset if you tell me my escape has no end either.","└ Heavenly Demon: Everything is better when it has an end.","└ Look at this punk changing her tune. Kekeke.","└ She really watches what she says around Grylls, doesn’t she? Haha.","└ Every time I see her, it feels like the Heavenly Demon has a soft spot for Grylls.","└ Praise the Sun: Hey, Grylls. Check out the post I uploaded. This shit is seriously amazing. Hahaha.","While the gallery’s reaction was heating up, Praise the Sun’s comment caught my eye.","If Praise the Sun had gone so far as to personally make a post, something quite entertaining must have happened.","Wondering what it was, I immediately searched for the post.","It must have been uploaded only moments ago, as it had barely received any upvotes.","Title: Review of sky-whale ambergris","Praise the Sun","(First-person video of flying through the sky)","(Video of a dark-elf attendant flailing frantically in the air)","(Video of Praise the Sun laughing heartily while shouting something in the Cetan language)","They said ambergris was incense, so I burned some. The smell is one thing, but gravity disappeared from the entire space. Hahaha.","Strictly speaking, it feels like being in an ocean where only air resistance exists. That makes it feel even more fucking amazing. Kekekeke.","He claimed that gravity had vanished from the entire space even though he had merely burned it as incense.","That taught me that it had an effect even when burned.","Not that it was of any immediate use to me.","When the time came, I intended to consume it directly rather than burn it as incense.","└ Wild Grylls: It looks fun just watching it. Did you really only burn it as incense?","└ Praise the Sun: Yeah. I was thinking of going to sleep when my body suddenly floated into the air, so it startled me. Haha.","└ Why is that attendant freaking out so badly? Hahahaha.","└ To be fair, I’d freak out too. Hahahaha.","└ Is it okay to upload this video? If that attendant uses the gallery, won’t they figure out who you are?","└ Praise the Sun: Oh. You’re right. I was having so much fun that I forgot. I’ll go edit it.","└ Too late, dude. I already saved the video. Haha.","└ Praise the Sun: Sigh. Do whatever you want. I don’t care whether it’s real life or the gallery. All that matters is having fun. Haha.","└ That does look pretty fun.","I thought this might be the first time I had ever seen Praise the Sun leave so many comments.","That showed just how excited he was.","For some reason, it made me feel proud.","└ Praise the Sun: I should invite my wives over so we can have fun together soon.","└ What are you going to do after inviting your wives?","└ Praise the Sun: What else? We’ll get nice and filthy...","Hmm.","Let’s move on.","One ought to respect people’s personal preferences, shouldn’t one?","Although this was less a personal preference and more the behavior of a complete lunatic... I could honestly understand the appeal.","Doing that while floating through the sky?","He would be accomplishing a feat(?) that no one had ever achieved before.","Even Earth had only managed it after constructing space stations, so imagine how impossible it would be here.","’Wait. You can fly just by burning it as incense?’","That thought made me look around.","Apart from the fireplace and the entrance, there were almost no openings through which anything could escape.","If I sealed those as well and burned the incense, couldn’t I enjoy the same experience as Praise the Sun?","’...I have to do this right now.’","I could never resist doing something idiotic.","Afterward, I received instructions on using the incense and the necessary equipment from Praise the Sun.","\"How is it, Wonmo? Isn’t this great?\"","\"Kyuuuuu! Kyuu!\"","Thanks to that, we were able to enjoy an exhilarating zero-gravity experience.","\"Uwooooooo! Woooooooah!\"","Kkobong, however, didn’t seem to enjoy it very much.","READ MORE ChapterS HERE : https://beastnovels.com/"]}]);
